hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla al-Ansari Abu Isa, from Ali, peace be upon him. 637 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: Abu Musa came to al-Husayn visiting him. Ali said to him: Have you come visiting the sick or gloating? He said: No, rather visiting. He said: If you have come visiting, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a man visits his Muslim brother, he walks in the harvest of Paradise until he sits, and when he sits mercy covers him; if it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray upon him until evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray upon him until morning."
"602","638 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, that Hibatullah ibn al-Husayn informed them, reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman with its meaning, and in it: For I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abu Mu'awiyah. Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu Mu'awiyah."
"603","Another. 639 - Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to me, from Husayn ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah - judge of Rayy - from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: I heard Commander of the Believers Ali say: I gathered, I and Fatimah, and al-Abbas and Zayd ibn Harithah. al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, my age is great, my bones thin, my burden many; if you see fit, O Messenger of Allah, to order for me such-and-such wasqs of food, do so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall do. Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to order for me as you ordered, do so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall do that. Zayd ibn Harithah said: O Messenger of Allah, you had given me land from which was my livelihood, then you took it back; if you see fit to return it to me, do so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall do that. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to entrust me this right which Allah has made for us in His Book in this fifth, so I distribute it in your lifetime, lest anyone dispute me over it after you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall do that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted it to me, and I distributed it in his lifetime. Then Abu Bakr entrusted it to me and I distributed it in his lifetime. Then Umar entrusted it to me and I distributed it in his lifetime, until the last year of the years of Umar, when much wealth came to him and he set aside our right, then sent to me and said: O Ali, this is your right, take it. I said: O Commander of the Believers, this year we are free of need of it, and the Muslims need it, so return it to them. So Umar returned it that year. And none called me to it after Umar, until I stood in this station of mine, when al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib met me and said: O Ali, you have taken from us today something that will never be returned to us. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ubayd. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman, from Ibn Numayr, from Hashim."
"604","Another. 640 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah informed him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, my brother narrated to me, from my father, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah in every state, and let it be said to him: May Allah have mercy on you. And let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs. I said to him: From Abu Ayyub? He said: From Ali."
"605","641 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Isa, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah, and let those around him say: May Allah have mercy on you, and let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Thaqafi al-Marwazi, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Yahya ibn Hammad, from Abu Awanah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, with its chain similarly. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yahya al-Qattan, Ali ibn Mushir, Hafs ibn Ghiyath, Hamzah al-Zayyat, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, and Abu Awanah narrated it from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from his father, from Ali; and Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj and Adi ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Haytham opposed them, narrating it from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from his father, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. The confusion is from Ibn Abi Layla, for he was poor in memory."
"606","Another. 642 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Ajami informed us, reading to him while we listened, in Baghdad - it was said to him: Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Karkhi informed you, reading to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit informed us, Abu Umar al-Qasim ibn Ja'far al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub al-Tusi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Abi Farwah, from Abd al-Rahman who said: I saw Ali perform ablution: he washed his face three times, washed his forearms three times, wiped his head once, then said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. Abu Farwah: his name is Muslim ibn Salim al-Juhani."
"607","Another. 643 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib al-Daraqazzi informed us there, that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur informed them, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted me the fifth of the fifth; I placed it in its places during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the lifetime of Abu Bakr, and the lifetime of Umar. Then wealth was brought, and he called me and said: Take it. I said: I do not want it. He said: Take it, you have more right to it. I said: We are free of need of it. So he placed it in the treasury. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Mutarrif ibn Tarif narrates it; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated it from Mutarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. Abu Awanah opposed him, narrating it from Mutarrif, from a man called Kathir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali; and this Kathir is unknown, and Mutarrif did not hear from Ibn Abi Layla. And this hadith is narrated by Abdullah ibn Abdullah al-Razi, from Abd al-Rahman, from Ali."
"608","Another. 644 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Khalaf - meaning Ibn al-Walid - narrated to us, Abu Ja'far - meaning al-Razi - and Khalid - meaning al-Tahhan - narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: As for semen, in it is ghusl; as for madhiy, in it is wudu."
"609","645 - And with it Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or it was asked about that - and he said: In madhiy is wudu, and in semen is ghusl."
"610","Another. 646 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Ahmad ibn Bundar al-Sha''ar narrated to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us. 647 - And with it Abu Nu'aym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. al-Tabarani said: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates from me a hadith while it is seen that it is a lie, he is one of the liars. The wording is al-Tabarani's. In the narration of Ibn Abi Asim, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, with him: While he sees that it is a lie, the rest the like. Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abu Abdullah ibn Majah narrated it - both - from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. It has a witness in the Sahih from the narration of Samurah ibn Jundub. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: al-A'mash narrated it from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali; and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla followed him, from al-Hakam; and Ubaydullah ibn Musa followed them both, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, so he raised it from Ali; others narrate it from al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Then - and Allah knows best - Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla heard it from Ali - peace be upon him - and from Samurah ibn Jundub, since the narrators are trustworthy."
"611","Another. 648 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il informed them, reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, al-Hulwani al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you supplications, if you say them you will be forgiven, though you are already forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Mighty; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne."
"612","649 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, with my reading to him - I said to him: Abu al-Ala' Wajih ibn Hibatullah al-Mubarak al-Saqati informed you, reading to him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Abdullah al-Raba'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Makhlad informed us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Khuldi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Sulayman - he is al-Hadrami - narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not teach you words, if you say them Allah will forgive you though you are already forgiven? There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"613","650 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you words, when you say them you will be forgiven though you are already forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Mighty; there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from Khalaf ibn Tamim, and from Safwan ibn Amr, from Ahmad ibn Khalid, both from Isra'il. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned that Hasan and Ali sons of Salih, and Yusuf ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq narrated it from Abi Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah; and the most likely is the word of one who said: from Abi Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah. Nor is the word of Isra'il to be rejected, from Abi Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali."
"614","Another. 651 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to sell two young slave brothers, so I separated between them. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Catch them up, return them, and do not sell them except together. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Wahhab, from Shu'bah, from a man, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah. Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated it from Abd al-Wahhab, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam."
"615","652 - al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Asadi al-Dimashqi informed us there, that Abu al-Qasim al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan informed them, reading to him: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ala' informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that Ali said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to sell two young slave brothers; I sold them and separated between them. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Catch them up, return them, and do not sell them except together, and do not separate between them. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Shu'bah and Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated it; Sa'id did not hear anything from al-Hakam. He mentioned a group narrating it from Sa'id, from al-Hakam. As for the hadith of Shu'bah, Waddah ibn Hassan al-Anbari narrated it from him, and Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith and Ali ibn Sahl followed them, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata', from Shu'bah. al-Daraqutni narrated it from Qadi al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili, from Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith and Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, mentioning it. I said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah has narrated it from al-Hakam."
"616","653 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Muhammad ibn Bundar al-Sha''ar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to sell two young slave brothers. He said: I sold them and separated between them. He said: I mentioned that to him, and he said: Return him."
"617","Another. 654 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Uqbah ibn Nizar al-Ansi narrated to us, Simak ibn Ubayd ibn al-Walid al-Absi narrated to us, saying: I entered upon Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, and he narrated to me that he witnessed Ali in al-Rahbah saying: I adjure by Allah a man who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and witnessed him on the day of Ghadir Khumm, except he stands; none stands except one who has seen him. Twelve men stood and said: We have seen him and heard him, when he took his hand saying: O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, oppose whoever opposes him, help whoever helps him, forsake whoever forsakes him. All but three stood; they did not stand, so he supplicated against them, and his supplication befell them. al-Walid ibn Uqbah was not mentioned by Ibn Abi Hatim in his book. Simak, he said: al-Thawri narrated from him. Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it from al-Qawariri, from Yunus ibn Arqam, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman similarly."
"618","Another. 655 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: My father used to converse at night with Ali; Ali would wear summer clothes in winter and winter clothes in summer. It was said to me: If only you asked him about this. So I asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me while I had ophthalmia on the day of Khaybar. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have ophthalmia. He spat in my eyes and said: O Allah, remove from him heat and cold. I have not felt heat nor cold since. He said: And he said: I shall send a man whom Allah and His Messenger love, and who loves Allah and His Messenger, not a fleer. He said: The people raised their heads for it. He said: So he sent Ali. Ibn Abi Layla is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman the judge; he was poor in memory. But this hadith has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Salamah ibn al-Akwa', about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spitting in the eye of Ali on the day of Khaybar. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ali ibn Hashim raised it, saying in it: from Ibn Abi Layla, from his father, from Ali. Ubaydullah ibn Musa followed him, from Ibn Abi Layla; so in these two narrations it is in the hadith of Abu Layla, from Ali. In the hadith of others it is from the hadith of Abd al-Rahman, his father, from Ali. In our narration I do not know the asker to Ali: whether it is Abu Layla or his son Abd al-Rahman."
"619","Another. 656 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Suddi Isma'il mention it, from Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali who said: When Abu Talib died I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him, then do not do anything until you come to me. He said: I buried him, then came to him. He said: Go and wash, then do not do anything until you come to me. He said: I washed, then came to him. He said: He supplicated for me with supplications, nothing of red and black camels would please me as much. He said: And Ali, when he washed the dead, would wash himself."
"620","657 - And with it Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, and Isma'il Abu Ma'mar, and Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us - Abu Ma'mar, freedman of Quraysh, said: al-Suddi informed me. Zahmawayh said in his hadith: He said: I heard al-Suddi, from Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali who said: When Abu Talib died I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him, and do not do anything about his affair until you come to me. So I buried him. He said: Go and wash, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I washed, then came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications, nothing of red and black camels would please me as much. Ibn Bakkar said in his hadith: al-Suddi said: Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - when he washed a dead person, would wash himself. Something like it is narrated in the narration of Najiyah ibn Ka'b."
"621","Abd al-Malik Abu Nawfal, from Ali, peace be upon him. 658 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bundar al-Sha''ar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Habib - brother of A'idh ibn Habib - narrated to us, from Nawfal ibn Abd al-Malik, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade bargaining before sunrise, and slaughtering milch animals. Imam Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Musa. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad and Sahl ibn Abi Sahl, from Ubaydullah ibn Musa. al-Rabi' ibn Habib Abu Salamah was declared trustworthy by Ahmad and Yahya. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not strong, and his hadiths from Nawfal are objectionable."
"622","Abd Khayr ibn Yazid al-Hamdani, Abu Umarah al-Jawwani, from Ali, peace be upon him. 659 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Za'idah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah al-Hamdani, from Abd Khayr who said: Ali entered al-Rahbah after praying Fajr, sat in al-Rahbah, then said to his lad: Bring me purification water. The lad brought him a vessel with water, and a basin. Abd Khayr said: We sat looking at him. He took the vessel with his right, poured onto his left hand and washed his palms three times. Abd Khayr said: Each time he did not enter his hand into the vessel until he washed them three times. Then he entered his right hand into the vessel, filled his mouth with water, rinsed mouth and nose, and blew with his left hand three times. Then he washed his face three times, then washed his right hand three times to the elbow, then washed his left hand three times. Then he entered his right hand into the vessel until water covered it, raised it with what it carried of water, wiped it with his left hand, then wiped his head with both hands together. Then he entered his right hand into the vessel, poured onto his right foot and washed it three times with his left hand. Then he entered his right hand into the vessel, filled it with water, poured with his right hand onto his left foot, and washed it three times with his left hand. Then he entered his right hand into the vessel, filled it with water and drank from it, then said: This is the purification of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); whoever wishes to look at the purification of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him look at this. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik, from Za'idah."
"623","660 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah ibn al-Husayn informed them, reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Malik ibn Urfutah narrated to me: I heard Abd Khayr say: I was with Ali; a chair and a tawar were brought. He said: He washed his palms three times, face three times, forearms three times, wiped his head - Yahya described beginning from the front of his head to its back - saying: I do not know whether he returned his hand or not. And washed his feet, then said: Whoever wishes to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Abd al-Rahman said to us: Shu'bah erred in it; it is Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Abu Awanah; and from al-Hulwani, from Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi, from Za'idah, all from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr; and from Ibn al-Muthanna, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah, from Malik ibn Urfutah. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, from Abu Awanah; and from Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi, from Husayn ibn Ali, from Za'idah; and from Suwayd ibn Nasr, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Shu'bah, from Malik ibn Urfutah. al-Nasa'i said: Malik ibn Urfutah is a mistake; the correct is Khalid; some abbreviated it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hibban, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Za'idah, from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, from Za'idah."
"624","661 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid informed us, Ubaydullah informed us, my grandfather Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah informed us, Khalid ibn Alqamah narrated to us, Abd Khayr narrated to us, from Ali: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped his head with both his hands once. This is a part of the preceding hadith."
"625","Another. 662 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, both saying: Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us. 663 - Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali who said: I used to see the inner sides of the feet more deserving of wiping than their outer sides, until I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe their outer sides. The wording is one. In a narration the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Isa ibn Yunus, from al-A'mash, from Abi Ishaq. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from al-A'mash."
"626","Another. 664 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, in the western side of Baghdad, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali who said: He performed ablution: rinsed mouth three times, sniffed three times from one handful, washed his face three times, then entered his hand into the rakweh, wiped his head and washed his feet. Then said: This is the ablution of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, and in it: Then he washed his feet to the ankles."
"627","Another. 665 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Uqbah Abu Kibran narrated to us, from Abd Khayr, from Ali who said: This is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he performed ablution three times each."
"628","666 - And with it Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Uqbah Abu Kibran al-Muradi narrated to us: I heard Abd Khayr say: Ali said: Shall I not show you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he performed ablution three times each."
"629","667 - And with it Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Qasim al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times each. al-Hasan ibn Uqbah was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Ma'in, and al-Qasim is trustworthy."
"630","Another. 668 - Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali regarding His saying: You are only a warner, and for every people a guide. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The warner and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim. al-Muttalib was declared trustworthy by Ahmad and Yahya. Abu Hatim said: He is not used as proof."
"631","669 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shukr al-Mu'addib informed us in Isfahan, that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muttalib ibn Ziyad, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali regarding the saying of Allah Mighty and Majestic: You are only a warner, and for every people a guide. He said: The warner is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim."
"632","Another. 670 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn al-Husayn informed them, reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Sal' narrated to us, from Abd Khayr, I heard him say: Ali stood on the pulpit, mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, and Abu Bakr - may Allah be pleased with him - was made successor; he acted by his action and followed his way until Allah - Mighty and Majestic - took him upon that. Then Umar was made successor; he acted by their action and followed their way until Allah took him upon that. Ibn Numayr narrated it from Ibn Sal'."
"633","671 - And with it Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sal', from Abd Khayr who said: I heard Ali say: Allah took His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the best state upon which a prophet among the prophets - peace be upon them - was taken. Then Abu Bakr was made successor; he acted by the action of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Prophet, and Umar likewise."
"634","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Ali, peace be upon him. 672 - Abu al-Fadl Isma'il ibn Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Khabzawi informed us, reading to him in Damascus - it was said to him: Hibatullah ibn Ahmad ibn al-Akfani informed you, reading to him - it was said to him: Abd al-Da'im ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali informed you, it was said to him: Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hasan al-Kilabi informed you: Abdullah ibn Iqab ibn al-Zifti informed us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hawari narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim al-Darir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father who said: A friend of his entered upon Ali - peace be upon him - visiting him. He said to him: I want to bequeath. Ali said: Indeed Allah says: If he leaves good. You leave only a small thing, so leave it for your dependents, for that is better."
"635","Uqbah ibn Zuhir, from Ali, peace be upon him. 673 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad, that al-Fath informed: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn ... narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrated to us, from Asim al-Jahdari, from Uqbah ibn Zuhir, from Ali ibn Abi Talib regarding His saying: So pray to your Lord and sacrifice. He said: Placing the right upon the left in prayer. Ibn Ziyad ... from Asim with this chain. Ibn Abi Hatim said: Hammad ibn Salamah and Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd differed in this hadith; Hammad said: From Asim al-Jahdari, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Zibyan, from Ali regarding His saying - Mighty and Majestic: So pray to your Lord and sacrifice, saying: Placing the right upon the left in prayer. Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrated from Asim al-Jahdari, from Uqbah ibn Zuhir, from Ali."
"636","Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ali, peace be upon him. 674 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd informed us, reading to him while we listened - it was said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The mukatab is compensated according to what he has paid. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi, from Abi Hisham al-Makhzumi, from Wuhayb; and from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, from Ishaq, from Isma'il, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ali, not raising it; and from Humayd ibn Mas'adah, from Sufyan, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Ali who said: When he has paid half, he is a debtor. al-Nasa'i said: Ibn Ulayyah is more established in Ayyub than Wuhayb, and his hadith is more likely correct. Abu Zur'ah said: From Ikrimah, from Ali, mursal."
"637","Another. 675 - Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Uqayli narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah: Ali said: When the people scattered from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, I looked among the slain and did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not flee, nor do I see him among the slain; but I see Allah - Mighty and Majestic - became angry and raised His Prophet. Nothing is better for me than to fight until I am killed. So I broke the sheath of my sword, charged upon the people, they made way for me, and behold the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"638","Those named Ali. Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Walibi al-Asadi, from Ali, peace be upon him. 676 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Abdullah al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, reading to him: Abu al-Qasim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abi Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Asadi who said: I saw Ali brought a riding animal; he placed his foot in the stirrup and said: In the name of Allah. When he settled upon it he said: Praise be to Allah. Then said: Glory be to Him who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we shall return. Then he said takbir three times, then said: There is no god but You, glory be to You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me; none forgives sins except You. Then he laughed. I said: Why did you laugh? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of what I said, then laughed. I said: Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Our Lord - Majestic and Mighty - wonders at the word of His servant: Glory be to You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me; none forgives sins except You. He said: My servant knows he has a Lord who forgives sins."
"639","677 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed us there, that Abu al-Mahasin As'ad ibn Ziyad informed them, reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Harim al-Shabbi narrated to us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq who said: Ali ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, that he witnessed Ali when he mounted: when he placed his foot in the stirrup he said: In the name of Allah. When he settled he said: Praise be to Allah. Then said: Glory be to Him who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we shall return. Then praised three times and said takbir three times, then said: There is no god but You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me; none forgives sins except You. Then laughed. It was said: What makes you laugh, O Commander of the Believers? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do the like of what I did and say the like of what I said, then laugh. We said: What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The servant - or he said: I wonder at the servant - when he says: There is no god but You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me; none forgives sins except You; he knows none forgives sins except Allah. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Waki', from Isra'il; and from Yazid ibn Harun, from Sharik ibn Abdullah; and from Abd al-Razzaq. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad. al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, both from Abi al-Ahwas. al-Nasa'i also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Qudamah, from Jarir, from Mansur, all from Abi Ishaq similarly. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn al-Junayd, from Qutaybah. al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih hadith."
"640","Another. 678 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa' al-Aquli informed us in Baghdad, that Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed them, reading to him: Abu Ja'far ibn al-Muslimah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn al-Jarrah informed us, Abdullah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah who said: Ibn al-Kawwa' stood to Ali - peace be upon him - and said: What is: By the scatterers scattering. He said: The winds. He said: What is: Then the bearers of weight. He said: The clouds. He said: What is: Then the runners with ease. He said: The ships. He said: What is: Then the distributors of command. He said: The angels. He said: What is this blackness in the moon? Ali, peace be upon him, said: And We made night and day two signs, then We erased the sign of night and made the sign of day visible. The verse. He said: O Ibn al-Kawwa', by Allah you did not intend knowledge, but you intended obstinacy; what of your saying, were you obstinate, O Ibn al-Kawwa': Who is your Lord? He said: Allah. He said: Who is the master of people? He said: Allah. He said: You have lied; Allah is the master of those who believe, and the disbelievers have no master."
"641","Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib, and it is said: he did not hear from him. 679 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Mansur ibn al-Saffar informed us, reading to him while we listened, in Nishapur - it was said to him: Your grandfather Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur informed you, reading to him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Khalaf informed us, al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Ali ibn Isa ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Najdah al-Qurashi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Muslim al-Qurashi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah informed me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn, from his father, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, grant me enjoyment of my hearing and sight until You make them the inheritors from me, grant me health in my religion and body, help me against whoever wrongs me until You show me my vengeance in him. O Allah, I have submitted my religion. O Allah, I have entrusted my affair to You, leaned my back to You, turned my face to You; no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I have believed in Your Messenger whom You sent and Your Book which You revealed. al-Hakim said: This is a hadith sahih in chain, and they did not include it. This Husayn ibn Ali from whom Musa ibn Uqbah narrated is Husayn the younger, whom Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak met. He narrated from him the hadith of the appointed times. Thus al-Hakim included it. I said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: I heard Abu Zur'ah say: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib did not reach Ali."
"642","Ali ibn Alqamah al-Anmari al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him. 680 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, reading to him: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Hiri informed us. 681 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abdullah al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali ibn Alqamah al-Anmari, from Ali who said: When was revealed: O you who believe, when you converse privately with the Messenger, send charity before your private conversation. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you see? A dinar? I said: They cannot bear it. He said: How much? I said: A barley grain. He said: You are indeed abstemious. He said: Then was revealed: Are you afraid to send charities before your private conversation. The verse. He said: Through me Allah lightened upon this nation. Their wording is one, except in the narration of al-Hiri: Through him Allah lightened. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Sufyan ibn Waki', from Yahya ibn Adam, and said: A hasan gharib hadith, we know it only through this channel. Abu Hatim narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah."
"643","Another. 682 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali ibn Alqamah, from Ali who said: A mule - or: she-mule - was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: What is this? He said: A mule - or: she-mule. I said: From what is it? He said: The donkey is put upon the mare, and this comes out between them. I said: So-and-so upon so-and-so? He said: No, only those who do not know do that. Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah is Ibn al-Mughirah."
"644","Alqamah ibn Qays ibn Abdullah al-Nakha'i al-Kufi from Ali, peace be upon him. 683 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Isbahani informed us there, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym al-Hafiz informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Sufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Maymun al-Tabban al-Madini narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Alqamah ibn Qays al-Nakha'i, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No suckling after weaning, and no orphanhood after puberty."
"645","Ilba' ibn Ahmar al-Yashkuri from Ali, peace be upon him. 684 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them, reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from al-Mundhir ibn Tha'labah, from Ilba' ibn Ahmar who said: Ali said: I proposed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his daughter Fatimah. He said: Ali sold armor of his and sold of his goods, reaching four hundred and eighty dirhams. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered two thirds to be put in perfume and a third in clothes, spat in a jar of water and ordered them to wash with it, and ordered her not to precede him in nursing her child. He said: She preceded him in nursing al-Husayn. As for al-Hasan, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did something in his mouth, it is not known what it is, so he was the more knowledgeable of the two men."
"646","Another. 685 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us there, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajali who said: Amr, nephew of Ilba', narrated to me, from Ilba' who said: Ali said: Sadaqah camels passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he took a hair from a camel's back and said: I have no more right to this hair than any man among the Muslims. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim made this Ilba' other than the first, saying: He narrated from Ali; his nephew's son Amr ibn Ghuzayy narrated from him; I heard my father say that."
"647","Umarah ibn Abd from Ali, peace be upon him. 686 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa' al-Aquli informed us in Baghdad, that Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Khayrun informed them, reading to him, saying: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslimah informed us, saying: It was read to chief Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn minister Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah - while I listened - saying: It was read to Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Umarah ibn Abd, from Ali - peace be upon him - who said: Musa and Harun went out, and Shabbar and Shabir, sons of Harun, went with them, until they reached a mountain with a couch; Harun slept upon it and passed away. When Musa returned to Banu Isra'il they said: You killed him, envying us his character and gentleness - or a word like it, Sufyan doubted. He said: How would I kill him when his two sons were with me? Choose a tribe from whomever you wish. He said: They chose ten from each tribe. He said: That is His saying: And Musa chose seventy men of his people. He said: They went until they reached him. He said: O Harun, who killed you? He said: None killed me, but Allah - Mighty and Majestic - took my soul. They said to Musa: We do not disobey. Trembling seized them. He kept going right and left, saying: My Lord, had You willed You would have destroyed them before, and me. Will You destroy us for what the foolish among us did? It is only Your trial. He said: He supplicated Allah, and He revived them and made them prophets. Umarah ibn Abd - Imam Ahmad said: Sound in hadith. Abu Hatim said: Unknown, not used as proof."
"648","Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib from his father, peace be upon him. 687 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. 688 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather: That Ali would travel until the sun set and it darkened; he dismounted, prayed Maghrib, then ate dinner, then prayed Isha right after it, then say: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Their wording is one, except Abdullah ibn Ahmad did not say: Then he ate dinner."
"649","689 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Usamah informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather: That Ali, when he traveled, would go after the sun set until it almost darkened, then dismount and pray Maghrib, then call for his dinner and eat, then pray Isha, then depart, saying: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa and Uthman. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, all from Abu Usamah."
"650","Another. 690 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Abu al-Makarim al-Mubarak ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammar al-Badara'i informed them, reading to him: Abu Ghalib Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Amr Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Dust al-Allaf informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from his father, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me for something. I said: O Messenger of Allah, when you send me for something, shall I be like the heated coin, or does the witness see what the absent does not see? He said: The witness sees what the absent does not see. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Nu'aym."
"651","Another. 691 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us there, that Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl informed them, reading to him: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us, al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi informed us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abdullah al-Juhani, from Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from his father, from his grandfather: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, three do not delay: prayer when it comes, funeral when present, and the unmarried woman when she finds a match. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id."
"652","692 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mahrabazd informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani informed us, Harmalah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abdullah al-Juhani narrated to me, that Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to him from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Ali, three do not delay: prayer when it comes, funeral when present, and the unmarried woman when she finds a match. In our hearing: be delayed. Ibn Majah narrated from it the mention of the funeral from Harmalah."
"653","693 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad al-Qati'i informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us - Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun - Ibn Wahb informed us, Sa'id ibn Abdullah al-Juhani narrated to me, that Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to him from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, O Ali, do not delay: prayer when it comes, funeral when present, and the unmarried woman when she finds a match."
"654","Another. 694 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri' informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The slogan of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O all good. Mansur ibn Abdullah was mentioned by Ibn Abi Hatim, and he mentioned no criticism in him."
"655","Another. 695 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abdullah al-Juhani, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather who said: They said to Ali: O Abu Hasan, describe for us the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He was white, his whiteness tinged with redness, long-lashed, black-eyed, neither short nor tall, closer to short; on his chest a line of hair; whoever saw him was awed by him; broad-shouldered, rough-handed and -footed, as if his sweat were pearls; when he walked he leaned forward, walking uphill; neither curly nor straight; I have not seen before him nor after him his like."
"656","Those named Amr. Amr ibn Hubshi from Ali, peace be upon him. 696 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Abdullah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us. 697 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them, reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Amr ibn Hubshi, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you send me to old people of age, and I fear I may not hit right? He said: Indeed Allah - Mighty and Majestic - will make firm your tongue and guide your heart. The wording is one. Ibn Hubshi: Abu Ishaq and Abdullah ibn al-Miqdam ibn al-Ward narrated from him."
"657","Amr ibn Hurayth ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum al-Qurashi Abu Sa'id al-Makhzumi, a Companion, from Ali, peace be upon him. 698 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn al-Husayn informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bahz and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata' - Affan said: Ya'la ibn Ata' narrated to us - from Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Amr ibn Hurayth: That he visited Hasan, with Ali present. Ali said: O Amr, do you visit Hasan while in the soul is what is in it? He said: Yes; you are not lord of my heart to turn it as you wish. He said: That does not prevent me from conveying counsel to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim visits a Muslim except Allah sends for him seventy thousand angels, praying upon him at whatever hour of the day it is until evening, or whatever hour of the night it is until morning."
"658","699 - And with it my father narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata', from Abdullah ibn Yasar: That Amr ibn Hurayth visited al-Hasan ibn Ali. Ali said to him: Do you visit al-Hasan while in your soul is what is in it? Amr said to him: You are not my lord to turn my heart as you wish. Ali said: That does not prevent us from conveying counsel to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim visits his brother except Allah sends for him seventy thousand angels praying upon him, from whatever hours of the day until evening, and whatever hours of the night until morning. Amr said to him: What do you say about walking in the funeral, ahead of it or behind it? Ali said: The excellence of walking behind it over ahead of it is like the excellence of the obligatory prayer in congregation over alone. Amr said: I saw Abu Bakr and Umar walking ahead of the funeral?! Ali said: They disliked to inconvenience people. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Hammad ibn Salamah. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated up to his saying: Morning, from Imran ibn Musa, from Hudbah ibn Khalid, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"659","Amr ibn Sufyan from Ali, peace be upon him. Already in the biography of Sa'id ibn Amr. Amr ibn Shurahbil al-Hamdani, Abu Maysarah al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him. 700 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed you, reading to him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Harith and Abi Maysarah, from Ali from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your Noble Face and all Your perfect words from the evil of what You hold by its forelock. O Allah, You remove sin and debt. O Allah, Your army is not defeated, Your promise is not broken, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail against You. Glory be to You and with Your praise."
"660","701 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus, that Ma'ali ibn Hibatullah ibn al-Hasan al-Tha'labi informed them, reading to him: Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us, Ali ibn Munir informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Khallal informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya ibn Haywah al-Naysaburi informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i informed us, Ahmad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Ahwas - meaning Ibn Jawwab - narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Harith and Abi Maysarah, from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say at his resting place: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your Noble Face and Your perfect words from the evil of what You hold by its forelock. O Allah, You remove sin and debt. O Allah, Your army is not defeated, Your promise is not broken, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail against You. Glory be to You and with Your praise. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abbas al-Anbari, from al-Ahwas. al-Nasa'i narrated it in action of day and night as we narrated it."
"661","Fadalah ibn Abi Fadalah al-Ansari from Ali, peace be upon him. 702 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad - meaning Ibn Rashid - narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Fadalah ibn Abi Fadalah al-Ansari - and Abu Fadalah was of the people of Badr - who said: I went out with my father visiting Ali ibn Abi Talib for an illness that weighed upon him. My father said: What keeps you in this house of yours? If your term comes, none but Bedouins of Juhaynah will take charge of you. Hasten to Madinah; if your term comes, your companions will take charge of you and pray upon you. Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to me that I shall not die until I am made commander, then this - meaning his beard - is dyed from the blood of this - meaning his head. He was killed, and Abu Fadalah was killed with Ali on the day of Siffin."
"662","Fatimah bint Ali ibn Abi Talib from her father, peace be upon him. 703 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'aym al-Bajali narrated to us, saying: Fatimah bint Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with them - narrated to me, saying: My father said from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever frees a Muslim or believing soul, Allah will shield with each of its limbs a limb of him from the Fire. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Nu'aym, and it is in the Musnad of Ishaq."
"663","Qays ibn Ubad al-Basri Abu Abdullah from Ali, peace be upon him. 704 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, Isma'il Abu Ma'mar narrated to me, Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Ubad who said: I said to Ali: What of this march of yours? A covenant the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to you, or an opinion you saw? He said: What do you want with this? I said: Our religion, our religion. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not covenant to me anything in it, but an opinion I saw. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Ma'mar, from Isma'il."
"664","705 - Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Salim al-Muradi narrated to us, from al-Hasan who said: When Ali came to Basrah in pursuit of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, intending to fight them, Abdullah ibn al-Kawwa' and Qays ibn Ubad entered upon him and said: O Commander of the Believers, narrate to us about this march of yours: a bequest the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeathed to you, or a covenant he covenanted to you, or an opinion you saw when the nation split and its word differed? He said: O Allah, no covenant; had he covenanted anything to me I would have stood by it. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die a sudden death nor was killed; he remained in his illness, each time the caller came announcing prayer to him, each time ordering Abu Bakr to lead people in prayer, until a woman among his wives objected in that, saying: Abu Bakr is a tender man, unable to stand in your place; order Umar to lead people in prayer. He said to her: You are the companions of Yusuf. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: Salim ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Muradi Abu al-Ala' al-An'umi - I asked my father about him, and he said: His hadith is written. I said: I think he is the one who narrated from al-Hasan. And Allah knows best."
"665","706 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abi Hashim al-Qasim ibn Kathir, from Qays al-Kharifi who said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led, Abu Bakr prayed, Umar made third, then tribulation struck us, as Allah Majestic in majesty willed. Abdullah said: My father said: His saying: Then tribulation struck us, he intended humility thereby."
"666","707 - And with it Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Kathir Abi Hashim, seller of sabiri, from Qays al-Kharifi who said: I heard Ali say upon this pulpit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led, Abu Bakr prayed, Umar made third, then tribulation struck us - or: tribulation befell us - and there was what Allah willed. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi."
"667","708 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, reading to him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hakim al-Mada'ini narrated to us, from Abi Maryam, from Ali who said: I went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we entered the Ka'bah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Sit. He climbed upon my shoulders. I went to rise with him, but he saw weakness in me, descended, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat for me and said: Climb upon my shoulders. I climbed upon his shoulders. He said: He rose with me. He said: It seemed to me that had I wished I would have reached the horizon of the sky, until I climbed upon the House, upon which was an idol of brass or copper. I kept wrestling it from its right and left, before it and behind it, until when I gained mastery over it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Throw it down. I threw it down, and it broke as glass breaks. Then I descended. I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went racing until we hid among the houses, fearing someone among people might meet us."
"668","709 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah - he is Ibn Musa - narrated to me, saying: Nu'aym ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abi Maryam: Ali said: I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we came to the Ka'bah. He said: Sit. I sat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed upon my shoulders, then I rose with him. When he saw my weakness from him, he said: Sit. I sat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended, sat for me, and said: Climb upon my shoulders. I climbed upon him. Then he rose with me until it seemed to me that had I wished I would have reached the horizon of the sky. I climbed upon the House, came to the idol of Quraysh, an image of a man of brass or copper. I kept wrestling it right and left, before it and behind it, until I gained mastery over it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come on, come on, while I wrestled it. He said to me: Throw it. I threw it, and it broke as glass breaks. Then I descended. We went running until we hid among the houses, fearing someone might learn of us. It was never raised upon it after."
"669","Another. 710 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abi Maryam, from Ali: That the wife of al-Walid ibn Uqbah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of al-Walid beating her. He said to her: Return and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has granted me protection. She went, stayed a while, then returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has not desisted from me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut a fringe from his garment and gave her. He said: Say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has granted me protection; this is a fringe from his garment. She stayed a while, then returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, he only increased beating me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and said: O Allah, upon al-Walid, twice or thrice. Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated it in the Musnad from Nasr ibn Ali and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dawud, from Nu'aym; and from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Abu Khaythamah, from Ubaydullah ibn Musa similarly."
"670","Malik ibn Umayr al-Hanafi al-Kufi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, peace be upon him. 711 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me, saying: Zayd ibn Suhan came to Ali and said: Narrate to me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade you. He said: He forbade me hantam, dubba', naqir, ji'ah, a gold ring - or he said: gold circle - silk, qassi, and the red saddle cloth. He said: A silk suit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he clothed me with it, and I went out in it. He took it and gave it to Fatimah or his aunt. Isma'il says that."
"671","712 - Abdullah said: My father narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, mentioning it with its chain and meaning, except he said: Sa'sa'ah ibn Suhan came to Ali, peace be upon him."
"672","713 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Malik ibn Umayr: That Sa'sa'ah ibn Suhan came to Ali and greeted him, saying: O Commander of the Believers, forbid us what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba', hantam, muqayyar, and ji'ah. Abu Dawud narrated up to his saying: ji'ah, from Musaddad, from Abd al-Wahid. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, both from Abd al-Wahid, from Isma'il. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim, from Marwan al-Fazari, from Isma'il similarly. We intended from mentioning this hadith only the mention of ji'ah, which is barley nabidh. This hadith is narrated from Malik, from Sa'sa'ah."
"673","Mujahid ibn Jabr al-Makki, Abu al-Hajjaj, from Ali, peace be upon him. 714 - Abu al-Ghana'im al-Muslim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Mazini al-Nasibi informed us in Damascus, that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim al-Darani informed them, reading to him: Sahl ibn Bishr al-Isfarayini informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Farisi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Nasr ibn Bujayr al-Dhuhli informed us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us. And Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad, that Abu Shuja' Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us, both saying: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Mujahid who said: Ali came out to us wrapping in a burd, enveloped in a khamisah. He said: When was revealed: So turn away from them, you are not blameworthy, none of us remained except certain of perishing, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ordered to turn away from us, until was revealed: And remind, for reminder benefits the believers. Our souls were pleased. Ali mentioned that he passed by a woman of the Ansar with clay before her. I said: Do you want to wet this clay? She said: Yes. I stipulated with her for each bucket a date. I wetted it, and she gave me sixteen dates. I brought them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This is the wording of Isma'il ibn Ishaq. In the narration of Yusuf ibn Ya'qub: wrapping in a burd, with him: He said: When was revealed. With him: from Mujahid who said: Ali mentioned that he passed by a woman of the Ansar with clay before her door. I said: Do you want to wet. With him he said: I wetted it, and she gave me sixteen. The rest the like. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Sulayman ibn Harb similarly. Wuhayb narrated part of it from Mujahid."
"674","715 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Jayyar informed us in Isfahan, that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, al-Hafiz Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah Sammuyah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, al-Mughirah ibn Salamah Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Mujahid narrated to us, saying: Ali came out to us enveloped in a khamisah, wrapped in a garment. He said: When this verse was revealed: So turn away from them, you are not blameworthy, what came after of revelation stopped; none of us but certain of perishing or confident of it. They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ordered to turn away from us. Then was revealed: And remind, for reminder benefits the believers. Imam Ahmad narrated in his Musnad from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Ayyub, from Mujahid who said: Ali said: I hungered once in Madinah severely; I went seeking work in the outskirts of Madinah, and behold a woman had gathered mud. He mentioned it, and at its end: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him; he ate with me. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from al-Makhzumi, from Wuhayb, mentioning part of the hadith. al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated, saying: It was said to Yahya ibn Ma'in: It is narrated from Mujahid that he said: Ali came out to us. He said: This is nothing. Abu Zur'ah said: Mujahid from Ali is mursal. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Mujahid reached Ali; he does not mention seeing or hearing. I said: Shu'bah, Yahya ibn Sa'id, Yahya ibn Ma'in, and Abu Hatim al-Razi denied Mujahid's hearing from A'ishah. al-Bukhari and Muslim included for Mujahid from A'ishah. Among that what Mansur narrated from Mujahid who said: I and Urwah entered the mosque; Ibn Umar sat by the room of A'ishah. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs, one of them in Rajab. We heard A'ishah clearing her throat in the room. Urwah said: O Mother of the Believers, do you not hear? The hadith. al-Bukhari narrated it from Qutaybah and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Muslim narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, all from Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid, from Mansur. al-Bukhari narrated: Do not revile the dead, for they have gone to what they sent forth. From Adam ibn Abi Iyas and Ali ibn al-Ja'd, both from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from A'ishah. He narrated from her hadith, saying: None of us had but one garment in which she menstruated ... the hadith, from Abu Nu'aym, from Ibrahim ibn Nafi', from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from her. Muslim narrated from the hadith of A'ishah: That she menstruated at Sarif and became pure on the day of Arafah ... the hadith, from al-Hasan al-Hulwani, from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, from Ibrahim ibn Nafi', from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from her. I said: Since Mujahid reached Ali, and the narration of Ayyub and Wuhayb from him: Ali came out to us, agrees, the affirmer is worthier than the denier. That is because al-Bukhari and Muslim, when they established Mujahid's narration from A'ishah, did not heed the word of one who denied his hearing from her. And Allah knows best what is correct."
"675","Another. 716 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me to Fatimah for an iron Hutami armor; he had armed me with it. He said: Send it to her to make it lawful for her thereby. I sent it to her. By Allah, its price was not such-and-four hundred dirhams."
"676","Another. 717 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, and Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Naysaburiyyah there, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudi informed us, al-Hakim Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Sukuni narrated to us in Hims, Kathir ibn Abd narrated to us, Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, from Musa al-Saghir, Mujahid narrated to us, saying: Ali said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had nothing to send to us, we sent to him from what we had. We stayed a day when he had nothing to send to us, nor we had to send to him. He said: I went out to a garden of Madinah and called: Who hires? A woman of the Ansar called me, saying: Water this basin of mine, each bucket for a date. I watered for her thirty buckets - Musa al-Saghir said: forty - and took dates from her. I brought them, sent some to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and ate some. Musa is Ibn Muslim al-Tahhan, Abu Isa al-Saghir. It is said he died in Makkah behind the Maqam while prostrating. Abu Hatim mentioned him, not mentioning him with criticism."
"677","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, peace be upon him. 718 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key of prayer is purification, its prohibition is takbir, its permissibility is taslim. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Waki'."
"678","719 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad, that Abu Shuja' Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharazah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key of prayer is purification, its consecration is takbir, its release is taslim. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, Hannad, and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad, all from Waki'. al-Tirmidhi also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abd al-Rahman, both from Sufyan. al-Tirmidhi said: This hadith is the most authentic thing in this chapter, and best. Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil is truthful; some scholars spoke about him regarding his memory. I heard Muhammad ibn Isma'il say: Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Ishaq, and al-Humaydi used the hadith of Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil as proof. Muhammad said: He is close in hadith."
"679","Another. 720 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ubaydullah - meaning al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Fitr, from Mundhir Abi Ya'la, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali: That he sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that if a child is born to him after him, to name him by his name and kunyah him by his kunyah. He said: It was a concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). His name was Muhammad, and his kunyah Abu al-Qasim. Waki' narrated it from Fitr."
"680","721 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Mundhir, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah who said: Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, what if a child is born to me after you, shall I name him by your name and kunyah him by your kunyah? He said: Yes. It was a concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Ali. Abu Dawud narrated it, and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu Usamah. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, both from Fitr similarly. al-Tirmidhi said: A sahih hadith."
"681","Another. 722 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali who said: A scorpion came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed. He said: May Allah curse you; you spare neither prophet nor other. Then he called for water and salt, and began sprinkling it upon her. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Mutarrif ibn Tarif narrated it from al-Minhal; Isma'il, son of al-Suddi's daughter, raised it from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Mutarrif, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali. Musa ibn A'yan, Asbat ibn Muhammad and others opposed him, narrating it from Mutarrif, from al-Minhal, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah mursal. Hamzah al-Zayyat likewise narrated it from al-Minhal, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah mursal, and it is more likely correct. I said: Abbad ibn Ya'qub raised it from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, our narration this."
"682","Another. 723 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Abu al-Faraj Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman al-Ghada'iri informed us in Aleppo - it was said he was of the Abdal - Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hammal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon a mule - or she-mule. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: Horses are put upon donkeys, and this comes out. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not do? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only those who do not know do that. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Sharik narrated it from Uthman - he is Ibn Umayr Abu al-Yaqzan - from Salim, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali. al-Thawri narrated it from Uthman, from Salim, from Ali, not mentioning Ibn al-Hanafiyyah. This Uthman is weak in hadith. In our hearing it occurred Ammar al-Duhni, from Salim; I do not know whether that is preserved or not."
"683","Another. 724 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Yunus ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Awn ibn Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, from his grandfather Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: I know only that we went out as pilgrims raising ihram for Hajj; neither the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor Umar - may Allah be pleased with him - became lawful until they circumambulated the House on the day of sacrifice, and Safa and Marwah. Yunus: There is no harm in him."
"684","Another. 725 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast continuously from sahar to sahar."
"685","Another. 726 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Yunus ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Awn Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, from his grandfather Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is ithmid, for it grows hair and removes dirt."
"686","727 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Hubaysh and Sulayman ibn Ahmad, among a group, narrated to us, saying: Ja'far al-Firyabi informed us, mentioning it."
"687","Another. 728 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali the elder, that he heard his father Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given four, none of Allah's prophets was given them: I was given the keys of the earth, named Ahmad, dust made purification for me, and my nation made the best of nations."
"688","729 - And with it my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdullah - meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil - from Muhammad ibn Ali, that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given what none of the prophets was given! We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it? He said: I was helped with terror, given the keys of the earth, named Ahmad, dust made purification for me, and my nation made the best of nations."
"689","Another. 730 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would eat tharid, drink milk, pray and not perform ablution."
"690","731 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was large-headed, large-eyed, long-lashed, his eye tinged with redness, thick-bearded, bright-complexioned; when he walked he leaned forward as if walking uphill, when he turned he turned wholly, rough-handed and -footed. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Affan and Hasan ibn Musa, from Hammad similarly."
"691","732 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il informed them, while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was large-headed, large-eyed, long-lashed, tinged with redness, thick-bearded, bright-complexioned, rough-handed and -footed; when he walked he leaned forward as if walking uphill, when he turned he turned wholly. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Rawh ibn Ubadah and Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"692","Another. 733 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah informed us, my father narrated to me, Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in seven garments. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan as well. It is established in the hadith of A'ishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three Sahuli garments."
"693","Another. 734 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali who said: When al-Hasan was born he named him Hamzah; when al-Husayn was born he named him after his uncle Ja'far. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: I was ordered to change the name of these two. I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So he named them Hasan and Husayn. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Zakariyya ibn Adi."
"694","Another. 735 - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'adhdhin informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Umm al-Baha' Fatimah bint Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'id ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Baghdadi informed you, reading to her - it was said to her: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi al-Muqri' informed you, reading to him: Abu al-Qasim Ja'far ibn Abdullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki al-Ruyani informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala' al-Hamdani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with him - from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: Much was said about Mariyah, mother of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, regarding a Copt cousin of hers visiting her and coming to her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take this sword, go; if you find him with her, kill him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I be in your command when you send me like the heated coin, nothing turning me until I carry out what you order me, or does the witness see what the absent does not see? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather the witness sees what the absent does not see. I came girded with the sword and found him with her. I drew the sword; when he saw me he knew I wanted him. He went to a palm, climbed it, threw himself on his back, raised his legs; behold he was castrated, smooth, having neither little nor much. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Praise be to Allah who has averted from us, people of the house. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Anas similarly."
"695","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from his grandfather Ali, peace be upon him. 736 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us. 737 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, reading to him. 738 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them, reading to him, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us, both saying: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us - Ibn al-Muqri' said: Bundar ibn Bashshar narrated to us - Abdullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhib narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Awn ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: I fought on the day of Badr; then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was prostrating, saying: O Living, O Sustainer. Then I went and fought; then I came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating, saying: O Living, O Sustainer. He said: Allah gave him victory. Their wording is one, except Ibn Hamdan has not in his narration: fighting. al-Nasa'i narrated it in action of day and night from Muhammad ibn Bashshar."
"696","Another. 739 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, Muhammad Umar - he is Ibn Ali - narrated to us, from Ali who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when you send me shall I be like the heated coin, or does the witness see what the absent does not see? He said: The witness sees what the absent does not see."
"697","Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi from Ali, peace be upon him. 740 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, that Ali said: You have seen me with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tying a stone upon my belly from hunger, and my charity today is forty thousand. I do not verify the hearing of Muhammad ibn Ka'b from Ali ... from Yazid ibn Ziyad, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b who said: One who heard Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, saying: I went out ... my house hungry, the hadith."
"698","Musayyib ibn Rafi' al-Kahili, from Ali, peace be upon him. 741 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad, that his father Abu Mansur Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubaydullah informed them, reading to him: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us, Abdullah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Ali - he is Ibn al-Ja'd - narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Ali who said: When the believer dies, his prayer place on earth weeps for him, and the ascent of his deed from heaven; then he recited: Neither heaven nor earth wept for them, nor were they reprieved."
"699","Maysarah al-Tuhawi, Abu Jamilah al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him. 742 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Warqa' informed me, from Abd al-A'la, from Abi Jamilah, from Ali: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and gave the cupper his wage."
"700","743 - And with it Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, both saying: Warqa' narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abi Jamilah, from Ali: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and ordered me, and I gave the cupper his wage. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hashim and Abu Dawud. al-Tirmidhi narrated it in the Shama'il, and Ibn Majah in his Sunan, both from Amr ibn Ali. Ibn Majah also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abadah, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Warqa'."
"701","Maysarah ibn Habib al-Nahdi Abu Hazim al-Kufi - I think he did not reach Ali - from Ali, peace be upon him. 744 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Akhdar al-Hafiz informed us in Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Nasr ibn al-Zaghuni informed them: Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Zaynabi informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Khalaf informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Sari al-Tammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Maysarah al-Nahdi who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with him - passed by people playing chess and said: What are these images to which you are devoted."
"702","Najiyah ibn Ka'b al-Anbari, and it is said al-Asadi, from Ali, peace be upon him. 745 - Abu al-Qasim Hibatullah ibn Ali ibn Sa'ud al-Ansari al-Busiri informed us, with my reading to him in Fustat - I said to him: Abu Sadiq Murshid ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini informed you, reading to him while you listened: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Naysaburi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh informed us, in words: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Muhammad, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq who said: I heard Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Ali - peace be upon him - that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Abu Talib has died. He said: Go and bury him. He said: He died a polytheist. He said: Go and bury him. When I had buried him I returned to him, and he said: Wash. Thus al-Nasa'i included it. Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Abi Ishaq."
"703","746 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Ali who said: When Abu Talib died I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old erring uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me. He said: I went, buried him, and he ordered me, so I washed. Then he supplicated for me with supplications, nothing presented of things would I love as much in their place. Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Abi Ishaq."
"704","747 - Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: When Abu Talib died I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old erring uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me. I did what he ordered me, then came to him. He said: Wash. Then he taught me supplications dearer to me than red camels. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sufyan similarly. al-Daraqutni was asked about this hadith and said: Shu'bah, al-Thawri, Isra'il, Sharik, Zuhayr, Qays, Warqa', and Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Abi Ishaq, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Ali. al-Husayn ibn Waqid and Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari opposed them, narrating it from Abi Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali; they erred in mentioning al-Harith. He mentioned other disagreement in it besides this. He said: The preserved is the word of al-Thawri and Shu'bah and whoever followed them, from Abi Ishaq, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Ali. Furat al-Qazzaz likewise narrated it from Najiyah ibn Ka'b as well. Something like it is narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali."
"705","Another. 748 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn ... informed them, reading to him: Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us, Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Farisi informed us, Abu Abdullah ibn Makhlad al-Duri informed us, Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Mu'awiyah - he is Ibn Hisham - narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Ali who said: Abu Jahl said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We do not call you a liar, but we deny what you have brought. So Allah Mighty and Majestic revealed: They do not call you a liar, but the wrongdoers deny the signs of Allah. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Mu'awiyah with its chain; and from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq, from Najiyah: That Abu Jahl ... without saying: from Ali. He said: This is more correct."
"706","749 - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Aquli informed us in Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed them, reading to him: Abu Ja'far ibn al-Muslimah informed us, Isa ibn Ali informed us, Abdullah al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Najiyah, from Ali: That he used to recite this letter: They do not call you a liar, unstressed."
"707","Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ali - peace be upon him - and Abdullah ibn Imran al-Ansari, from Ali, peace be upon him. 750 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi, Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman, and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafiyan informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, al-Haytham Abu Qatan and al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us - the wording is al-Husayn's - both saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Hurmuz, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither tall nor short, large-headed and -bearded, rough-handed and -footed, his face tinged with redness, long of the masrubah, large of the joints; when he walked he leaned forward, as if descending from a slope. I have not seen his like before him nor after him. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Rawh ibn Ubadah, Abu Nu'aym, and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, all from al-Mas'udi."
"708","751 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Mujammi' ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Imran al-Ansari, and al-Mas'udi, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Hurmuz, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither short nor tall, large-headed and -bearded, rough-handed and -footed, large of the joints, his face tinged with redness, long of the masrubah; when he walked he leaned forward as if uprooting from rock. I have not seen before him nor after him his like, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu al-Nadr said: al-masrubah. Abu Nu'aym also said: al-masrubah. He said: As if descending from a slope. Abu Qatan said: al-masrabah. Yazid said: al-masrubah."
"709","752 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed you, reading to him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ali that he described the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: He was large-headed, white, tinged with redness."
"710","753 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us: That Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, and Isma'il, son of al-Suddi's daughter, narrated to me, saying: Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that he described the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: He was large-headed, white, tinged with redness, large-bearded, large of the joints, rough-handed and -footed, long of the masrubah, abundant-headed hair, wavy; leaning in his walk as if descending in a slope; neither tall nor short. I have not seen his like before him nor after him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ali ibn Hakim said in his hadith: Ali ibn Abi Talib described for us the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: He was large-headed, good-haired, wavy. In the narration of Ibn Abi Asim: Abundant-haired, wavy, leaning in his walk. Its end: I have not seen before him nor after him his like, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"711","754 - Abu al-Izz Shihab ibn Mahmud ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hatimi informed us, with my reading to him in the Herat mosque - I said to him: Abu al-Fath Abd al-Salam ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Iskaf - known as Talbarah - and Abu Salih Dhakwan ibn Sayyar al-Dahhan informed you, reading to them while you listened - it was said to them: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Farisi informed you, saying: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Shurayhi informed us, reading to him: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Salih ibn Sa'id, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was abundant-headed hair, wavy, large-bearded, tinged in his face with redness, long of the masrubah, large of the joints; when he walked he leaned forward as if descending from a slope. I have not seen before him nor after him his like, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Isma'il, from Abu Nu'aym; and from Sufyan ibn Waki', from his father, both from al-Mas'udi, from Uthman ibn Muslim, from Nafi' similarly, saying: A sahih hadith. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it. He said: The correct is the word of one who said: From Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ali, not mentioning Jubayr in it. And Allah knows best. Some mentioned it from Nafi', from his father, from Ali; some say: From Nafi', from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"712","Nujayy al-Hadrami al-Kufi, father of Abdullah, from Ali, peace be upon him. 755 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn al-Adib informed him, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Shu'bah who said: Ali ibn Mudrik narrated to me, from Abi Zur'ah, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The angel does not enter a house in it a dog, nor one junub, nor an image."
"713","756 - And with it Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik who said: I heard Aba Zur'ah narrate from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father who said: I heard Ali narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Angels do not enter a house in it an image, nor a dog, nor one junub. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, like the narration of Zuhayr, and from Muhammad ibn Ja'far Ghundar. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik. Abu Dawud narrated it from Hafs ibn Umar. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ghundar, both from Shu'bah. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from Yahya. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, from Abu al-Walid Hisham."
"714","Another. 757 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Mudrik al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy al-Hadrami, from his father who said: Ali said: I had a station with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) none of creation had. I would come to him every dawn, greeting him until he cleared his throat. One night I came, greeted him, saying: Peace upon you, O Prophet of Allah. He said: At ease, O Abu Hasan, until I come out to you. When he came out to me I said: O Prophet of Allah, has anyone angered you? He said: No. I said: Why did you not speak to me before, until you spoke to me tonight? He said: I heard movement in the room. I said: Who is this? He said: I am Jibril. I said: Enter. He said: No, come out to me. When I went out he said: In your house is something no angel enters while it is in it. I said: I do not know it, O Jibril. He said: Go and look. I opened the house and found nothing but a puppy al-Hasan played with. I said: I found only a puppy. He said: They are three; no angel ever enters while one of them is in it: a dog, janabah, or an image of a soul. al-Nasa'i narrated it from al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya ibn Dinar, from Abu Usamah, from Shurahbil."
"715","Another. 758 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, reading to him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father that he traveled with Ali, being keeper of his purification water. When he came parallel to Nineveh, heading to Siffin, Ali called: Be patient, Abu Abdullah, be patient, Abu Abdullah, on the bank of the Euphrates. I said: What? He said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, his eyes overflowing. I said: O Prophet of Allah, has anyone angered you? What is with your eyes overflowing? He said: Rather Jibril just rose from me, informing me that al-Hasan will be killed on the bank of the Euphrates. He said: He said: Would you like me to let you smell of his dust? He said: I said: Yes. He stretched his hand, took a handful of dust and gave it to me. I could not hold my eyes from overflowing."
"716","al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah al-Hilali al-Kufi, having companionship, from Ali, peace be upon him. 759 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id informed them, saying: Ali ... al-Mu'alla al-Bahhathi informed us: Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawrani informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us: Abu Arubah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Abi Abd al-Rahim: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah: Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from Madinah as pilgrim, and I went out from Yemen. I said: Labbayk, ihram like the ihram of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have raised ihram for umrah and hajj together."
"717","Nu'aym ibn Dajajah al-Asadi, from Ali, peace be upon him. 760 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah ibn al-Husayn informed them, reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Nu'aym ibn Dajajah al-Asadi who said: I was with Ali; Abu Mas'ud entered upon him and said to him: O Farrukh, are you the one saying: A hundred years shall not come upon people while on earth an eye blinks? Your backside has missed the pit. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A hundred years shall not come upon people while on earth an eye blinks of those alive today; the ease of this nation and its relief is after the hundred."
"718","761 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Minhal, from Nu'aym ibn Dajajah who said: I was with Ali when Abu Mas'ud came. Ali said: Farrukh has come. He sat. Ali said: You give fatwa to people? He said: Yes, and inform them the last is worse. He said: Tell me, did you hear anything from him? He said: Yes, I heard him say: A year of a hundred shall not come upon people while on earth an eye blinks. He said: Your backside has missed the pit, and you erred in the first of your fatwa. He said that only to those present with him that day. Is ease except after the hundred."
"719","Nu'aym ibn Yazid, from Ali, peace be upon him. 762 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Isa al-Rasibi narrated to me, Umar ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Yazid, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to bring him a dish in which he writes what his nation shall not go astray after him. He said: I feared his soul might escape me. He said: I said: I memorize and retain. He said: I counsel prayer, zakat, and what your right hands possess. Nu'aym: I did not find him in the book of Ibn Abi Hatim."
"720","Wahb ibn al-Ajda' al-Kufi from Ali, peace be upon him. 763 - Abu al-Shuja' Ridwan ibn Muhammad ibn Mahfuz ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl, Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid, Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Mansur ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafiyyun, and Abu Zur'ah Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr al-Laftawani, all in Isfahan, that Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, reading to him: Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Abu Sa'id Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Nusayr ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' ibn Wasil al-Qurashi al-Razi informed us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Yahya ibn Daris ibn Yasar al-Bajali al-Razi informed us, saying: Muslim - he is Ibn Ibrahim - informed us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda', from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr except while the sun is high."
"721","764 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us. 765 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan and Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda', from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not pray after Asr, unless you pray while the sun is high."
"722","766 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda', from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None prays after Asr unless the sun is white, high. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Jarir. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Jarir. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abd al-Rahman; and from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah, from Ya'qub al-Dawraqi, from Jarir."
"723","Wahb ibn Abdullah Abu Juhayfah al-Suwa'i the Companion, from Ali, peace be upon him. 767 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, reading to her: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Ziyad al-Hadhdha' al-Raqqi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad al-A'war narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Juhayfah, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah is more just than to double His punishment upon His servant in the Hereafter; whoever commits a sin in this world, Allah covers it for him and pardons him, Allah is more generous than to return to something He has pardoned and covered."
"724","768 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us - Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq said: informed me - from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Juhayfah, from Ali."
"725","769 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Isbahani informed us there, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym al-Hafiz informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us: Isma'il ibn Abdullah Sammuyah narrated to us: al-Husayn - he is Ibn Hafs - narrated to us: Hajjaj al-A'war narrated to us: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abi Juhayfah, from Ali."
"726","770 - My maternal uncle, the imam, the scholar Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim al-Narsi informed us: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Abu Juhayfah, on authority of Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it - and al-Narsi said: is punished for it - then Allah is too just to repeat His punishment upon His servant, and whoever commits a sin and Allah conceals it and pardons him, then Allah is too just to return to something He has already pardoned. Al-Narsi said: then Allah concealed him. And al-Husayn ibn Hafs said: to return to something He has already pardoned. And the rest is the same. Al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Abu Abdah ibn Abi al-Safar. And Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hammal, both of them on authority of Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, and al-Tirmidhi said: a hasan gharib hadith. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement concerning it, and that it was reported mawquf and marfu, he said: and what is correct is on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Abu Juhayfah, and its being raised (to the Prophet) is correct."
"727","Another 771 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah informed them - recited to him - Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asadi Luwayn narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us: on authority of Ziyad ibn Zayd al-Suwai, on authority of Abu Juhayfah, on authority of Ali who said: It is part of the Sunnah in prayer to place the palms upon the palms beneath the navel. And Abu Muawiyah reported it on authority of Abd al-Rahman, except that he said: Ziyad ibn Ziyad."
"728","772 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Maamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Ibn Abi Umar - he is Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Adani - informed us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us: on authority of Ziyad ibn Ziyad al-Suwai, on authority of Abu Juhayfah, on authority of Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: It is part of the Sunnah in the prescribed prayer to place the hands upon the hands beneath the navel."
"729","Another 773 - And with it, on authority of Ziyad ibn Ziyad, on authority of Abu Juhayfah, on authority of Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: And it is part of the Sunnah in the prescribed prayer that when a man rises in the first two rakahs he should not lean upon the ground unless he is a very old shaykh unable to do otherwise."
"730","Another 774 - The imam, the hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ali al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us - by ijazah if it was not hearing - that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed them - in Baghdad - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ayyub al-Bazzaz informed us: Abu Tahir Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Muaddib informed us: Abu Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf narrated to us: Abu al-Abbas Sahl ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman al-Wasiti - known as Ibn Abi Sahl - narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Tai informed us: Muammal ibn Ismail informed us: on authority of Sufyan, on authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on authority of Abu Juhayfah, on authority of Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to the people of Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are sending me to a people and I have no knowledge of judging, so he placed his hand upon my chest and said: Indeed Allah - mighty and majestic - will guide your heart and steady your tongue, so when the two disputants sit before you, do not judge for the first until you have heard from the other, just as you heard from the first, for that is more likely to make the judgment clear to you. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I remained a judge after that, or: I never doubted a judgment after that."
"731","Hani ibn Hani al-Hamdani, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 775 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ubayd Allah - meaning Ibn Umar - informed us: Ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: Ammar came seeking permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Give him permission, welcome to the pure one, the purified one. Israil and Shubah reported it on authority of Abu Ishaq."
"732","776 - Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us - in Baghdad - that Ismail ibn Ahmad al-Samarqandi informed them - recited to him - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal informed us: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Nifri informed us: Muhammad - he is Ibn Rawh al-Junday Saburi - narrated to us: Harun - he is Ibn Ishaq - narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: Ammar sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recognized his voice, and said: Welcome to the pure one, the purified one."
"733","777 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah informed them - recited to him - Al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali: that Ammar sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The pure one, the purified one? Give him permission. Al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Bundar, on authority of Ibn Mahdi, and said: a hasan sahih hadith. And Ibn Majah brought it on authority of Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi, on authority of Waki, on authority of Sufyan. And Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, on authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, on authority of Waki, on authority of Sufyan."
"734","Another 778 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us - in Baghdad - that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan al-Amiri narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: on authority of Israil, on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and Jafar and Zayd, and he said to Zayd: You are our brother and our freedman, he said: so he hopped. Then he said to Jafar: You resemble my creation and my character, he said: so he hopped behind the hopping of Zayd. Then he said to me: You are from me and I am from you, so I hopped behind the hopping of Jafar."
"735","779 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Husayn informed us - recited to him - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdun informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hajjaj narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani and Hubayrah ibn Yarim, on authority of Ali: that the daughter of Hamzah followed them calling: O uncle, O uncle. So Ali took her, he took her hand, and said to Fatimah: Take your cousin and carry her away, then Ali and Zayd and Jafar disputed concerning her, so Ali said: I took her and she is my cousin. And Jafar said: She is my cousin and her maternal aunt is married to me. And Zayd said: She is my brother's daughter, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged her to belong to her maternal aunt, and said: The maternal aunt is in the position of the mother, then he said to Ali: You are from me and I am from you, and he said to Jafar: You resemble my creation and my character, and he said to Zayd: You are our brother and our freedman, so Ali said to him: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry the daughter of Hamzah? So he said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. And Imam Ahmad also reported it on authority of Yahya ibn Adam, on authority of Israil. And Abu Dawud brought it on authority of Abbad ibn Musa, on authority of Ismail ibn Jafar, on authority of Israil, with something similar. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban reported from it, concerning Jafar: You resemble my creation and my character, on authority of al-Hasan ibn Nabhan, on authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Musa."
"736","Another 780 - The judge Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us - in Baghdad - that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them - recited to him - Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Khallal informed us - recited to him - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Shihab al-Daqqaq al-Nifri informed us - recited to him - Muhammad ibn Nuh - he is Ibn Abdullah al-Junday Saburi - narrated to us: Harun - he is Ibn Ishaq - narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: Indeed al-Hasan most resembled the people in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the chest to the head, and al-Husayn from below that."
"737","781 - And al-Mubarak informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil informed us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani who said: Ali said: Al-Hasan most resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the chest to the head, and al-Husayn resembled what is below that. Al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, on authority of Israil, and said: a hasan gharib hadith. And Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, on authority of al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, on authority of Shabbabah, on authority of Israil."
"738","Another 782 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us - in Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them - recited to him - [...] ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi and Mansur ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn Janah al-Wasiti narrated to us: [...] narrated to us: Nasr ibn Ali Abu Amr al-Jahdami narrated to us: Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us: on authority of al-Amash, on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani who said: Ammar sought permission to enter upon Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, so he said: Give him permission, welcome to the pure one, the purified one, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ammar is filled with faith up to his marrow. Ibn Majah brought it on authority of Nasr ibn Ali. And Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, on authority of Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam, on authority of Aththam."
"739","Another 783 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: When al-Hasan was born I named him Harb, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son, what did you name him? I said: Harb, he said: Rather he is Hasan, then when al-Husayn was born I named him Harb, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son, what did you name him? He said: I said: Harb, he said: Rather he is Husayn. Then when the third was born I named him Harb, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son, what did you name him? I said: Harb, he said: Rather he is Muhassin. Then he said: I named them by the names of the children of Harun: Shabbar, and Shabir, and Mushabbir."
"740","784 - And Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Umari informed us that Ismail ibn al-Samarqandi informed them - recited to him - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Khallal informed us: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Nifri informed us: Muhammad - he is Ibn Nuh - narrated to us: Harun - he is Ibn Ishaq - narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: When al-Hasan was born, then he mentioned something similar. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it in his Musnad, on authority of al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, on authority of Israil."
"741","Another 785 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Asbahani informed us there that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah Sammuyah narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Ibn Abi Zaidah - he is Yahya - narrated to us: on authority of his father, on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: Abu Bakr used to lower his voice when he recited, and Umar used to recite aloud, and a man - Sammuyah said: and others than I reported on authority of Sahl: Ammar - would take from this surah and from that surah, so it was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to Abu Bakr: Why do you lower your voice? He said: I let Him whom I converse with hear. And he said to Umar: Why do you recite aloud? - Sammuyah said: from my memory - He said: I drive away Satan and awaken the drowsy. And he said to the man - meaning Ammar - Why do you take from this surah and that surah? He said: Do you see me mixing with it what is not of it? He said: No. He said: Then all of it is good."
"742","786 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us - in Baghdad - that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them - recited to him - Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khalili informed us: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai narrated to us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Mughaffal al-Shashi informed us: al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us: Ali ibn Bahr al-Qattan narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali who said: Abu Bakr used to lower his voice when he recited, and Umar used to recite his recitation aloud, and Ammar when he recited would take from this surah and that surah, so that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to Abu Bakr: Why do you lower your voice? He said: I let Him whom I converse with hear. And he said to Umar: Why do you recite your recitation aloud? He said: I frighten Satan and awaken the drowsy. And he said to Ammar: Why do you take from this surah and that surah? He said: Do you hear me mixing with it what is not of it? He said: No, he said: Then all of it is good. Imam Ahmad reported it on authority of Ali ibn Bahr with its chain, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali, without doubt."
"743","787 - Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan informed us - in Nishapur - that Fatimah bint al-Hasan ibn al-Muzaffar al-Baghdadi informed them - recited to her - Abd al-Ghafir ibn Muhammad al-Farisi informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Mikal informed us: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan al-Jawaliqi informed us: Sahl ibn Uthman al-Abdi narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hani ibn Hani, on authority of Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: Abu Bakr - may Allah be pleased with him - used to lower his voice when he recited, and Umar - may Allah be pleased with him - used to recite aloud, and Ammar - may Allah be pleased with him - would take from this surah and that surah. He said: So that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to Abu Bakr: Why do you lower your voice? He said: I let Him whom I converse with hear. And he said to Umar: Why do you recite aloud? He said: I frighten Satan and awaken the drowsy. And he said to Ammar: Why do you take from this surah and that surah? He said: Do you hear me mixing with it what is not of it? He said: Then all of it is good."
"744","Hubayrah ibn Yarim ibn Abd Wudd al-Hamdani, Abu al-Harith al-Kufi, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 788 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them - recited to him - Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hubayrah, on authority of Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the gold ring, and the mitharah (soft saddle cloth), and al-qassi (silk garments), and al-jiah (a drink vessel). We intended from it only the mention of al-jiah. Imam Ahmad reported the mention of al-jiah - I think in the Book of Drinks - on authority of Abu Kamil, on authority of Zuhayr ibn Abi Ishaq. And Abu Dawud reported it on authority of Hafs ibn Umar and Muslim ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Shubah, on authority of Abu Ishaq, and he did not mention al-jiah. And al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Qutaybah, on authority of Abu al-Ahwas, and in it is the mention of al-jiah, and he said: a sahih hadith. And al-Nasai reported it on authority of al-Mukharrimi, on authority of Yahya ibn Adam, and on authority of Zuhayr, on authority of Qutaybah, on authority of Abu al-Ahwas, all of them on authority of Abu Ishaq, and in it is al-jiah, and on authority of Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, on authority of Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, on authority of Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, on authority of Abu Ishaq. And Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. He has another hadith already mentioned in the biography of Hani, mentioning the daughter of Hamzah, peace be upon him."
"745","Another 789 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: on authority of Sufyan and Shubah and Israil, on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hubayrah, on authority of Ali that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to awaken his family in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"746","790 - And al-Mubarak ibn al-Mattush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us (H). 791 - And al-Muayyad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that al-Husayn informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala informed us, they both said: Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us: - and Abdullah said: narrated to me - Abu Ishaq, on authority of Hubayrah ibn Yarim, on authority of Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to awaken his family in the last ten nights, and would lift the waist-wrapper. Their wording is one. Al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Ghaylan, on authority of Waki, on authority of Sufyan, and said: a hasan sahih hadith."
"747","Yazid ibn Umayyah al-Dayli, Abu Sinan, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 792 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali al-Warraq narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me: on authority of Abu Sinan Yazid ibn Umayyah al-Dayli who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib fell severely ill until he was near death and we feared for him, then he recovered and convalesced, so we said to him: Glad tidings to you, Abu Hasan, praise be to Allah who has healed you, we had feared for you. He said: But I did not fear for myself, the truthful one believed (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that I shall not die until I am struck upon this - and he pointed to the front left of his head - and this is dyed from it with blood - and he took his beard - and he said: The most wretched of this ummah will kill you, just as the most wretched of the sons of so-and-so of Thamud hamstrung the she-camel of Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traced him to his nearest clan apart from Thamud. Yazid ibn Umayyah al-Dayli: Abu Zurah al-Razi deemed him trustworthy."
"748","Yusay al-Hadrami al-Kufi, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 793 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi informed us - in Cairo - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn al-Shaybani informed them - recited to him - Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii informed us: Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us - meaning on authority of al-Amash - on authority of Dharr, on authority of Yusay who said: A man came to Ali and said: Allah says: {Allah will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will never grant the disbelievers a way over the believers} - yet these believers are being killed?! So Ali said: Come near: Allah will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will never grant the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection a way over the believers."
"749","Al-Kuna: Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 794 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us: Abu Zaidah Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us: al-Muharibi narrated to us: on authority of Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, on authority of Abu Burdah, that Abu Musa entered upon al-Hasan ibn Ali visiting him when sick, so Ali said to him: Have you come to us as a visitor or as a visitor of your nephew through sickness? He said: No, rather I came visiting the sick, so Ali said: Indeed I heard him - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - say: Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits, mercy overwhelms him. Abu Hayyan: his name is Yahya ibn Hayyan. And al-Muharibi, his name is Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad, both of them are among the men of the Sahih of al-Bukhari."
"750","Abu Hayyah ibn Qays al-Wadii al-Hamdani, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 795 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Abu Hayyah who said: I saw Ali performing ablution, so he washed his palms until he cleaned them, then rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water three times and washed his face three times and his forearms three times, and wiped his head and washed his feet to the ankles, and took the remainder of his purification water and drank it while standing, then said: I wanted to show you how the purification of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was."
"751","796 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Asbahani informed us there that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - recited to him while he was present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari informed us: on authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on authority of Israil ibn Yunus, on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Abu Hayyah ibn Qays who said: I witnessed Ali in al-Rahbah, he urinated then performed ablution, so he washed his palms three times, and rinsed and sniffed three times, and washed his face three times, and his forearms three times each, and wiped his head and washed his feet three times, then stood upright, then took and drank the remainder of his ablution water, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do, so I wanted to show you. Abu Dawud reported it on authority of Musaddad, and Abi Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi, and Amr ibn Awn. And al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Hannad and Qutaybah. And al-Nasai reported it on authority of Qutaybah, all of them on authority of Abu al-Ahwas with something similar. And Ibn Majah reported part of it on authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, on authority of Abu al-Ahwas."
"752","797 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: on authority of Sufyan, on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Abu Hayyah, on authority of Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times each. Imam Ahmad reported it on authority of Abd al-Rahman. And al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Bashshar, on authority of Ibn Mahdi, and said: It is the best thing in this chapter, and the most correct. And al-Nasai reported it on authority of Abu Dawud al-Harrani, on authority of Abi Attab Sahl ibn Hammad, on authority of Shubah, on authority of Abu Ishaq with it, more complete than the first."
"753","Another 798 - My maternal uncle, the imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Abu Zurah Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed them - recited to him in Baghdad - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Muqaddami informed us: al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us, he said: Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah al-Qattan informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Abu Ishaq, on authority of Abu Hayyah, on authority of Ali who said: I used to draw the bucket for a date, stipulating that it be a firm (good) one. Thus Ibn Majah reported it in his Sunan."
"754","Abu Khalifah, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 799 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us - in Baghdad - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them - recited to him - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Umar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us (H). 800 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, they both said: Abu Yala informed us: Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Umar narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated to me: on authority of his father, on authority of Abu Khalifah, on authority of Ali, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed Allah - mighty and majestic - is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives for it what He does not give for harshness."
"755","801 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us - my father said: I heard him narrating - on authority of Abdullah ibn Wahb, on authority of Abu Khalifah, on authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah is Gentle, loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."
"756","Abu Razin, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 802 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Maamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us - in Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them - recited to him - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Musa ibn Abi Aishah, on authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Razin, on authority of his father, on authority of Ali who said: I said to al-Abbas: Ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the chamberlainship (custody of the Kaba) for us, so he said: He will give you what is better for you than it: the watering (siqayah), which brings you provision and is not taken from you. Yahya ibn Main was asked about a hadith reported by Musa ibn Abi Aishah on authority of Abdullah ibn Razin on authority of Abu Razin on authority of Ali, so it was said to Yahya: Who is this Abu Razin? So he said: Thus it is, and he did not know him."
"757","Umm Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, and she has companionship, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him, and in some narrations: Umm Masud ibn al-Hakam, and she has companionship, and I think she is she, and she may have two sons from two husbands, and Allah knows best, and it is possible that this one is different from that one. 803 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah informed them - recited to him - Al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abdullah narrated to me: on authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, on authority of Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, on authority of his mother who said: We were at Mina, when a crier cried out: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Do not fast, for they are days of eating and drinking. She said: So I lifted the ropes of the tent, and the crier was Ali ibn Abi Talib. Imam Ahmad also reported it on authority of Qutaybah, on authority of Layth ibn Sad, on authority of Ibn al-Had, on authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, on authority of Amr ibn Sulaym, on authority of his mother, with something similar. And likewise al-Nasai reported it on his authority."
"758","804 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them - recited to him - Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us - by ijazah - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Isa ibn Hammad Zughbah narrated to us - by dictation - he said: al-Layth ibn Sad informed us: on authority of Yahya ibn Said, on authority of Yusuf ibn Masud ibn al-Hakam, on authority of his grandmother that she said: While we were at Mina, a rider approached and I heard him calling out: They are days of eating and drinking, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: Who is this? He said: Ali ibn Abi Talib. Al-Nasai reported it on authority of Isa ibn Hammad."
"759","805 - And Zahir also informed us - in Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them - read to him - Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed us, and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr narrated to him on authority of Sulayman ibn Yasar that Masud ibn al-Hakam narrated to him on authority of his mother that she said: A rider passed by us while we were at Mina with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling out among the people: Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking. So my sister said: This is Ali ibn Abi Talib. And I said: Rather he is so-and-so. Al-Nasai reported it on authority of Ahmad ibn al-Haytham, on authority of Harmalah."
"760","Umm Musa, and it is said: her name is Habibah, on authority of Ali, peace be upon him. 806 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us: Mughirah narrated to us: on authority of Umm Musa, on authority of Ali who said: The last speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Prayer, prayer, fear Allah concerning what your right hands possess."
"761","807 - Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us - in Baghdad - that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them - recited to him - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal informed us: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Nifri informed us: Muhammad - he is Ibn Nuh al-Junday Saburi - narrated to us: Harun - he is Ibn Ishaq - narrated to us: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us: on authority of al-Mughirah, on authority of Umm Musa, on authority of Ali - peace be upon him - that he said: The last speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Prayer, prayer, fear Allah concerning what your right hands possess. Imam Ahmad reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Fudayl. And Abu Dawud reported it on authority of Zuhayr, he is Ibn Harb. And Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Sahl ibn Abi Sahl, on authority of Ibn Fudayl, and he did not say: Fear Allah concerning what your right hands possess."
"762","Another 808 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Musa informed us: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us: on authority of al-Mughirah, on authority of Umm Musa who said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Ibn Masud to climb a tree and bring him something from it, so his companions looked at the thinness of his legs and laughed at them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are you laughing at? The leg of Abdullah on the Day of Resurrection will be heavier than Uhud."
"763","809 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Asbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them - recited to her - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us: on authority of Mughirah, on authority of Umm Musa who said: I heard Ali say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Ibn Masud to climb a tree and bring him something from it, so his companions looked at the thinness of his legs and laughed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you laugh? The leg of Abdullah on the Day of Resurrection will be heavier than Uhud. Imam Ahmad reported it on authority of Ibn Fudayl."
"764","Another 810 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them - recited to him - Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: on authority of his father, on authority of Mughirah, on authority of Umm Musa, on authority of Ali who said: I have not suffered eye inflammation since the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in my eye."
"765","811 - And al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us: on authority of Mughirah, on authority of Umm Musa who said: I heard Ali say: I have neither suffered eye inflammation nor headache since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped my face and spat in my eye on the day of Khaybar when he gave me the banner."
"766","812 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them - recited to him - Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us: on authority of Mughirah, on authority of Umm Musa who said: The killer of al-Zubayr sought permission to enter upon Ali, so he said: Let him enter the Fire, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"767","The tenth part of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah of Diya al-Maqdisi. Musnad of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah al-Taymi, may Allah be pleased with him. From the Musnad of Abu Muhammad Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Amir ibn Kab ibn Sad ibn Taym ibn Kab ibn Luayy al-Taymi, may Allah be pleased with him. 813 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush informed us, with my recitation to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, recited to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Man al-Ghifari narrated to me: Dawud ibn Khalid ibn Dinar informed me that he and a man called Abu Yusuf from Banu Taym passed by Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abu Yusuf said to him: We find with others than you hadith that you do not have! So he said: I have much hadith, but Rabiah ibn al-Hudayr said - and he used to keep to Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah -: that he never heard Talhah narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) any hadith at all except one hadith. Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman said: I said to him: And what is it? He said: Talhah said to me: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we overlooked Harrat Waqim, he said: so we drew near to it, and there were graves at Mahniyyah, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, are these the graves of our brothers? He said: The graves of our companions, then we went out until when we came to the graves of the martyrs, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are the graves of our brothers. It was reported on authority of Uthman [...] there is preserved from him only this hadith, on authority of Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, on authority of Rabiah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hudayr, on authority of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he came to the graves of the martyrs. And Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Dawud ibn Khalid ibn Dinar reported on authority of Rabiah, Muhammad ibn Man al-Ghifari and Ibn Abi Fudayk reported on his authority. Abu Dawud reported it on authority of Hamid ibn Yahya, on authority of Muhammad ibn Man, with something similar."
"768","Another 814 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath, grandson of Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mandah, informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah informed us: Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: my father narrated to us: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, on authority of Abi Anas Malik ibn Abi Amir who said: I was with Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah when a man entered upon him and said: O Abu Muhammad, by Allah I do not know whether this Yemeni knows the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than you, or he is lying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! So he said: By Allah we do not doubt that he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what we did not hear, and knew what we did not know, we were a wealthy people with houses and families, so we used to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the two ends of the day, and he was a poor man with neither wealth nor family, his hand was only with the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would go around with him wherever he went, so we do not doubt that he knew what we did not know, and heard what we did not hear, and we have not found anyone in whom there is good attributing to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say. Meaning: Abu Hurayrah."
"769","815 - And Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadan informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ararah informed us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq: on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Abi Anas ibn Abi Amir who said: I was with Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah when a man entered upon him and said: O Abu Muhammad, by Allah we do not know whether this Yemeni knows the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than you, or he says about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say? So he said: By Allah we do not doubt that he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what we did not hear, and knew what we did not know, we were a wealthy people with houses and families, and we used to come to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the two ends of the day then return, and he was a poor man with neither wealth nor family, his hand was only with the hand of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would go around with him wherever he went, so we do not doubt that he knew what we did not know, and heard what no one heard, and we shall never find anyone in whom there is good saying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say. Meaning: Abu Hurayrah. Abu Yala al-Mawsili also reported it on authority of Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid, on authority of al-Khadir ibn Muhammad al-Harrani, on authority of Muhammad ibn Salamah, on authority of Ibn Ishaq. Al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on authority of Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani, on authority of Muhammad ibn Salamah, on authority of Ibn Ishaq. And he said: a hasan gharib hadith."
"770","Another 816 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Abu Kurayb informed us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: on authority of Talhah ibn Yahya, on authority of Musa and Isa, the two sons of Talhah, on authority of their father, that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a bedouin who came asking him about who has fulfilled his vow, who is he? And they did not dare to ask him, honoring him and fearing him, he said: So the bedouin asked him, and he turned away from him, then he asked him and he turned away from him, then I appeared from the door of the mosque wearing green garments, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me he said: Where is the one asking about who has fulfilled his vow? The bedouin said: I am, O Messenger of Allah, he said: This is among those who have fulfilled their vow."
"771","817 - And Asad ibn Sad ibn Rawh informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, recited to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub narrated to us: my father narrated to me: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Uhud he ascended the pulpit, so he praised Allah, mighty and majestic, and extolled Him, then recited this verse: {Men who were true to what they covenanted with Allah} the whole verse, so a man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is he? So I came forward wearing two green garments, so he said: O questioner, this is among them."
"772","818 - And Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Isa ibn Musa ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Uhud he ascended the pulpit and recited this verse: {Men who were true to what they covenanted with Allah}, so a man asked him and said: O Messenger, who are they? So I came forward wearing two green garments, so he said: O questioner, this is among them."
"773","819 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Isa ibn Musa ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: on authority of my grandfather Sulayman, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father Talhah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and we returned to Medina he ascended the pulpit and preached, and recited this verse: {Men who were true to what they covenanted with Allah} the whole verse, so a man said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? So I came forward wearing two green garments, so he said: O questioner, this is among them. Al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala, and said: a hasan gharib hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Yunus ibn Bukayr. I say: And this narration of Ayyub ibn Sulayman is other than the narration of Yunus ibn Bukayr. And Talhah ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah: al-Bukhari said: munkar al-hadith. And al-Nasai said: Not strong. And Yahya ibn Main said: Trustworthy. And Abu Zurah said: His hadith is sound, and he is more beloved to me. And Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: He reported on authority of his father, on authority of his grandfather, Ahmad ibn al-Fadl al-Asqalani and Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi and Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hisinjani reported on his authority, and he did not mention any criticism of him. I say: And al-Fadl ibn Sukayn ibn Sukhayt al-Sindi - and he reported on authority of this Sulayman - said: Sulayman is trustworthy. And Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Isa, he said: He reported on authority of his father and on authority of Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, his son Sulayman reported on his authority. And al-Bukhari said in his Tarikh: Sulayman ibn Isa, Said ibn Yahya ibn Said said: my father narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Isa narrated to us: on authority of his grandfather Musa: I was captured on the day of the Camel and Ali brought me."
"774","Another 820 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Musa Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hammal narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Sulayman - he is Ibn Sufyan - narrated to me, he said: I heard Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah narrating on authority of his father, on authority of his grandfather Talhah who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the crescent he said: O Allah, bring it upon us with blessing and faith and safety and Islam, my Lord and your Lord is Allah."
"775","821 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Amir narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Sufyan al-Madini narrated to us: Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me: on authority of his father, on authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he saw the crescent said: O Allah, bring it upon us with blessing and faith, and safety and Islam, my Lord and your Lord is Allah. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it in his Musnad on authority of Abu Amir. And al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Bundar, on authority of Abu Amir, and said: a hasan gharib hadith. Sulayman ibn Sufyan al-Madini, Abu Sufyan: Yahya ibn Main and Abu Hatim al-Razi and al-Daraqutni spoke about him."
"776","Another 822 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us, recited to him in Baghdad, that the imam Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us: Mujammi ibn Yahya narrated to us: on authority of Uthman ibn Mawhab, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of Talhah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"777","823 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us (H). 824 - And Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Adnan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Nizar informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Ali - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman - informed us, they both said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: on authority of Mujammi ibn Yahya, on authority of Uthman ibn Mawhab, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we have known how to greet you with peace, so how do we send blessings? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and bless Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"778","825 - And with this chain, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Isa ibn Musa ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, my father narrated to me: Sulayman narrated to me: on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father Talhah who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This tashahhud we have known, so how do we send blessings upon you? So he said to me: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and bless Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. Imam Ahmad and Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it in their two Musnads on authority of Muhammad ibn Bishr. And al-Nasai reported it on authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Muhammad ibn Bishr. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Israil and Sharik narrated it on authority of Musa ibn Mawhab, on authority of Musa, on authority of his father, and Khalid ibn Sulayman al-Makhzumi reported it on authority of Musa, on authority of Zayd ibn Kharijah, and it is the most correct of them."
"779","Another 826 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad informed me: on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, that two men from Bali accepted Islam, so one of them was killed in the path of Allah, and the other was delayed a year after the one killed, then died. Talhah said: I saw Paradise in a dream, and I saw the latter of the two men admitted to Paradise before the first, so in the morning I narrated that to the people, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Did he not fast Ramadan after him and pray after him six thousand rakahs? And such-and-such rakahs."
"780","827 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Abi Salamah who said: Two men from the people of Yemen stayed with Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, so one of them was killed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the other remained a year after him, then died on his bed, so Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah was shown that the one who died on his bed entered Paradise a while before the other, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How long did he remain after him? He said: A year, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He prayed one thousand eight hundred prayers and fasted Ramadan."
"781","828 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Maamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them both, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us: on authority of Ibn al-Had, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on authority of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah: that two men from Bali came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and their acceptance of Islam was one together, and one of them was more striving than the other, so the striving one of them raided and was martyred, then the other remained a year after him then died. Talhah said: While I was at the gate of Paradise I saw them both, then one who goes out came out and gave permission to one of them, the latter of the two who had died, then he returned and gave permission to the one who was martyred, then he said: Return, for your time has not yet come, so in the morning Talhah narrated to the people and they marveled at that, and it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they narrated the hadith to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: At which of that do you marvel? They said: O Messenger of Allah, this one was the more striving of the two men, then he was martyred in the path of Allah, then the other entered Paradise before him! So he said: Did this one not remain a year after him? They said: Yes, he said: And he reached Ramadan and fasted and prayed such-and-such prostrations in the year? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between them is farther than what is between heaven and earth. Imam Ahmad also reported it on authority of Qutaybah ibn Said, on authority of Bakr ibn Mudar, on authority of Ibn al-Had. And Ahmad ibn Mani reported it on authority of Yazid ibn Harun, on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it on authority of al-Fadl ibn Musa and Abdah ibn Sulayman, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of Imran ibn Musa, on authority of Yaqub ibn Humayd, on authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad and Ibn Abi Hazim, one of them adding to his companion, on authority of Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had. And Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Rumh, on authority of al-Layth ibn Sad, on authority of Ibn al-Had, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of Talhah. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of Imran ibn Musa, on authority of Yaqub ibn Humayd, on authority of Abd al-Aziz, some of them shortened it and some reported it in full. Ibn Abi Khaythamah said: Yahya ibn Main was asked about this hadith and said: Mursal, he did not hear from Talhah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: It is a hadith reported by Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, on authority of Abi Salamah, Yazid ibn al-Had and Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated it on his authority; as for Yazid ibn al-Had, he connected it on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, and Muhammad ibn Ishaq left it unconnected (mursal) on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Abi Salamah, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah reported it on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of Talhah, and there is disagreement on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, so Ismail ibn Jafar and Yazid ibn Harun reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of Talhah. And Hammad ibn Salamah and Said ibn Amir reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr. And Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi and al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani and Muhammad ibn Yala and Junadah ibn Salm reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of Abi Hurayrah: that Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah saw in a dream. And the most correct of them all is the word of Yazid ibn al-Had, and the mention of Abi Hurayrah in it is a mistake, and Allah knows best."
"782","Another 829 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim and Umm Habibah Aishah bint Maamar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us: on authority of Yahya ibn Said, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, on authority of Isa ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, on authority of his father, that he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Safaih al-Rawha, when we came upon a hamstrung donkey, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This donkey, its seeker is about to come, he said: So we did not remain long before its owner came, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, to divide it among the traveling companions, he said: Then we went out until when we were at Athayat al-Arj there was a gazelle with an arrow in it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Bakr to stand over it and protect it from the people, he said: And the owner of the donkey was a man from Bahz. Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Hisham ibn Ammar, on authority of Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, with something similar. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ibn Uyaynah alone reported it on authority of Yahya ibn Said. Al-Daraqutni reported it on authority of Abu Umar Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Qadi, on authority of Ismail ibn Ishaq, on authority of Ali ibn al-Madini, on authority of Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, and mentioned it. Ali ibn al-Madini said: I said to Sufyan when I came to this hadith: This hadith on authority of Isa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father, that it is [...] al-Thaqafi, on authority of Yahya ibn Said, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Isa ibn Talhah, on authority of Umayr ibn Salamah, on authority of al-Bahzi? So Sufyan said: I thought it was on authority of Talhah, and I am not certain of it, but as for the hadith I have brought it to you. Al-Daraqutni said: And what is correct with us is that this hadith was reported by Umayr ibn Salamah, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no one between him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"783","Another 830 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated to us: Talhah ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to me: on authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, on authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that a group of three men from Banu Udhrah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam, he said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will take care of them? Talhah said: I will, he said: So they stayed with Talhah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, so one of them went out in it and was martyred, he said: Then he sent another expedition, so another went out in it and was martyred, he said: Then the third died on his bed, he said: Talhah said: So I saw these three who had stayed with me in Paradise, and I saw the one who died on his bed ahead of them, and I saw the one who was martyred last following him, and I saw the one who was martyred first of them last of them, he said: So something entered me from that, he said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, he said: So he said: And what did you find objectionable in that? There is no one better with Allah than a believer who lives long in Islam for his glorification and magnification and declaring Allah one. Abd ibn Humayd reported it in his Musnad on authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, on authority of Waki. And al-Nasai reported it in the Book of the Deeds of Day and Night, on authority of Zakariyya ibn Yahya, on authority of Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, on authority of Waki, with something similar. And Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported it in his Musnad on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri, on authority of Abdullah ibn Dawud, on authority of Talhah ibn Yahya with its chain, something similar."
"784","Another 831 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us (H). 832 - And Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, recited to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Isa ibn Musa ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me on the day of Uhud: Talhah the Good, and in the expedition of Dhu al-Ushayrah: Talhah the Generous, and on the day of Hunayn: Talhah the Bountiful. Their wording is one, and al-Hasan ibn Ali added, so he said: Whoever wishes to look at a martyr upon the face of the earth, let him look at Talhah, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me he said: My predecessor in this world and the Hereafter. Abu al-Qasim - meaning al-Tabarani - said: With sin and shin both, with sin meaning: hardship (al-usrah), and with shin: a place."
"785","Another 833 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed me - with my recitation to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you, recited to him while you were present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, he said: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Isa ibn Musa ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates a hadith from me and lies, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"786","834 - And the hafiz, the imam Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us in his book that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, recited to him: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Ismail al-Tirmidhi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman Abu Ayyub al-Talhi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates from me and lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"787","835 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: al-Fadl ibn Sukayn ibn Sukhayt al-Sindi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Isa ibn Musa ibn Talhah narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Al-Fadl said: This Sulayman was Kufan, trustworthy. Ibn Said reported it on authority of Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi, on authority of Sulayman ibn Ayyub."
"788","Another 836 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, recited to him while we listened, it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed you, recited to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub narrated to us: my father narrated to me: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of Talhah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given a favor, let him mention it, so whoever mentions it has thanked for it, and whoever conceals it has been ungrateful for it."
"789","Another 837 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Asbat narrated to us: Mutarrif narrated to us: on authority of Amir, on authority of Yahya ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: Umar saw Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah heavy-hearted and said: What is wrong with you, has the leadership of your cousin displeased you, O Abu so-and-so? He said: No, except that I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nothing prevented me from asking him about it except ability over it until he died, I heard him say: Indeed I know a word that no servant says at his death except that his color brightens for it, and Allah relieves his distress. He said: So Umar said: Indeed I know what it is, he said: And what is it? He said: Do you know a word greater than a word with which he commanded his uncle at death: There is no god but Allah. Talhah said: You have spoken the truth, by Allah it is it. And this hadith has already come in the Musnad of Umar ibn al-Khattab with its paths."
"790","Another 838 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdullah al-Khallal al-Adib informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Qasim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: on authority of Talhah ibn Yahya, on authority of Yahya and Isa, the two sons of Talhah, on authority of their father who said: A camel branded on its face was brought past the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: If only the owners of this camel would move the Fire away from this beast, he said: So I said: I shall brand in the farthest place from its face, he said: So I branded on the root of the tail."
"791","Another 839 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, recited to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was among a group of his companions with a quince in his hand turning it over, so when I sat with him he pushed it toward me, then said: Take it, Abu Muhammad, for it strengthens the heart, and perfumes the soul, and removes the heaviness of the chest."
"792","840 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us of it, recited to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed you, recited to him while you were present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub narrated to us with its chain, the like of it."
"793","Another 841 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us, recited to him while we listened in Isfahan, it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed you, recited to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub narrated to us: my father narrated to me: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of Talhah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Part of humility is being content with the lowest of the sitting places of gatherings."
"794","Another 842 - And with it, on authority of Talhah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The one who marries among his people is like the one who brings herbage to his home."
"795","Another 843 - And with it, on authority of Talhah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was never a prophethood except that after it came killing and crucifixion."
"796","Another 844 - And with it, on authority of Talhah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Amr ibn al-As is among the righteous of Quraysh."
"797","Another 845 - And with it, Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of my grandfather, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of Talhah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Amr, indeed you are of sound opinion in Islam."
"798","Another 846 - And with it, on authority of Talhah: he prayed with a people, then when he finished he said: I forgot to seek your permission before I went ahead of you, are you pleased with my prayer? They said: Yes, and who would dislike that, O disciple of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man who leads a people while they dislike him, his prayer does not pass beyond his ear."
"799","Another 847 - And with it, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: On the day of Uhud I made the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon my back until he stood upright, and came upon the rock, and was concealed from the polytheists, so he said: Like this, and he gestured with his hand behind my back: This is Jibril, peace be upon him, informed me that he will not see you on the Day of Resurrection in terror except that he will rescue you from it."
"800","Another 848 - And with it, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: On the day of Uhud an arrow struck me, so I said: Hass (in pain), so he said: If you had said: In the name of Allah, the angels would have flown with you while the people looked at you."
"801","Another 849 - And with it, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me he said: My predecessor in this world and my predecessor in the Hereafter."
"802","Another 850 - And with it, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me he said: Whoever wishes to look at a martyr walking upon the face of the earth, let him look at Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah."
"803","Another 851 - And with it, on authority of Musa ibn Talhah, on authority of his father who said: The saddle and the perfume of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were entrusted to me, so a man came asking him for one of them, so he said: That is with Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, so he came to me and informed me, so I refused him, so he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he replied to him with the like of that, so he came to me and informed me, so I refused him, so he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said the like of that, so he returned to me, so I said to myself: He has not sent him to me except that he wishes to fulfill his need, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hardly asked anything except that he did it, and that I should attend to the person of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more beloved to me than that I should attend to his saddle, so I handed it to him, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended a journey, so he commanded that a saddle be prepared for him, so he came to me and said: Which of the two saddles was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So I said: The Taifi one, so he saddled it for him, then brought it near to him, so when it rose with him it overturned, so he said: Who saddled this? They said: So-and-so, so he said: Return it to Talhah, so it was returned to me. Talhah said: By Allah I did not deceive anyone in Islam except him, so that the saddle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would return to me."
"804","Musnad of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him). Musnad of Abu Abdullah al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam ibn Khuwaylid ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy ibn Kilab ibn Murrah al-Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him. 852 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Muhammad - meaning Ibn Amr - narrated to us: on authority of Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: When this surah was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Indeed you will die and indeed they will die, then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute}, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will there be repeated upon us what was between us in this world along with private sins? He said: Yes, it will surely be repeated upon you until every possessor of a right is given his right, so al-Zubayr said: By Allah, the matter is severe."
"805","853 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, recited to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us in Mecca: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Dubayli narrated to us: Sad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, on authority of Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, on authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: When {Then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute} was revealed, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will dispute be repeated upon us after what was between us in this world? He said: Yes, he said: The matter is then severe."
"806","854 - And Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: on authority of Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: When this verse was revealed: {Indeed you will die and indeed they will die}, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will there be repeated upon us what happens between us in this world along with private sins? He said: Yes, it will surely be repeated upon you until every possessor of a right is returned his right. Al-Zubayr said: The matter is severe. And Ahmad ibn Mani also reported it on authority of Yazid ibn Harun, on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, with something similar."
"807","855 - And al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Maamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, on authority of Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of his father who said: When this verse was revealed: {Indeed you will die and indeed they will die} until he reached {you will dispute}, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will dispute be repeated upon us after what was between us in this world? He said: Yes, he said: The matter is then severe. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it on authority of Abdah ibn Sulayman and Abi Usamah, on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr. And Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported it in his Musnad on authority of Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah and Abi Khaythamah, on authority of Sufyan. And al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani, and said: a hasan sahih hadith. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ali ibn Mushir and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl and Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Khalid al-Wasiti and al-Fadl ibn Musa reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on authority of Yahya, on authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr. And Abdah ibn Sulayman and Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on authority of Yahya, on authority of Ibn al-Zubayr who said: When it was revealed, so he made it from the Musnad of Ibn al-Zubayr, and those mentioned before from the Musnad of al-Zubayr, and what is correct is Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, and the word is the word of whoever connected it on authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr, and Allah knows best."
"808","Another 856 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them, recited to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us: my father narrated to me: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on authority of Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, on authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When {Then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute} was revealed, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, along with our disputing in this world? He said: Yes, and when {Then you will surely be questioned that Day about bliss} was revealed, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, what bliss shall we be questioned about? And they are only - meaning: the two black ones, dates and water - He said: Indeed that shall be."
"809","857 - And Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Harbadhqani informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Baghban informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to me: Abbas ibn Mujashi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on authority of Ibn Hatib, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: When this verse was revealed: {Then you will surely be questioned that Day about bliss}, they said: O Messenger of Allah, and what bliss shall we be questioned about? And they are only the two black ones, dates and water, so he said: Indeed that shall be. Dropped from this narration: on authority of Ibn al-Zubayr."
"810","858 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Khallal informed you, recited to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us in Mecca: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Dubayli narrated to us: Abu Abdullah Said ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, on authority of Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of his father who said: When {Then you will surely be questioned that Day about bliss} was revealed, al-Zubayr said: And what bliss, when it is only the two black ones, dates and water? He said: Indeed it shall be. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah both reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar, on authority of Sufyan, and he said: a hasan hadith. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated it on authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on authority of Yahya, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr. And Ziyad ibn Ayyub reported it on authority of Ibn Uyaynah, and did not mention in it Ibn al-Zubayr, he shortened it and left it unconnected, and the word is the word of whoever connected it."
"811","Another 859 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah that Abu al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed them, recited to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abdullah ibn al-Harith of the people of Mecca, Makhzumi, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Insan narrated to me - he said, and he praised him well -: on authority of his father, on authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Liyyah, until when we were at al-Sidrah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the edge of the Black Qarn facing it, and faced Nakhib with his sight - meaning: a valley - and stood until all the people gathered, then said: Indeed the game of Wajj and its thorny trees are a sanctuary, inviolable. And that was before his descent upon al-Taif and his besieging Thaqif."
"812","860 - Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us that Umar al-Bistami informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Shuayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Insan al-Thaqafi narrated to us: on authority of his father, on authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of his father al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: We came with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Liyyah, until when we were at al-Sidrah the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the edge of the Black Qarn, and faced the people with his sight, and stood until all the people gathered, then said: Indeed the game of Wajj is inviolable, and its thorny trees are inviolable, inviolable, and that was before his descent upon Thaqif. Imam Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith. And Imam Abu Dawud reported it on authority of Hamid ibn Yahya, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith. Al-Daraqutni said: al-Baghawi dictated it to us on authority of Ahmad ibn Hanbal, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, so he said: on authority of Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Insan, rather it is Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abdullah, thus Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Musa ibn Harun narrated it on authority of Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and likewise al-Humaydi and Ishaq said, and Allah knows best."
"813","Another 861 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: on authority of his father, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that day: Talhah has made (Paradise) obligatory, when Talhah did with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did. Ibn Ishaq said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud rose toward a rock of the mountain to ascend it, and he had grown heavy and had put on two coats of mail, so when he went to rise and could not, Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah sat beneath him and he rose until he stood upon it."
"814","862 - And Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Sinan al-Harawi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on authority of Yahya ibn Abbad, on authority of his father, on authority of his grandfather Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that day: Talhah has made (it) obligatory."
"815","863 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah informed us: my father narrated to me: Yaqub narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of Ibn Ishaq: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: on authority of his father, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that day: Talhah has made (it) obligatory, when Talhah did with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did, meaning when Talhah knelt for him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended upon his back. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, on authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Wahb ibn Jarir, on authority of his father, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq with its chain, saying: Talhah has made (it) obligatory."
"816","Another 864 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Harbadhqani informed us in Isfahan that Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghban informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: on authority of his father, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: By Allah, I hear the saying of Muattib ibn Qushayr, brother of Banu Amr ibn Awf, while drowsiness overcomes me, I hear it only as in a dream, when he said: {If we had anything of the matter, we would not have been killed here}."
"817","865 - My mother Umm Ahmad Ruqayyah bint Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah, may Allah have mercy on her, informed us, with my recitation to her, I said to her: Abu al-Muzaffar Hibat Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Samarqandi informed you by ijazah: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Niali informed them while he was present: Abu al-Qasim al-Hasan ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mundhir informed us, recited to him: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Nahwi narrated to us by dictation: Sadan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: By Allah, I hear the saying of Muattib ibn Qushayr, brother of Banu Amr ibn Awf, while drowsiness overcomes me, I hear it only as in a dream: {If we had anything of the matter, we would not have been killed here}. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it with its meaning on authority of Yahya ibn Adam, on authority of Ibn Abi Zaidah, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"818","866 - The imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja al-Waiz informed us, recited to him while we listened, on the street between Cairo and Egypt, it was said to him: Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed you, recited to him while you listened: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Azdi informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub al-Mahbubi informed us: Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi informed us: Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: on authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on authority of Thabit, on authority of Anas, on authority of Abi Talhah who said: I raised my head on the day of Uhud and I looked, and there was none of them that day except swaying under his shield from drowsiness, so that is His saying: {Then He sent down upon you after distress security, drowsiness}. And Abu Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
"819","867 - And with it, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: on authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on authority of his father, on authority of al-Zubayr, the like of it, he said: This is a hasan hadith."
"820","Another 868 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja al-Bistami informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Isa ibn Ahmad al-Asqalani narrated to us: Yazid narrated to us: Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to us: on authority of his father that Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt asked al-Zubayr for divorce, and she disliked him and there was harshness in him toward women, so he refused her that, until labor pains struck her, so she pressed him while he was performing ablution for prayer, and she did not leave him until he divorced her one divorce, then he went out and a man of his family met him and informed him that she had given birth, he said: She has deceived me, may Allah deceive her, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: The Book of Allah has preceded concerning her, so propose to her, so he said: She shall not return to me. Ibn Majah reported it in his Sunan on authority of Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj, on authority of Qabisah, on authority of Sufyan, on authority of Amr ibn Mihran, on authority of his father, on authority of al-Zubayr. I do not think Maymun ibn Mihran reached al-Zubayr, and Allah knows best."
"821","Another 869 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mattush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sulayman - meaning al-Taymi - informed us: on authority of Abi Uthman, on authority of Abdullah ibn Amir, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, that a man gave a horse called Ghamrah or Ghamra in charity, he said: So he found a horse or a foal attributed to that horse, so he was forbidden from it."
"822","870 - And Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us that Umar ibn Abdullah informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn al-Munadi - he is Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah - narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: al-Taymi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Amir narrated to us: on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, that a man gave a horse called Ghamrah or Ghamra in charity - or he said: so he found a foal being sold, or a filly - so it was attributed - or: she was attributed - to that horse, so he was forbidden from it."
"823","871 - And with it, Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: on authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on authority of Abi Uthman al-Nahdi, on authority of Ibn Amir, that al-Zubayr gave a horse in the path of Allah in charity, so he found a horse of its offspring being sold, so he was forbidden to buy it. Ahmad ibn Mani and Ishaq ibn Rahawayh both reported it on authority of Yazid ibn Harun. And Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Yahya ibn Hakim, on authority of Yazid ibn Harun. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Sulayman al-Taymi reports it on authority of Abi Uthman, on authority of Abdullah ibn Amir, on authority of al-Zubayr, Yazid ibn Zuray and Ibn al-Mubarak and Yazid ibn Harun said it on authority of al-Taymi, and Asim al-Ahwal opposed him and reported it on authority of Abi Uthman, on authority of Ibn Abbas, that al-Zubayr gave a horse in the path of Allah in charity, and likewise Yahya al-Qattan said on authority of al-Taymi, in agreement with Asim. And it is said: on authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on authority of Abi Uthman, on authority of Amir, that al-Zubayr."
"824","Another 872 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah that Hibat Allah informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Shaddad - meaning Ibn Said - narrated to us: Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us: on authority of Mutarrif who said: We said to al-Zubayr: O Abu Abdullah, what has brought you? You neglected the caliph until he was killed, then you came seeking his blood. Al-Zubayr said: We used to recite it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abi Bakr and Umar and Uthman: {And fear a trial that will not afflict only those who wronged among you}, we did not think that we were its people until it fell from us where it fell."
"825","873 - And Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Shukr al-Tamimi informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Muhammad informed us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan, he said: al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said: This verse was revealed while we were numerous with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {And fear a trial that will not afflict only those who wronged among you}, so we said: What is this trial? Who are these people? And we did not perceive that it fell where it fell. Al-Nasai reported it on authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on authority of Ibn Mahdi, on authority of Jarir ibn Hazim. And Umar ibn Habib reported it on authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on authority of al-Hasan, he said: Jawn ibn Qatadah narrated to me, he said: al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated to me. And Ruwaym ibn Yazid reported it on authority of Sallam, on authority of Yunus, on authority of al-Hasan, on authority of Abi Salit, on authority of al-Zubayr. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Muqri alone reported it on authority of Sallam ibn Sulayman al-Qari, on authority of Yunus, on authority of al-Hasan, on authority of Abi Salit, on authority of al-Zubayr, and the companions of Yunus opposed him and said: on authority of al-Hasan, on authority of al-Zubayr, and likewise Dawud ibn Abi Hind and Ali ibn Zayd and Mubarak ibn Fadalah reported it on authority of al-Hasan, on authority of al-Zubayr, it is what is preserved, and Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wasawisi reported it on authority of Ishaq al-Azraq, on authority of Dawud, on authority of al-Hasan, on authority of Jawn ibn Qatadah, on authority of al-Zubayr."
"826","Another 874 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Abi al-Zinad - informed us: on authority of Hisham, on authority of Urwah who said: My father al-Zubayr informed me that on the day of Uhud a woman came running until she almost reached the slain, he said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that she should see them, so he said: The woman, the woman. Al-Zubayr said: So I realized she was my mother Safiyyah, he said: So I went out running to her, and I caught her before she reached the slain, he said: So she struck my chest - and she was a strong woman - she said: Away from me, may you have no mother. He said: So I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has adjured you. He said: So she stopped and brought out two garments with her, and said: These are two garments I brought for my brother Hamzah, for his killing has reached me, so shroud him in them. He said: So we brought the two garments to shroud Hamzah in them, when beside him was a slain man of the Ansar to whom had been done as had been done to Hamzah, he said: So we felt reluctance and shame that Hamzah be shrouded in two garments while the Ansari had no shroud, so we said: A garment for Hamzah and a garment for the Ansari, so we measured them, and one of them was larger than the other, so we cast lots between them, and we shrouded each one in the garment that came out for him. Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported it in his Musnad on authority of Abi Khaythamah, on authority of Sulayman ibn Dawud. And al-Haytham ibn Kulayb reported it on authority of al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah, on authority of Sulayman. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad: Yahya and Abu Hatim said: He is not used as proof, and Malik ibn Anas deemed him trustworthy."
"827","Another 875 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jawzjani informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us: Ahmad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa narrated to us at Askar Mukram: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Dinar al-Tahi narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us: on authority of his father, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suck and two sucks do not prohibit, nor one swallow and two swallows. Abu Hatim reported it in his book, and before it the hadith of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and after it his hadith on authority of Aishah, then he said: I do not deny that Ibn al-Zubayr heard this report from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and heard it from his father and his maternal aunt Aishah on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so at one time he rendered what he heard, and at another he reported on their authority, and this is something widespread among the Companions."
"828","Another 876 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Amr ibn Safwan al-Madini narrated to us: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed us: on authority of his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning or an evening expedition in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it. Al-Daraqutni was asked about the hadith of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr - meaning on authority of his father - who said: Whoever prays the prayer and sits in his place until the sun rises, it is like a morning expedition in the path of Allah, so he said: Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwadhi reports it on authority of Amr ibn Safwan al-Jumahi, on authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of his father, and Haytham al-Duri reported it on authority of Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari, on authority of Husayn ibn Muhammad, and said in it: on authority of Safwan ibn Amr, and he erred in it, rather it is Amr ibn Safwan."
"829","877 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdullah al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Abd al-Samad narrated to us: on authority of Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah al-Dastuwa'i, on authority of Abi al-Zubayr, on authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would preach or remind of the days of Allah until that was recognized in his face, as if he were a warner of a people saying: The matter comes upon you in the morning. He said: And when he had recently been with Jibril, peace be upon him, he would not smile laughing until he had departed from him."
"830","878 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us that Hibat Allah informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us: on authority of Hisham, on authority of Abi al-Zubayr, on authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah or Maslamah - Kathir said: And my memory is: Salamah - on authority of Ali or on authority of al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would preach to us and remind us of the days of Allah until that was recognized in his face, as if he were a warner of a people whom the matter reaches in the morning, and when he had recently been with Jibril he would not smile laughing until he had departed from him. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it in his Musnad on authority of Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith."
"831","Another 879 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yaqub narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Abdullah ibn Ata ibn Ibrahim, freedman of al-Zubayr, narrated to me: on authority of his mother and his grandmother Umm Ata, they both said: By Allah, it is as if we are looking at al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam when he came to us upon a white mule of his, and said: O Umm Ata, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has forbidden the Muslims to eat of the meat of their sacrifices beyond three days. She said: I said: May my father be ransom for you, what do we do with what was gifted to us? He said: As for what was gifted to you, do with it as you wish."
"832","880 - And al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of Ibn Ishaq who said: Abdullah ibn Ata ibn Ibrahim, freedman of al-Zubayr, narrated to us: on authority of his mother and his grandmother Umm Ata, they both said: By Allah, it is as if we are looking at al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam when he came to us upon a white mule of his, and said: O Banu Ata, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has forbidden the Muslims to eat the meat of their sacrifices beyond three days, so do not eat it. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, what do we do with what was gifted to us? He said: What was gifted to you, do with it as you wish. Here he made the whole hadith from the words of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"833","Another 881 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mattush informed us that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Attab - he is Ibn Ziyad - narrated to us: Abdullah, he is Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us: Fulayh ibn Muhammad informed us: on authority of al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave al-Zubayr a سهم, and his mother a سهم, and his horse two shares. Thus Imam Ahmad reported it in his Musnad: Fulayh ibn Muhammad, on authority of al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr. And al-Bukhari said in his Tarikh: Fulayh ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam al-Qurashi al-Madani, on authority of his father, mursal; Ibn al-Mubarak reported on his authority."
"834","Another 882 - Abu Muhammad Hibat Allah ibn Yahya ibn Ali ibn Jaldah al-Misri informed us there that Abdullah ibn Rifa'ah ibn Ghadir ibn Ali al-Sa'di informed them, recited to him: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khulai informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Ishaq al-Tujibi al-Nahhas informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar ibn al-Ward al-Baghdadi informed us: Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi informed us: Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham informed us: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated to us: on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Muttalibi: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: on authority of his father Abbad, on authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr that he said: By Allah, I saw myself looking at the anklets of Hind bint Utbah and her companions with their garments tucked up, fleeing, with nothing - little or much - between us and seizing them, when the archers inclined toward the camp after we had uncovered the enemy from it, and left our backs exposed to the cavalry, so we were attacked from behind us, and a crier cried out: Indeed Muhammad has been killed, so we turned back, and the enemy turned upon us after we had struck the standard-bearers so that none of the enemy drew near him. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it with something similar, longer than this, on authority of Wahb ibn Jarir, on authority of his father, on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"835","Another 883 - Abu Najih Fadl Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ahmad al-Jawzjani informed us, recited to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed you, recited to him while you listened in Nishapur: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ismail ibn Yahya al-Harbi informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Hashim ibn Habban al-Tusi narrated to us: Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us: on authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim who said: Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said: Whoever among you is able to have a hidden store of righteous deed, let him do it. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani reports it on authority of Ibn Fudayl, on authority of Ismail, on authority of Qays, on authority of al-Zubayr, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was not followed in raising it, and Shubah and Zuhayr and Yahya al-Qattan and Hushaym and Ali ibn Mushir and Ibn Uyaynah and Abu Muawiyah and Abdah and Muhammad ibn Yazid reported it on authority of Ismail, on authority of Qays, on authority of al-Zubayr, halted (mawquf), and it is what is correct."
"836","884 - My maternal uncle, the imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed them, recited to him: ... It was said to him: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed you: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii and Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar informed us, they said: Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us: on authority of Ismail, on authority of Qays, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever among you is able to have a hidden store of righteous deed, let him do it."
"837","Another 885 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us: on authority of Muslim ibn Jundub, on authority of al-Zubayr (H)."
"838","886 - And Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us: on authority of Muslim ibn Jundub, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would rush into the thickets and find only the space of our feet. The wording of Ahmad ibn Mani. And the narration of Imam Ahmad said: We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would leave and rush into the thickets, and find only the measure of the space of our feet. Yazid said: al-ajam, that is al-utam (the fortified houses). And Imam Ahmad also reported it on authority of Yahya ibn Adam, on authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on authority of Muslim ibn Jundub: one who heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated to me, he said: We used to pray the Friday prayer ... the hadith."
"839","Another 887 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Hamdun ibn Abbad al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Yazid narrated to us: Hisham al-Dastuwa'i informed us: on authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on authority of Yaish ibn al-Walid (H). 888 - And Abu Muawiyah Shayban al-Tamimi, on authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on authority of Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (H)."
"840","889 - And the imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah Shayban informed us: on authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on authority of Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disease of the nations before you has crept to you: envy and hatred, and hatred is the shaver, the shaver of religion, not the shaver of hair."
"841","890 - And with it, on authority of Yaish ibn al-Walid, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you will not believe until you love one another; shall I not inform you of a matter which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread peace among you. Ahmad reported it in his Musnad, and with him it is all one hadith, on authority of Yazid ibn Harun, on authority of Hisham al-Dastuwa'i and Abi Muawiyah Shayban. And Imam Ahmad also reported it on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, on authority of Harb ibn Shaddad, on authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: that Yaish ibn al-Walid narrated to him: that a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr narrated to him: that al-Zubayr narrated to him, and mentioned it. And he also reported it on authority of Abi Amir, on authority of Ali ibn Mubarak, on authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on authority of Yaish: that a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr narrated to him that al-Zubayr narrated to him. And he reported it on authority of Ibrahim ibn Khalid, on authority of Rabah, on authority of Mamar, on authority of Yahya, on authority of Yaish, on authority of a freedman of the family of al-Zubayr. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: And the word is the word of Harb ibn Shaddad and whoever followed him, on authority of Yahya."
"842","Another 891 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muslim ibn Sulayman al-Arbili informed us, recited to him, I said to him: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Asakir ibn al-Murahhib al-Bataihi informed you, recited to him while you listened: Abu Talib Abd al-Qadir ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Muhammad informed you, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us, recited to him, he said: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Warraq, known as Ibn al-Askari, informed us: Harun ibn Yusuf - he is Ibn Ziyad al-Shatawi - narrated to us: Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us: Umm Urwah bint Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me: on authority of her father Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of her grandfather al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blessed al-Zubayr, and his children, and the children of his children. Umm Urwah said: And I am among those reached by the blessing of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Marwan, I think he is Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Khalid ibn Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Walid ibn Uthman ibn Affan al-Qurashi al-Umawi, the shaykh of Abu Abdullah Ibn Majah; Abu Hatim al-Razi deemed him trustworthy. Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported it in his Musnad on authority of Zuhayr ibn Harb, on authority of Muhammad al-Hasan al-Madani al-Makhzumi, on authority of Umm Urwah - as I think - bint Jafar ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, on authority of her father, on authority of her grandfather al-Zubayr. And al-Makhzumi is spoken about."
"843","Another 892 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us: Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us: the two sons of al-Mundhir, Ubayd Allah and Muhammad, narrated to us: on authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on authority of his father, on authority of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, that the Messenger of Allah said: Whoever wishes his record to please him, let him increase in it seeking forgiveness. Al-Tabarani said: This hadith is not reported on authority of al-Zubayr except with this chain; Atiq ibn Yaqub alone reported it. And Abd Allah and Muhammad are the two sons of al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr, and Allah knows best."
"844","893 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Salamah ibn Abi Jamil informed us, recited to him while we listened in Damascus, it was said to him: Abu Muhammad Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Faris al-Ansari al-Akfani informed you, recited to him while you listened, it was said to him: Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Daim ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd Allah al-Hilali al-Qattan informed you, it was said to him: Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hasan ibn Musa ibn Rashid al-Alai informed you, recited to him, he said: Abu al-Abbas Abdullah ibn Attab ibn al-Zifti informed us, recited to him while I listened: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hawari narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim al-Darir narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: on authority of his father, on authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on authority of al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for me his two parents on the day of Uhud. It has been mentioned in the Sahih that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for him his two parents on the day of the Trench, and the day of Uhud was before the Trench, so this hadith is other than that. The eleventh part of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah of Diya al-Maqdisi."
"845","Musnad of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him). From the hadith of Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ibn Abd Awf ibn al-Harith ibn Zuhrah ibn Kilab al-Zuhri (may Allah be pleased with him). 894 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Umm Habibah Aishah bint Maamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadham informed us: Abu Muhammad Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: on authority of Abi Salamah who said: Abu al-Raddad complained, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf visited him, so Abu al-Raddad said: The best of them and the most joining of kin I know, Abu Muhammad. So Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah the Exalted said: I am Allah, and I am al-Rahman, I created the womb, and derived for it from My name, so whoever joins it I join him, and whoever cuts it I cut him off."
"846","895 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: on authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on authority of Mamar, on authority of al-Zuhri: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Raddad al-Laythi informed him, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah said: I am Allah, and I am al-Rahman, I created the womb, and split for it from My name, so whoever joins it I join him, and whoever cuts it I cut him off. Imam Ahmad and Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it on authority of Abd al-Razzaq, and with them both it is (that Raddad al-Laythi), and thus Mamar reported it."
"847","896 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: on authority of al-Zuhri: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me: that Abu al-Raddad al-Laythi informed him, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: I am al-Rahman, and I created the womb, and derived for it from My name, so whoever joins it Allah joins him, and whoever cuts it I cut him off. Imam Ahmad also reported it on authority of Sufyan ibn Uyaynah. And Abu Yala al-Mawsili reported it on authority of Abi Khaythamah, on authority of Sufyan, as the narration of al-Adani. And Abu Dawud reported it on authority of Musaddad and Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, on authority of Sufyan, and on authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Asqalani, on authority of Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi, on authority of Sufyan, and said: a sahih hadith. And Mamar reported this hadith on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of Raddad al-Laythi, on authority of Abd al-Rahman, and Mamar - thus he says. Muhammad - meaning al-Bukhari - said: And the hadith of Mamar is mistaken. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, on authority of Hibban, on authority of Abdullah, on authority of Mamar. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it, and said: Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq reported it on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Abi Salamah: that Abu al-Raddad informed him, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: And what is correct is the hadith of Ibn Abi Atiq and whoever followed him. And this hadith has been reported on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf by other than this path."
"848","897 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Khaythamah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hisham al-Dastuwa'i informed us: on authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz: that his father narrated to him that he entered upon Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf visiting him when sick, so Abd al-Rahman said to him: May kinship join you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah the Exalted said: I am al-Rahman, and it is the womb, I split for it from My name, so whoever joins it I join him, and whoever cuts it I cut him - or he said: whoever cuts it off, I cut him off."
"849","898 - And Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Maamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi, recited to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hisham al-Dastuwa'i informed us: on authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz: that his father narrated to him that he entered upon Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf visiting him when sick, so Abd al-Rahman said to him: May kinship join you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: I am al-Rahman, and it is the womb, I split for it from My name, so whoever joins it I join him, and whoever cuts it I cut him - or he said: whoever cuts it off, I cut him off. Imam Ahmad reported it on authority of Yazid ibn Harun. And al-Haytham ibn Kulayb reported it on authority of Isa ibn Ahmad al-Asqalani - Asqalan of Balkh - on authority of Yazid, with something similar. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Hisham al-Dastuwa'i reports it on authority of Yahya, on authority of Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Qariz: that his father narrated to him, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. And Shayban reported it on authority of Yahya, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz narrated to me: that a man informed him, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. And likewise Aban said: on authority of Yahya. And there is disagreement on authority of al-Awzai: Said ibn Ishaq and Ibn Abi al-Ushrin said: on authority of al-Awzai, on authority of Yahya, on authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, he said: so-and-so narrated to me, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. And al-Walid ibn Mazyad and Yahya ibn Hamzah said: on authority of al-Awzai, on authority of Yahya, on authority of Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf fell sick, and a relative visited him. And al-Firyabi said: on authority of al-Awzai, on authority of Yahya: a man came to Abd al-Rahman and he sent him. And Ikrimah ibn Ammar said: on authority of Yahya: a relative of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, on authority of Abd al-Rahman. And the companions of Yahya disagreed on it, and the best of them in statement on it is what Shayban and Aban said, and Allah knows best. I say: and Allah knows best, if al-Daraqutni, may Allah have mercy on him, had said: and the best of them in statement is Hisham, it would have been more fitting; for in the narration of Shayban and Aban, Ibrahim did not make clear to them who the informer was, while in the narration of Hisham he made clear that the informer was his father, and Allah knows best."
"850","Another 899 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Mattush informed us, with my recitation to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed you, recited to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me: on authority of Makhul, on authority of Kurayb, on authority of Ibn Abbas: that Umar said to him: O boy, have you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or from any of his companions: when a man doubts in his prayer, what should he do? He said: While he was thus, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came, and said: What are you discussing? So Umar said: I asked this boy whether he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or any of his companions, when a man doubts in his prayer, what should he do? So Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he prayed one or two, let him count it as one; and when he does not know whether he prayed two or three, let him count it as two; and when he does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him count it as three; then let him prostrate when he finishes his prayer while sitting, before he greets."
"851","900 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us that al-Husayn informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: my father narrated to us: on authority of Ibn Ishaq who said: Makhul narrated to me: on authority of Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, on authority of Ibn Abbas who said: I sat with Umar ibn al-Khattab and he said to me: O Ibn Abbas, have you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anything by which the Muslim man is commanded when he forgets in his prayer, how should he act? He said: So I said: No by Allah, and have you heard, O Commander of the Believers, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anything about that? He said: So he said: No by Allah. While we were thus, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came, and said: What are you discussing? He said: So Umar said to him: I asked him, and informed him of what he had asked him. So Abd al-Rahman said to him: But I have heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. So Umar said to him: Then you are with us trustworthy, what did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: So Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you forgets in his prayer until he does not know whether he added or decreased, then if he doubts between one and two, let him count it as one; and when he doubts between two and three, let him count it as two; and when he doubts between three and four, let him count it as three, until the doubt is toward addition; then he prostrates two prostrations while sitting before he greets, then he greets. Al-Tirmidhi reported it on authority of Ibn Bashshar, on authority of Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthman, on authority of Ibrahim ibn Sad with its chain, and said: a hasan sahih hadith. And Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Abu Yusuf Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqi, on authority of Muhammad ibn Salamah. And Ismail al-Makki reported it on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, on authority of Ibn Abbas."
"852","901 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us, recited to him in Baghdad, that Umar al-Bistami informed them, recited to him: Ahmad al-Khalili informed us: Ali al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Ismail al-Makki narrated to us: on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, on authority of Ibn Abbas who said: I was discussing something of prayer with Umar. He said: Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to us and said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: We said: Yes. He said: I bear the testimony of Allah that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you is in doubt of decrease in his prayer, let him pray until he is in doubt of increase."
"853","902 - And with it, al-Haytham informed us: Abu Hatim al-Razi Muhammad ibn Idris narrated to us: al-Ansari narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us: on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, on authority of Ibn Abbas who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him pray a rakah, then prostrate two prostrations. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it on authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on authority of Ismail ibn Muslim. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ibrahim ibn Sad and Muhammad ibn Salamah and Isa ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari and Talhah ibn Zayd reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on authority of Makhul, mursal, and thus Muhammad ibn Ishaq heard it from Makhul, mursal. And Ismail Ibn Ulayyah and Abd Allah ibn Numayr and Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, mursal. And on authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on authority of Husayn ibn Abd Allah, on authority of Makhul, on authority of Kurayb, on authority of Ibn Abbas, on authority of Abd al-Rahman: these three ضبطوا on authority of Ishaq both the mursal and the connected. And Ahmad ibn Hanbal reported it on authority of Muhammad ibn Yazid correctly, on authority of Ismail ibn Muslim, on authority of al-Zuhri, so the hadith returns to Ismail ibn Muslim, and Ismail is weak. In the Musnad of Imam Ahmad: Ismail narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Makhul narrated to me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays and doubts, and he mentioned it. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: And Husayn ibn Abd Allah said to me: Did he connect it for you? So I said: No. So he said: But he narrated to me that Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him, on authority of Ibn Abbas who said: I sat with Umar ibn al-Khattab and mentioned the hadith. I say: And Husayn ibn Abd Allah is spoken about."
"854","Another 903 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us: on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten are in Paradise: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, may Allah be pleased with them, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, and Sad is in Paradise, and Said is in Paradise, and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah is in Paradise. Imam Ahmad and al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasai all reported it on authority of Qutaybah ibn Said. And al-Tirmidhi also reported it on authority of Abu Musab al-Zuhri, on authority of al-Darawardi, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, on authority of his father, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar, and he did not mention Abd al-Rahman. And it is said: Umar ibn Said reported it on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, on authority of his father, on authority of Said ibn Zayd. Al-Bukhari said: And it is more correct."
"855","Another 904 - The hafiz, the imam Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Madini informed us in his book that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me: my father narrated to me: on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: My name in the pre-Islamic time was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abd al-Rahman. And Uqbah ibn Mukram reported it on authority of Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, on authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf."
"856","905 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed you: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to me: Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us: my father narrated to me: on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: My name was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abd al-Rahman. I say: Perhaps Yaqub heard it from both of them, and Allah knows best."
"857","Another 906 - The judge Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari, and Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Sufi in Baghdad, and Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib in the outskirts of Damascus - it was said to each one of them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzaz informed you, recited to him while you listened: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Kharaqi informed us: Abu Bakr Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Mustafad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid al-Qaysi narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Huddani narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said: We were at Arafat (H). 907 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Hudbah narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shayban informed us, he said: I was at Arafat, and I met Abu Salamah, so I said: Narrate to me something you heard from your father with no one between your father and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: My father narrated to me: on authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed Allah has obligated the fasting of Ramadan, and I have established its standing (in prayer). The wording of Abu Yala. And in the narration of Jafar al-Firyabi that he said: Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted, has obligated the fasting of Ramadan, and I have established for you its standing."
"858","908 - And Abu al-Hasan al-Umari and Abu Ahmad al-Sufi and Abu Hafs al-Muaddib informed us that Abu Bakr al-Bazzaz informed them, recited to him: Abu Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abu al-Qasim al-Kharaqi informed us: Abu Bakr al-Firyabi narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki al-Jarrah narrated to us: on authority of Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami: al-Nadr ibn Shayban narrated to us: on authority of Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, on authority of his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, on authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Indeed Allah the Exalted has obligated the fasting of the month of Ramadan, and I have established for you its standing, so whoever fasts and stands in faith and seeking reward exits his sins as on the day his mother bore him. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi reported it on authority of Nasr ibn Ali, on authority of al-Nadr. And Imam Ahmad reported it on authority of Surayj ibn al-Numan, on authority of Nuh ibn Qays, on authority of Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami, on authority of al-Nadr ibn Shayban al-Huddani. And on authority of Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, on authority of al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh reported it on authority of al-Fadl, on authority of Nasr ibn Ali. And al-Nasai reported it on authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on authority of al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, on authority of Nasr ibn Ali. And on authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on authority of al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, on authority of al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl. And on authority of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak al-Mukharrimi, on authority of Abi Hisham al-Makhzumi, on authority of al-Qasim, and he said: This is mistaken, and what is correct is the hadith of Abi Salamah on authority of Abi Hurayrah. And Ibn Majah reported it in Prayer on authority of Ali ibn Muhammad, on authority of Waki and Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, on authority of Nasr ibn Ali, and on authority of Yahya ibn Hakim, on authority of Abi Dawud, on authority of Nasr ibn Ali. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: al-Nadr ibn Shayban reports it on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of his father. Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami al-Akbar and Abu Aqil al-Dawraqi Bashir ibn Uqbah and al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Huddani narrated it, and al-Zuhri reported it on authority of Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on authority of Abi Hurayrah, and he did not mention in it: and I have established for the Muslims its standing; rather he mentioned in it the virtue of its fasting, and the hadith of al-Zuhri is closer to what is correct, and Allah knows best."
"859","909 - Abu Muhammad Yunus ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hashimi informed us in Egypt that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa ibn Shuayb informed them, recited to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad - Sarkhasi - narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi narrated to us: Abu Muhammad Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk informed me, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed me: on authority of Muslim ibn Jundub, on authority of Nawfal ibn Iyas al-Hudhali who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was a companion to us, and what an excellent companion. And one day he returned with us until he brought us into his house, and entered and bathed, then came out and sat, and we were brought a platter with bread and meat. When it was placed, Abd al-Rahman wept. So I said: O Abu Muhammad, what makes you weep? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and neither he nor the people of his house ever ate their fill of barley bread, so I do not see us kept after except for what is better for us. Al-Tirmidhi reported it in the Book of al-Shamail on authority of Abd ibn Humayd. The name of Ibn Abi Fudayk is Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Muslim ibn Abi Fudayk. And Ibn Abi Dhib is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"860","910 - And Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us, recited to him, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by ijazah, and it was said to him: Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed you, recited to him, he said: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, they both said: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu Amr ibn Hamdan narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sad narrated to us: Duhaym narrated to us - meaning on authority of Ibn Abi Fudayk - Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to me: on authority of Muslim ibn Jundub, on authority of Nawfal ibn Iyas al-Hudhali who said: Abd al-Rahman was a companion to us, and what an excellent companion. And one day he returned with us until we entered his house, and he entered and bathed, then came out and sat with us, and we were brought a platter with bread and meat. When it was placed, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf wept. So we said to him: O Abu Muhammad, what makes you weep? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and neither he nor the people of his house ever ate their fill of barley bread, and I do not see us kept after except for what is better for us. In our hearing it was: Duhaym ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us - and Duhaym is Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim - and ana or na or an dropped."
"861","Another 911 - Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us in Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzaz informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Kharaqi informed us: Abu Bakr Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Firyabi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us: on authority of Ibn Shihab, on authority of Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The fasting person on a journey is like the one who breaks fast at home."
"862","912 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Asbahani informed us there that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim al-Nabil informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami and Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to me, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us - and what is correct is Abd Allah ibn Musa - on authority of Usamah ibn Zayd, on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One fasting Ramadan on a journey is like one breaking fast at home. Ibn Majah reported it on authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir, on authority of Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yunus ibn Yazid reported it from the narration of al-Qasim ibn Mabur on his authority, and Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi, and Uqayl ibn Khalid from the narration of Salamah on his authority, and Yazid ibn Iyad, on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on authority of his father, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Ibn Abi Dhib reported it on authority of al-Zuhri, and there is disagreement on his authority: Man ibn Isa and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri and Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat and others reported it on authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of his father, halted (mawquf). And Abu Muawiyah al-Darir opposed them, reporting it on authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, on authority of his father, halted. And what is correct is on authority of Abi Salamah, on authority of his father, halted."
"863","Another 913 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi informed them, recited to him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ziyad ibn Khalid al-Mawsili narrated to us (H). 914 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, they said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us: my uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us: on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him when they finished tawaf, and said: O Abu Muhammad, what did you do about touching the Corner? So he said: I touched and left. So he said: You did right. The wording of Ibn Sadaqah. And in the narration of al-Mawsili he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me when we finished tawaf of the House: How did you act, O Abu Muhammad? I said: I touched and left. He said: You did right. Abu Hatim al-Busti reported it on authority of al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Mashar al-Harrani, on authority of Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala, on authority of Bishr ibn al-Sari, on authority of al-Thawri, on authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me ... the hadith. Al-Tabarani said: None reported this hadith on authority of Abd Allah ibn Umar except al-Qasim ibn Yahya; Muqaddam alone reported it. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Bishr ibn al-Sari and Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ata al-Wasiti reported it on authority of his uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya, on authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar. Muhammad ibn Fudayl and al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani followed them both, reporting it on authority of Hisham, on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman. And Mutamir said: on authority of Ubayd Allah, on authority of Hisham, on authority of his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd al-Rahman. And likewise it was said on authority of Ibn Fudayl, mursal. And likewise Zuhayr said on authority of Hisham, on authority of his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd al-Rahman. And Ibn Wahb said: on authority of Malik and Said ibn Abd al-Rahman and Amr ibn al-Harith and others, on authority of Hisham, on authority of his father, mursal. And Hammad ibn Zayd said: A companion of mine narrated to us on authority of Hisham, and mentioned it mursal as well, and it is what is preserved."
"864","Another 915 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, on authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I witnessed the alliance of al-Mutayyabin with my uncles while I was a boy, and I would not wish red camels in exchange for breaking it. Al-Zuhri said: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam did not meet an alliance except that it strengthened it, and there is no alliance in Islam, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar."
"865","916 - And Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Ismail Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us: on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I witnessed as a boy with my uncles the alliance of al-Mutayyabin, and I would not wish red camels in exchange for breaking it. Imam Ahmad reported it on authority of Ismail. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban reported it on authority of al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, on authority of Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq."
"866","917 - Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Salam informed us in Baghdad that Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Abnawi informed them, recited to him: Ismail ibn Masadah al-Ismaili informed us: Hamzah ibn Yusuf al-Sahmi informed us: Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz say: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh say: I came to Egypt, and I came to Ahmad ibn Salih, so he asked me: Where are you from? I said: From Baghdad. He said: Where is your home from the home of Ahmad ibn Hanbal? I said: I am among his companions. He said: Write for me the location of your home, for I intend to come to Iraq so that you may bring me together with Ahmad ibn Hanbal. So I wrote for him. Then Ahmad ibn Salih came to us in the year twelve to Affan, and asked about me and met me, and said: The appointment between me and you. So I took him to Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and sought permission for him, and said: Ahmad ibn Salih. He said: Ibn al-Tabari? I said: Yes. So he gave him permission. So he stood to him and welcomed him and brought him near, and said to him: It has reached me that you have collected the hadith of al-Zuhri, so come that we may recall what al-Zuhri reported on authority of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they recalled together and neither brought something unknown to the other until they finished, and I never saw better than their recalling together. Then Ahmad ibn Hanbal said to Ahmad ibn Salih: Come that we may recall what al-Zuhri reported on authority of the children of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they recalled together and neither brought something unknown to the other, until Ahmad ibn Hanbal said to Ahmad ibn Salih: With you is al-Zuhri on authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on authority of his father, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I witnessed the alliance of al-Mutayyabin with my uncles - and the rest of the hadith. So Ahmad ibn Salih said: Yes. So Ahmad ibn Hanbal wrote it from him. smiling and saying: A reliable man, Abu Salih Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, reported it on authority of al-Zuhri. So he said: Who reported it on authority of Abd al-Rahman? So he said: Two trustworthy men narrated it to me: Ismail Ibn Ulayyah and Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal. So Ahmad ibn Salih said to Ahmad ibn Hanbal: I ask you by Allah but that you dictate it to me. So Ahmad said: From the book. So he stood and entered and brought out the book and dictated it to him. So Ahmad ibn Salih said: If I had not benefited in Iraq except this hadith it would be much. Then he bade him farewell and left. And Khalid reported it on authority of Abd al-Rahman."
"867","918 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn informed them, recited to him: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Wahb - he is Ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti - narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: on authority of Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Ishaq - on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I witnessed while a boy an alliance with my uncles, al-Mutayyabin, and I would not wish red camels in exchange for breaking it. Jubayr is not mentioned in this narration. And Abu Yala reported it on authority of Abbas al-Narsi, on authority of Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal. And on authority of Abi Khaythamah, on authority of Ismail Ibn Ulayyah, as the narration of Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ahmad ibn Mani, with the mention of Jubayr. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq reports it on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr, on authority of his father. Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and Ismail and Ibrahim ibn Tahman and Kharijah ibn Musab and Khalid al-Wasiti narrated it. And there is disagreement on his authority: it is said: on his authority, on authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr, on authority of Abd al-Rahman - and his father Jubayr is not mentioned."
"868","919 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah informed us: on authority of Urwah: that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me and Umar ibn al-Khattab such-and-such land as a grant. So al-Zubayr went to the family of Umar and bought their share from them. Then he came to Uthman ibn Affan and said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf claims that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him and Umar ibn al-Khattab such-and-such land, and I have bought the share of the family of Umar. So Uthman said: Abd al-Rahman is acceptable in testimony for him and against him."
"869","Another 920 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us, recited to him, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by ijazah (H). 921 - And it was said to our shaykh: Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed you, recited to him: Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, they both said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir al-Tai narrated to us: Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us: on authority of his father, on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: We were tested with hardship and we were patient, and we were tested with prosperity and we were not patient. And Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman did not hear this hadith from his father, rather he heard it from a man on his authority."
"870","922 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi informed us that Umar al-Bistami informed them: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Ziyad narrated to us in Baghdad: Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abdullah - he is Ibn al-Mubarak - informed us: Yunus ibn Yazid informed us: on authority of al-Zuhri: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed me: that he came as a delegate upon Muawiyah in his caliphate. He said: So I entered the enclosure, and greeted a gathering of the people of al-Sham, then sat among them. A man of them said to me: Who are you, O youth? He said: I am Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. He said: May Allah have mercy on your father. He informed me, he said: So-and-so informed me - naming a man - that he said: By Allah, I shall join the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and renew my contact with them, and speak to them. He said: So I came to Medina in the caliphate of Uthman and met them except Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. I was informed that he was at a land of his at al-Jurf. So I rode to him until I came to him, and he was placing his cloak aside, turning water with a shovel in his hand. When he saw me he was shy of me, so he threw the shovel and took his cloak. So I greeted him and said to him: I have come for a matter, and I have seen something more astonishing than it. Has there come to you except what came to us? And did you know except what we knew? So Abd al-Rahman said: Nothing came to us except what came to you, and we knew only what you knew. He said: So I said: Why do we renounce the world while you desire it? And we are light for jihad besides us, while you are our predecessors and our best and the companions of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Abd al-Rahman said: Nothing came to us except what came to you, and we knew only what you knew, but we were tested with hardship and were patient, and we were tested with prosperity and were not patient. Al-Tirmidhi reported this hadith from the narration of Yunus, on authority of al-Zuhri, on authority of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, on authority of his father."
"871","923 - Al-Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak ibn Mahmud informed us in Baghdad, that Abu al-Fath Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Sahl al-Karukhi informed them, reading to him. 924 - And Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja al-Wa'iz informed us in the street between Cairo and Misr, it was said to him: Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed you, reading to him. Both said: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Azdi informed us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jarrah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub informed us, Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi informed us, Qutaybah narrated to us, Abu Safwan narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: We were tested along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with hardship and we were patient, then we were tested with ease and we were not patient. Abu Isa said: This hadith is hasan. Abu Safwan's name is Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan al-Qurashi al-Umawi, from the men of the Sahih."
"872","Another, 925 - My uncle, the Imam, the learned Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi informed us, reading to him, that Abu Zur'ah Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir al-Maqdisi informed them, reading to him in Baghdad, Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Muqawwimi informed us, al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us, Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah al-Qattan informed us, Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa al-Himsi narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrates it and is alone with it, from Anas ibn Ayyash, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, and he erred in it; rather Muhammad ibn Amr narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi as mursal."
"873","Another, 926 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah informed us, my father narrated to me, Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out heading toward his charity land, and entered, faced the qiblah and fell prostrate, and prolonged the prostration until I thought Allah, mighty and majestic, had taken his soul in it, so I drew near to him then sat, and he raised his head and said: Who is this? I said: Abd al-Rahman. He said: What is the matter with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, you prostrated a prostration and I feared Allah, mighty and majestic, had taken your soul in it. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and gave me glad tidings, and said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you, I send peace upon him, so I prostrated to Allah, mighty and majestic, in gratitude."
"874","927 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us. 928 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad also informed us, that Abu Adnan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Nizar informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman - informed us. Both said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Hawti Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abd al-Wahid - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf - from his father, from his grandfather who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate a prostration and prolong it, then he raised his head, so I asked him about that and he said: Jibril met me and said: Whoever sends blessings upon you, Allah sends blessings upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you, Allah sends peace upon him. He said: I think he said ten. He said: So I prostrated to Allah in gratitude. In this narration it is from the narration of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father, and in the narration of Imam Ahmad from the narration of Abd al-Wahid from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman."
"875","929 - With this chain, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abi al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden, and I was following him, and he said: Jibril met me and said: I give you glad tidings that Allah says: Whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you, I send peace upon him."
"876","930 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us in al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Salamah Mansur ibn Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abi al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and I followed him until he entered palm trees, and he prostrated and prolonged the prostration until I feared that Allah had caused him to die or taken him. He said: So I came to look, and he raised his head and said: What is the matter with you, O Abd al-Rahman? He said: So I mentioned that to him. He said: Then he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Shall I not give you glad tidings that Allah, mighty and majestic, says to you: Whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you, I send peace upon him."
"877","931 - With it, my father narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, from Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: I entered the mosque and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) coming out of the mosque, so I followed him, and he mentioned the hadith."
"878","932 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Qutaybah informed us, Harmalah ibn Yahya al-Tujibi informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, that Abu al-Zubayr narrated to him, from Suhayl ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them one day with cheerfulness on his face, and said: Jibril came to me and said: Shall I not give you glad tidings, O Muhammad, of what Allah has given you from your ummah, and what He has given your ummah from you? Whoever among them sends one blessing upon you, Allah sends blessings upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you, Allah sends peace upon him. Al-Hakim narrated it in al-Mustadrak, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Sha'rani, from his grandfather, from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, like the narration of Imam Ahmad. Al-Daraqutni was asked about the hadith of Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prolonged his prostration ... the hadith, and he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrates it from Abd al-Wahid, and there is disagreement from him: Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam and al-Darawardi narrated it from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Sulayman ibn Bilal differed from them, narrating it from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Abd al-Wahid, adding Asim in its chain; and al-Himmani narrated it, making it from Abd al-Wahid, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and that is not preserved; and the correct view is the saying of Sa'id ibn Salamah and al-Darawardi. With Amr ibn Abi Amr therein is another chain: al-Layth narrates it from Ibn al-Had from Amr from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Huwayrith from Muhammad ibn Jubayr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki narrated it with disagreement from him: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated it from Abi al-Zubayr from Suhayl ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf; Ishaq ibn Abi Farwah differed, narrating it from Abi al-Zubayr from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father. I say: Al-Daraqutni's saying has shown that the narration of Ibn [...] from al-Darawardi Abd al-Aziz which we presented, the saying of Abd al-Wahid from his father from his grandfather, erred in his saying from his father. In al-Tusi's narration from Abi Salamah al-Khuza'i from Layth from Yazid ibn Abi Habib is also error; it is only Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, by proof of Imam Ahmad's narration and al-Daraqutni's saying also. And Allah knows best."
"879","933 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the voice of Ibn al-Mughtarif, or Ibn al-Gharif the camel-driver in the middle of the night, while we were heading to Makkah, so Umar urged his mount until he joined the people, and he was with Abd al-Rahman; when dawn broke Umar said: Now be quiet, now dawn has broken, remember Allah. He said: Then he saw Abd al-Rahman wearing leather socks, and said: Two socks? He said: I wore them with one better than you, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar said: I adjure you to remove them, for I fear people will look at you and follow you."
"880","934 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that a group of Arabs came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah and embraced Islam, then Madinah's fever epidemic befell them, so they relapsed and left Madinah; a group of his Companions - meaning the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - met them and said to them: Why have you returned? They said: Madinah's epidemic befell us and we disliked Madinah. They said: Do you not have in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an example? Some said: They became hypocrites, and some said: They did not become hypocrites, they are Muslims, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: What is the matter with you that you are two groups concerning the hypocrites, while Allah has overthrown them for what they earned, the verse."
"881","Another, 935 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, reading to her, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to me, my uncle al-Harith ibn al-Dahhak narrated to me, Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrating from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which part of the night is most heard? He said: The last middle of the night, then prayer is accepted until you pray Fajr, then there is no prayer until the sun is a spear's length or two spears high, then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands at a spear's length, then there is no prayer until the sun declines, then prayer is accepted until the sun is a spear's length or two, then there is no prayer until the sun sets. He said: Then he said: Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, he is his ransom from the Fire, requited limb for limb; and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, she is her ransom from the Fire, requited limb for limb; and any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women, they are his ransom from the Fire, requited two limbs of them for one of him. Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn al-Dahhak ibn Muhajir ibn Zurayq Abu Ishaq al-Himsi: Abu Hatim al-Razi was asked about him and said: Truthful. And his uncle al-Harith: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim did not mention him in his book."
"882","Another, 936 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, reading to him in Isfahan, it was said: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, reading to him, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ja'far ibn al-Fadl al-Mukharrimi al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Shaybah al-Hizami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Ala ibn Husayn al-Nabaqi al-Muttalibi narrated to me, he said: al-Walid ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: Umamah bint Abi al-As was in the throes of death, so Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My daughter is in her death throes. So he sent to his daughter: To Allah belongs what He takes and to Allah belongs what remains. She was in throes a second time, and she sent to him that my daughter is in throes, so he sent to his daughter: To Allah belongs what He takes and to Allah belongs what remains. Then it was the third time, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her, and she brought the child out to him, and her soul was rattling in her chest, and with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were some of his Companions, and his eyes shed tears until he grasped his beard, and they noticed while looking at him, and he said: Why are you looking? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you moved to tears. He said: A mercy which Allah, mighty and majestic, places wherever He wills, and Allah only has mercy on the merciful among His servants. Muhammad ibn al-Ala ibn Husayn and al-Walid ibn Ibrahim: I did not see them mentioned in al-Bukhari's history nor the book of Ibn Abi Hatim; and this hadith has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Usamah ibn Zayd: The daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to him that my son is dying. So witness us. In Hajjaj's narration from Shu'bah: My daughter has been attended, so he sent greetings of peace, saying: To Allah belongs what He takes, and His is what He gives, and everything with Him is for an appointed term, so let her be patient and reckon; and he mentioned the rest, its end: Allah only has mercy on the merciful among His servants."
"883","Musnad of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Ishaq Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas Malik ibn Uhayb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah ibn Kilab al-Zuhri, may Allah be pleased with him. Buraydah ibn al-Husayb al-Aslami, a Companion, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with them both. 937 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather who said: Buraydah mentioned that when Mu'awiyah camped at Dhi Tuwa, Sa'd came and seated him on his couch, and Sa'd said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master."
"884","Busr ibn Sa'id al-Hadrami al-Madani, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 938 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id: That Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said at the time of Uthman's tribulation: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a tribulation; the one sitting in it is better than the standing, the standing better than the walking, and the walking better than the running. He said: What do you think, if he enters upon me in my house and stretches his hand to me to kill me? He said: Be like the son of Adam. Imam Ahmad and al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, and al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan hadith. Some narrated this hadith from Layth ibn Sa'd, adding a man in this chain. The man is Husayn al-Ashja'i, who comes later."
"885","Bakr ibn Qirwash al-Kufi, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him. 939 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim and A'ishah bint Ma'mar informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abi al-Abbas: He heard Aba al-Tufayl narrating from Bakr ibn Qirwash, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Dhu al-Thudayyah and said: A devil of the hollow, a herder of horses, a man from Bajilah called al-Ashhab, or Ibn al-Ashhab, pursues him, a sign among an unjust people. Sufyan said: Ammar al-Duhni informed me, he said: A man of ours - meaning from Bajilah - called al-Ashhab or Ibn al-Ashhab pursued him. It was said: al-Radhah is the hollow in the mountain."
"886","940 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Ala - meaning Ibn al-Abbas - from Abi al-Tufayl, from Bakr ibn Qirwash, from Sa'd; it was said to Sufyan: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: The devil of the hollow pursues him, meaning a man from Bajilah."
"887","941 - And al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abi al-Abbas, from Abi al-Tufayl, from Bakr ibn Qirwash, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned Dhu al-Thudayyah, saying: A devil of a hollow, pursued by a man from Bajilah called al-Ashhab or Ibn al-Ashhab, a sign among an unjust people. Al-Bukhari said in his history: al-Ala ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Sha'ir al-Makki, freedman of Banu al-Dayl, heard Aba al-Tufayl and Aba Ja'far; al-Thawri, Ibn Jurayj and Ibn Uyaynah narrated from him, and Ibn Uyaynah used to praise him. And Bakr ibn Qirwash: Abu al-Tufayl heard from him. Ali said to me: I heard of his mention only in this, and the hadith of Qatadah. Ali said: What can be said of Abu Bakr ibn Qirwash. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it, saying: The correct view is the first saying, meaning the narration of al-Ala ibn Abi al-Abbas from Abi al-Tufayl from Bakr. Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ashja'i, and it is said Husayl, and it is said Abd al-Rahman ibn Husayn."
"888","942 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us at Dar al-Qazz in Baghdad, that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Hafiz informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far al-Hashimi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Yazid ibn Khalid al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Ayyash, from Bukayr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ashja'i that he heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning this hadith, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if he enters upon me in my house and stretches his hand to kill me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be like the two sons of Adam, and Yazid recited: If you stretch your hand to me, the verse. Al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it from Ayyash without mentioning Husayn, and it has preceded thus. Abu Dawud narrated it after the hadith of Busr ibn Sa'id. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it, saying: The hadith of Mufaddal ibn Fadalah is closest to correct, meaning this narration. And Allah knows best."
"889","Dinar Abu Abd Allah al-Qarrazz, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 943 - Al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah - meaning Ibn Zayd - narrated to us. 944 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu Abd Allah al-Qarrazz narrated to us, that he heard Sa'd ibn Malik and Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless the people of Madinah in their city, bless them in their sa' and bless them in their mudd. O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and intimate friend, and I am Your servant and Messenger; Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah, and I ask You for the people of Madinah the like of what Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah and the like of it with it. Madinah is fortified with angels; at every pass of it are two angels guarding it; neither plague nor the Dajjal shall enter it. Whoever intends it with evil, Allah melts him as salt melts in water. The wording is one, except that in Imam Ahmad's narration: guarding it in the dual. This hadith Muslim narrated in his Sahih: Whoever intends it with evil, to its end, from the hadith of Zayd ibn Aslam from al-Qarrazz from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas only. And he narrated the like from the hadith of Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, without mention of plague and Dajjal, and the mention of Dajjal and plague from the hadith of Nu'aym ibn Abd Allah from Abu Hurayrah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Umar ibn Nubayh narrates it from Abi Abd Allah al-Qarrazz from Sa'd. Muhammad ibn Musa al-Madani narrated it from Abi Abd Allah al-Qarrazz from Abu Hurayrah. Usamah ibn Zayd narrated it from al-Qarrazz from Sa'd and Abu Hurayrah; all the sayings are thus correct. And Allah knows best."
"890","Another, 945 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud - meaning al-Hashimi - narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abi Abd Allah al-Qarrazz, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque. And it was narrated from Umar ibn al-Hakam from Sa'd."
"891","946 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Abi al-Zinad - informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abi Abd Allah al-Qarrazz, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque. This hadith has a witness in Sahih Muslim, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah."
"892","Dhakwan al-Samman Abu Salih al-Madani, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 947 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abi Salih, from Sa'd who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was supplicating with two fingers, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make it one, make it one, and pointed with the index finger. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abi Mu'awiyah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abi Khaythamah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Mukharrimi from Abi Mu'awiyah. Al-Hakim narrated it in al-Mustadrak from Ibrahim ibn Ismah ibn Ibrahim, from Yahya, from Yahya, from Abi Mu'awiyah, and said: It is authentic on their condition if Abu Salih al-Samman heard from Sa'd. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it, saying: The saying of Abu Mu'awiyah is closest to correct, meaning this narration."
"893","Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith al-Jurashi, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 948 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ibn Kasib narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Rabi'ah - he is Ibn al-Harith al-Jurashi - who said: Ali was mentioned before Mu'awiyah while Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas was with him, and Sa'd said to him: Is Ali mentioned in your presence? He has four virtues; that one of them be mine is dearer to me than such and such! He mentioned red camels, his saying: I shall give the banner, his saying: In the position of Harun to Musa, his saying: Whomsoever I am his master, and Sufyan forgot the fourth. Mentioned in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Bukayr ibn Mismar from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father: I shall give the banner, and his saying: Harun to Musa."
"894","Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah al-Thaqafi, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 949 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that al-Mukhtar ibn Abd al-Hamid informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from Sa'd who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the pledge of the women, a woman stood up to him as if from the women of Mudar, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a burden on our fathers, sons and husbands, so what is lawful for us of their wealth? He said: The fresh that you eat and give as gifts. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sawwar al-Misri from Abd al-Salam. Abu Zur'ah and Abu Hatim said: Ziyad ibn Jubayr from Sa'd is mursal. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrates it from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, and there is disagreement from him: al-Thawri narrated it from Ziyad from Sa'd; Hushaym made it mursal from Yunus from Ziyad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sa'd over charity ... the hadith. And it is said: This Sa'd is a man of the Ansar, not Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, and that is more correct, Allah willing."
"895","Zayd ibn Aslam, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 950 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz - meaning al-Darawardi - narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until a people come out who eat with their tongues as cows eat with their tongues. Abu Zur'ah said: Zayd ibn Aslam from Sa'd is mursal."
"896","Zayd ibn Ayyash, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 951 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Tusi informed them, reading to him, Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Buhturi informed us, Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Musa al-Sarakhsi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad al-Hashimi informed us, Abu Mus'ab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri al-Madani narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, that Zayd Abu Ayyash informed him, that he asked Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas about white wheat for sult, saying which is better? He said: The white, then he forbade him that, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about buying dates for fresh dates, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does the fresh decrease when it dries? They said: Yes, so he forbade that."
"897","952 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abi Ayyash who said: Sa'd was asked about selling sult for barley or something of this, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about dates for fresh dates, and said: Does the fresh decrease when it dries? They said: Yes. He said: Then no, in that case."
"898","953 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Isbahani informed us there, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah informed us, Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid that Abu Ayyash informed him, that he heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fresh dates for dry dates on credit."
"899","954 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad, that Zayd Abu Ayyash informed him, that he asked Sa'd about white wheat - meaning for sult - Sa'd said to him: Which of them is better? He said: The white, so he forbade him that, and Sa'd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about buying dates for fresh dates, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does the fresh decrease when it dries? They said: Yes, so he forbade that. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Numayr and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Malik. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated it from al-Qa'nabi from Malik, and from al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' from Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam likewise. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah from Malik and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad from Waki' and Ishaq ibn Sulayman from Malik likewise. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr ibn Ali from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Malik, and from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi from Sufyan from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, and from Harun ibn Abd Allah from Ma'n from Malik likewise. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Idris from Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri from Malik."
"900","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib ibn Hazn, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 955 - Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us. 956 - And Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi and Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd who said: We used to lease land in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for what was on the water channels of crops, and what was watered by water of it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that, and permitted us to lease it for gold and silver. This is the wording of Ibn Mani'. And in Imam Ahmad's narration: and what was watered by water of it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that and permitted us. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun."
"901","957 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Muhammad ibn Ikrimah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: That the owners of farms in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lease their farms for what would be on the water carrier of crops, and what was watered by water around the well, so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing over some of that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to lease for that, and said: Lease for gold and silver. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Yazid ibn Harun. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from his uncle from his father Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Yazid ibn Harun."
"902","Another, 958 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, that al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq narrated to him, that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated of the hadith of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: No hamah, no contagion and no tiyarah; if there is anything in tiyarah, it is in the woman, the horse and the house. And he used to say: If plague is in a land, do not descend upon it, and if it is in a land and you are in it, do not flee from it."
"903","959 - With it, Abu Ya'la informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Amir - he is al-Aqadi - narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Hadrami, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: I asked Sa'd about tiyarah and he rebuked me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No contagion and no tiyarah; if tiyarah is in anything, it is in the horse, the woman and the house."
"904","960 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Malik: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No hamah, no contagion and no tiyarah; if it is, it is in the woman, the horse and the house."
"905","961 - And Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: I asked Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas about tiyarah and he became angry and rebuked me, saying: Who narrated to you? I disliked telling him who narrated to me, so Sa'd said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No contagion, no tiyarah and no hamah; if tiyarah is in anything, it is in the horse, the woman and the house. Imam Ahmad brought it in full from Isma'il from Hisham from Yahya from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Isma'il from Aban ibn Yazid, without mention of plague. The mention of plague is mentioned in Sahih Muslim. Ibn Hibban narrated it from Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi' from Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Hammal from Isa ibn Yunus from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Yahya from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it from Abi Qilabah al-Raqashi from Abi Amir al-Aqadi, Wahb ibn Jarir, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith and Hafs ibn Umar, all from Hisham from Yahya from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq from Sa'id. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated it from Hisham from Yahya from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Sa'd, and Mu'adh ibn Hisham and Muhammad ibn Abi Adi differed from him, narrating it from Hisham from Yahya from al-Hadrami from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Sa'd; and the saying of these two is more correct. It is the correct view. This hadith has a witness in the two Sahihs from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar from his father."
"906","Another, 962 - Abu Shuja' Muhammad ibn al-Maqrun al-Muqri informed us in Baghdad that al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Daqqaq informed us, Abd Allah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abi Suhayl ibn Malik, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Baqi' al-Khayl, and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib came forward, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is al-Abbas, the uncle of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most joining of kin."
"907","963 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, and Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan in Naysabur, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, reading to him, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us, al-Hakim Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hafiz informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Uthman al-Uthmani narrated to us in Baghdad, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, Abu Suhayl Nafi' ibn Malik narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most joining of kin."
"908","964 - And Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari and others informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him, Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, Abu Suhayl ibn Malik - meaning the uncle of Malik ibn Anas - narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out preparing an army and looked at the people, and there was al-Abbas, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is al-Abbas, the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most joining of kin. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it from Ali ibn al-Madini. Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Humayd ibn Makhlad al-Nasa'i from Ali ibn al-Madini. Abu Hatim al-Razi said, when asked about Muhammad ibn Talhah: His place is truthfulness; his hadith is written but not used as proof. He mentioned nothing besides that. Abu Bakr al-Shafi'i also narrated it from Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Ibrahim ibn Hamzah and Ali ibn al-Madini, and from Zayd ibn Akhzam, from Ishaq ibn Idris, and from Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar from Muhammad ibn Khallad, all from Muhammad ibn Talhah likewise."
"909","Another, 965 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us, that Umar al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Ibn Kasib narrated to us from dictation, Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, he said: I said to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: Here is a handsome man claiming to be of your people. He said: Is he known? I said: No. He said: I heard Sa'd say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever claims something not of him, Allah strips him as leaves are stripped. Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'dah: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He narrated from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Ya'qub ibn Utbah; Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani and Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Umawi narrated from him, and he mentioned no criticism of him."
"910","Shurayh ibn Ubayd Abu al-Salt al-Hadrami al-Himsi, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 966 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Hafiz informed us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far al-Hashimi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to me, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I hope my ummah will not fail before its Lord in that it be delayed half a day. It was said to Sa'd: How much is half that day? He said: Five hundred years. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan."
"911","Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah ibn al-Majishun, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 967 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Abu Ali al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah, that Sa'd heard a man saying: Labbayk, Possessor of the Ascensions, and said: He is indeed the Possessor of Ascensions, but we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not say that."
"912","968 - And al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan who said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me, that Sa'd ibn Malik heard a man saying: Labbayk, Possessor of Ascensions. He said: Allah is the Possessor of Ascensions, but we did not say that with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Zur'ah said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah from Sa'd is mursal. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrates it from Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah, and there is disagreement from him: al-Qasim ibn Ma'n, Yahya al-Qattan, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar and al-Thawri narrated it from Ibn Ajlan from Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah from Sa'd; al-Darawardi differed from them, narrating it from Ibn Ajlan from Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah from Amir ibn Sa'd from Sa'd, and al-Darawardi was not followed on Amir. And it was narrated from al-Thawri from Ibn Ajlan from Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah: Sa'd heard a man saying: I seek refuge with You from its Zaqqum and its chains, and said: We did not supplicate thus in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated it from al-Thawri, and I think he erred in it; the correct with this chain is: Labbayk, Possessor of Ascensions. And Allah knows best."
"913","Ubayd Allah, and it is said Abd Allah ibn Abi Nuhayk, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 969 - Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid informed us in Isfahan, that his grandfather Ghanim ibn Khalid informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab and Isa ibn Hammad Zughbah narrated to us, both said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Nuhayk, from Sa'id or Sa'd, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an. Zughbah said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Nuhayk."
"914","970 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim and A'ishah bint Ma'mar informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Nuhayk who said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas met me and said: Who are you? So I traced my lineage to him and he knew me, while I was coming from the market, and said: Merchants are earners, merchants are earners; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an. Sufyan said: Meaning he finds sufficiency in it."
"915","971 - Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Nuhayk, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hajjaj and Abi al-Nadr from al-Layth from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Abd Allah ibn Abi Nuhayk. Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated it from Abi al-Nadr from al-Layth from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ibn Abi Nuhayk without naming him. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Sufyan from Amr ibn Dinar like Imam Ahmad's narration. Imam Ahmad and Ishaq also narrated it from Waki' from Sa'id ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Nuhayk. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abi al-Walid al-Tayalisi, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id and Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Mawhab al-Ramli, and from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Sufyan from Amr. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Amr ibn Dinar, Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj, Sa'id ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi al-Makki, Husam ibn Misakk, Umar ibn Qays and al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ibn Abi Nuhayk from Sa'd; and there is disagreement from al-Layth in mentioning Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: as for the strangers from al-Layth they narrated it correctly from Sa'd, while the Egyptians narrated it saying: from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id in place of Sa'd, and some said: from Sa'id or from Sa'd; and Qutaybah said: from al-Layth from a man, naming neither Sa'd nor another. He mentioned much disagreement therein, saying: The correct is the saying of Amr ibn Dinar and Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Abi Nuhayk from Sa'd."
"916","Narration of Amir ibn Sa'd from his father. 972 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, that Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, reading to him, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib informed us, Abu Umar al-Qasim ibn Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to me, from Ibn Uthman. Abu Dawud said: He is Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Uthman, from Ash'ath ibn Ishaq ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Makkah intending Madinah, and when we were near Azwara he dismounted, then raised his hands and supplicated Allah for a while, then fell prostrate and remained long, then stood and raised his hands and supplicated Allah for a while, then fell prostrate; Ahmad mentioned three times. He said: I asked my Lord and interceded for my ummah, and He gave me a third of my ummah, so I fell prostrate in gratitude to my Lord; then I raised my head and asked my Lord for my ummah and He gave me a third of my ummah, so I fell prostrate to my Lord in gratitude; then I raised my head and asked my Lord for my ummah and He gave me the last third, so I fell prostrate to my Lord. Abu Dawud said: Ahmad ibn Salih dropped Ash'ath ibn Ishaq when he narrated it to us; Musa ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated it to me from him. Thus Abu Dawud brought it in his Sunan."
"917","Another, 973 - The Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja al-Wa'iz informed us in the street between Misr and Cairo, that Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur al-Harawi informed them, reading to him, Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim al-Azdi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Jarrahi informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub informed us, Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad informed us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded placing the hands and erecting the feet."
"918","974 - Abd Allah said: Mu'alla said: Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sa'd: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded placing the hands: and he mentioned the like, without mentioning from his father. Abu Isa said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan and more than one narrated from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sa'd: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded placing the hands and erecting the feet, as mursal, and this is more correct than Wuhayb's hadith. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated it, and there is disagreement from Wuhayb also: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak and Mu'alla ibn Asad said: from Wuhayb, from Ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father; and likewise said Surayj ibn Yunus from Abi Khalid al-Ahmar from Ibn Ajlan. Affan narrated it from Wuhayb from Ibn Ajlan from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Amir ibn Sa'd as mursal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), without saying from his father. Likewise said al-Ashajj from Abi Khalid from Ibn Ajlan. Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Samarqandi - a well-known trustworthy - narrated it from Mu'alla ibn Asad from Wuhayb from Ibn Ajlan from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father. Hamdan ibn Umar said: from Mu'alla from Wuhayb from Ibn Ajlan from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim and Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, combining them, and narrated it with chain from Sa'd. Al-Darawardi, Abu Damrah and Ali ibn Ghurab narrated it from Ibn Ajlan from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Amir ibn Sa'd as mursal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Thawri narrated it from Ibn Ajlan from Bukayr from Amir ibn Sa'd as mursal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also; the mursal is closer."
"919","Another, 975 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abi al-Fath informed us in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sa'id ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir informed us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I forbid you a little of what intoxicates in large amount. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman from Muhammad ibn Ja'far."
"920","976 - And Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us in Baghdad, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them, reading to him, Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Bazzaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Daqqaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq - he is Ibn Buhlul - narrated to us, Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Bukayr al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I forbid you a little of what intoxicates in large amount. Imam Ahmad narrated it in the Book of Drinks from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi from al-Dahhak."
"921","977 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Kathir al-Madani narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbid you a little of what intoxicates in large amount. Likewise narrated the judge Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim from Abi Sa'id al-Ashajj. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Humayd ibn Makhlad from Sa'id ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam, and from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ammar al-Mawsili from al-Walid ibn Kathir. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Qahtabah from Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad from al-Dahhak. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrates it from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father; a group narrated it thus, among them Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim, al-Darawardi, al-Walid ibn Kathir Abu Sa'id, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir. Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi and Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated it from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman from Bukayr from Amir ibn Sa'd as mursal, not mentioning Sa'd therein; and the correct is the hadith of Amir ibn Sa'd from his father."
"922","Another, 978 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us with my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed you, reading to him while you were present, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ibn Kasib narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn A'idh, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father: That a man came to prayer while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with them, and when he reached the row he said: Give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the speaker? The man said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then your sins will be forgiven and you will be martyred in the way of Allah. Thus in this narration; and the well-known is: Your horse will be hamstrung."
"923","979 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim and A'ishah bint Ma'mar informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn A'idh, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to prayer while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with us, and said when he reached the row: O Allah, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer he said: Who is the speaker just now? The man said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the way of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"924","980 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah ibn Mus'ab ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Ibn A'idh, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd who said: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with us, and said: O Allah, give me the best of what You give the righteous. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished he said: Who is the speaker just now? The man said: I am. He said: Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be killed in the way of Allah."
"925","981 - Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus, that Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Maliki informed them, reading to him, it was said to him: The judge al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rida al-Antaki informed you, reading to him, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Jazlan narrated to us, Abu Zur'ah - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr - narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn A'idh, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that a man came to prayer while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with us, and said when he reached the row: O Allah, give me the best of what You have given Your righteous servants. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished he said: Who is the speaker just now? He said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the way of Allah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in the Book of Day and Night from Muhammad ibn Nasr from Ibrahim ibn Hamzah from Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Abdah from Abd al-Aziz. Ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah from Ahmad ibn Abdah from al-Darawardi. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrates it from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn A'idh from Amir ibn Sa'd; and there is disagreement over al-Darawardi: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah, Khalid ibn Khidash, Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr and others narrated it from al-Darawardi from Suhayl from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn A'idh. Dirar ibn Surad and al-Himmani differed from them, narrating it from al-Darawardi from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from Muslim ibn A'idh; the first saying is more correct."
"926","Another, 982 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad, that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa al-Sijzi informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Amir ibn Sa'd narrating from his father who said: When Sa'd ibn Mu'adh gave judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah that those on whom the razor had run be killed and their wealth and offspring be divided, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has judged among them today with the judgment of Allah, mighty and majestic, which He judged above seven heavens. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi and Harun ibn Abd Allah from Abi Amir from Muhammad ibn Salih. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar narrated it from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from Amir ibn Sa'd from Sa'd; Iyad ibn Abd al-Rahman differed from him, narrating it from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from his father from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf; both erred. Shu'bah differed from them, narrating it from Sa'd from Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, and that is correct."
"927","Another, 983 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibah informed them, reading to him, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Wuhayb, from Abi Waqid al-Laythi, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is cut for the price of a shield."
"928","984 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abi Waqid al-Laythi, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is cut for the price of a shield. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from al-Mughirah ibn Salamah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar from Abi Hisham al-Mughirah ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi from Wuhayb. Abu Waqid is Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Za'idah al-Laythi, spoken about. Imam Ahmad said: I see no harm in him. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of A'ishah."
"929","Another, 985 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Malik, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet but described the Dajjal to his ummah, and I shall describe him with a description no one before me described: he is one-eyed, and Allah, mighty and majestic, is not one-eyed."
"930","986 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet but described the Dajjal to his ummah, and I shall describe him with a description no one before me described: he is one-eyed, and Allah is not one-eyed. Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it from Abi Khaythamah from Yazid ibn Harun. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it from Isa ibn Ahmad from Yazid. Al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated it from Yazid, with addition."
"931","987 - Al-Hafiz Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us in his book, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, from his grandfather: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet but described the Dajjal to his ummah, and I shall describe him with a description no prophet before me described: he is blind in the right eye."
"932","Another, 988 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, reading to him, Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, he said: My grandfather informed us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Ghafiqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Makhramah, from his father, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: I heard Sa'd and some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There were two brothers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one better than the other; the better of them died, then the other lived forty nights after him, then died. The virtue of the first over the second was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did he not pray? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and there was no harm in him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you know what his prayer attained for him? The parable of prayer is like a deep sweet river at a man's door into which he plunges five times daily; what do you think that leaves of his dirt? You do not know what his prayer attained for him."
"933","989 - And Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus, that Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Maliki informed them, reading to him, it was said to him: The judge Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rida al-Antaki informed you, reading to him in the outskirts of Damascus at al-Sha'ur, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, reading to him, he said: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Jazlan dictated to us, Abu Zur'ah - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr - narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to me, from his father, from Amir ibn Sa'd who said: I heard Sa'd and some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating that two brother men in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one better than the other, died, the better of them, then the other lived forty nights after him, then died. The virtue of the first was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did he not pray? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and there was no harm in him. He said: What makes you know what his prayer attained for him? Then he said at that: The parable of prayer is like a deep sweet river at one of your doors into which he plunges five times daily; what do you think that leaves of his dirt? You do not know what his prayer attained for him."
"934","990 - And al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us in Baghdad, that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Harun, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah narrated to me, from his father, from Amir ibn Sa'd who said: I heard Sa'd and some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There were two brother men in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one better than the other; the better of them died, then the other lived forty nights after him, then died. The excellence of the first over the second was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did he not pray? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and there was no harm in him. He said: What makes you know what his prayer attained for him? Then he said at that: The parable of prayer is like a river at a man's door, deep and sweet, into which he plunges five times daily; what do you think that leaves of his dirt? Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Malik narrated it in al-Muwatta that it reached him from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father. Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated it from his father from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father; it is said Malik took it from Makhramah ibn Bukayr. And Allah knows best. Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri from Salih ibn Abi Farwah from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from Aban ibn Uthman from Uthman; Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri is alone with it; if he preserved it accurately, the hadith is his. And Allah knows best."
"935","Another, 991 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq narrated to me, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you clears his throat while in the mosque, let him conceal his phlegm so it does not touch a believer's skin or garment and harm him."
"936","992 - With it, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah - meaning Ibn Numayr - narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you clears his throat in the mosque, let him bury it so it does not touch a believer's skin or garment and harm him."
"937","993 - And Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus, that Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Maliki informed them, reading to him, it was said to him: The judge al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rida al-Antaki informed you, reading to him, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, reading to him, he said: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Jazlan dictated to us, Abu Zur'ah - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr - narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us. 994 - And Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq. 995 - And Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq. 996 - And Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Atiq, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you clears his throat in the mosque, let him conceal his phlegm so it does not touch a believer's skin or garment and harm him."
"938","997 - Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq; and Ya'qub, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to me. Ya'qub said: Ibn Abi Atiq, from Amir ibn Sa'd, he narrated to him from his father Sa'd who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you clears his throat in the mosque, let him conceal his phlegm lest it touch a believer's skin or garment and harm him. Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari from Abd al-A'la from Ibn Ishaq."
"939","Another, 998 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Musa - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Wazir Abu al-Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The servant was commanded to prostrate on seven limbs of his: his face, his hands, his knees and his feet; whichever he does not place, he has diminished. Abd Allah ibn Ja'far is Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Makhramah al-Zuhri; al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated for him. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"940","Another, 999 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us, reading to him while we heard in Damascus, it was said: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Qays al-Maliki informed you, reading to him while you heard, it was said to him: The judge Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rida al-Antaki informed you, reading to him in the outskirts of Damascus at al-Shaghur, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, reading to him, he said: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Jazlan dictated to us, Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Safwan al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud: Supply arrows to Sa'd; shoot, O Sa'd; may Allah shoot for you; shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you. His saying: Shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you, is mentioned in the Sahih."
"941","1000 - And this Abu Abd Allah informed us, that Abu al-Majd Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tha'labi informed them, Abu al-Faraj Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: My uncle narrated to me, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Ja'far say: I heard Isma'il ibn Muhammad, he said: And my father used to add in his chain, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud say: Supply arrows to Sa'd; shoot, may Allah shoot for you; shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"942","1001 - With it Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim informed us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Makhramah, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud to my father: Supply arrows to Sa'd; shoot, O Sa'd; may Allah shoot for you; shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it in the Book of the Deed of Day and Night."
"943","Another, 1002 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah informed us, my grandfather Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If what a fingernail carries of Paradise were to appear, what is between the horizons of the heavens and the earth would be adorned."
"944","1003 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed me, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah informed us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If what a fingernail carries of what is in Paradise were to appear, what is between the horizons of the heavens and the earth would be adorned for it; and if a man of the people of Paradise were to look out and his bracelets appeared, their light would efface the light of the sun as the sun effaces the light of the stars. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Suwayd ibn Nasr from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ibn Lahi'ah and said: A strange hadith, known by this chain only from the hadith of Ibn Lahi'ah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrates it, and there is disagreement from him: al-Layth narrated it from Yazid from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd from his father from his grandfather; Yahya ibn Ayyub differed, narrating it from Yazid ibn Habib from Umar from Sa'd; the first is more correct. I did not write this hadith from Ibn Lahi'ah's hadith except for al-Daraqutni's saying that al-Layth narrated it from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, and it has come to us by another route."
"945","1004 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us, Harmalah ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, that Sulayman ibn Humayd narrated to him that Amir ibn Sa'd narrated to him, Sulayman said: I know only that he narrated to me from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: If what a fingernail carries of Paradise were to descend into this world, what is between heaven and earth would be adorned for it. Sulayman ibn Humayd: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him without mentioning criticism of him."
"946","Another, 1005 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Fath al-Nahrawani informed us in Baghdad, that Abu al-Hasan Sa'd al-Khayr ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Ansari informed them, reading to him, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad al-Dawani informed us, Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Kassar informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sunni informed us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id and the judge Abu Ubayd Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Harb informed us, both said: Zayd ibn Ahzam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that a Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, my father used to join kin and do such, so where is he? He said: In the Fire. The Bedouin seemed grieved by that, and said: O Messenger of Allah, where is your father? He said to him: Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him tidings of the Fire. Then the Bedouin embraced Islam. He said: Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has burdened me with toil; I never pass by the grave of a disbeliever but I give him tidings of the Fire. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym and al-Walid ibn Ata ibn al-Agharr narrate it from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd from Sa'd and others; others narrate it from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from al-Zuhri as mursal, and that is correct. I say: This narration we narrated strengthens the connected."
"947","Another, 1006 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to hand me arrows on the day of Uhud, saying: Shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you. We intended from the hadith only his saying: He used to hand me arrows; the ransom has been mentioned in the Sahih."
"948","1007 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, reading to him in Isfahan, it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Harith informed you, reading to him while you were present, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ziyad ibn Ridhah informed us, reading to him, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Mutayr al-Tabarani narrated to us, Abu Zur'ah - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi - narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Hajwah ibn Mudrik al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make his shooting straight and answer his supplication."
"949","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1008 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, the judge Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu al-Rabi' and Abu Bakr both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit who said: Mu'awiyah came in one of his pilgrimages and Sa'd came to him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say concerning Ali three traits; that one of them be mine is dearer to me than the world and what is in it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whomsoever I am his master; and you are to me in the position of Harun to Musa; and I shall give the banner ... Whomsoever I am his master, suffices; for another has been mentioned in the Sahih."
"950","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mall Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1009 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Suwayd narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abi Uthman, from Sa'd ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be a tribulation; the sitting in it is better than the standing, the standing in it better than the walking, the walking in it better than the running, the running in it better than the riding, and the riding in it better than the galloping."
"951","A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, may Allah be pleased with him. 1010 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qudsi informed us in Damascus, that Abu al-Majd Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tha'labi informed them, reading to him, Abu al-Faraj Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali ibn Sinan al-Nasa'i informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us in his hadith, from Ibn Wahb who said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal narrated to him, from Khuzaymah, from A'ishah daughter of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from her father, that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a woman with pebbles before her glorifying Allah, and he said: Shall I tell you of what is easier for you than this, or better? He said: Glory be to Allah as many as He created in heaven, glory be to Allah as many as He is creating, Allah is Greatest the like of that, praise be to Allah the like of that, and there is no power except with Allah the like of that. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it in the Deed of Day and Night. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Salih from Ibn Wahb. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Asbagh ibn al-Faraj from Ibn Wahb and said: A hasan gharib hadith from Sa'd's hadith."
"952","1011 - Abu al-Fadl Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us in Baghdad, that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them, reading to him, Abu al-Hasan Jabir ibn Yasin ibn Mahmud al-Attar informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas al-Mukhallis informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, he narrated to him, from Khuzaymah, from A'ishah bint Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from her father: That he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a woman with date stones or pebbles before her glorifying with them, and he said: Shall I tell you of what is better than this? He said: Glory be to Allah as many as He created in heaven, glory be to Allah as many as He created on earth, glory be to Allah as many as between that, glory be to Allah as many as He is creating, Allah is Greatest the like of that, praise be to Allah the like of that, there is no god but Allah the like of that, and there is no power except with Allah the like of that. Al-Hakim narrated it in his book from Isma'il ibn Ahmad from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asqalani from Harmalah ibn Yahya from Ibn Wahb from Amr from Sa'id from A'ishah, without mentioning Khuzaymah in the chain. Likewise Abu Hatim narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim from Harmalah ibn Yahya."
"953","Another, 1012 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Abi al-Zinad, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he took the Fara' road, would enter ihram when his mount stood up with him, and when he took the other road, would enter ihram when he ascended the height of al-Bayda. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Muhammad ibn Bashshar from Wahb ibn Jarir."
"954","Another, 1013 - Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Ja'd ibn Aws who said: A'ishah bint Sa'd narrated to me, she said: Sa'd said: I complained of an illness in Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left wealth, and I have only one daughter; shall I bequeath two thirds of my wealth and leave her a third? He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath half and leave her half? He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath a third and leave her two thirds? He said: A third, and a third is much, three times. He said: Then he placed his hand on his forehead and wiped my face, chest and belly, saying: O Allah, heal Sa'd and complete his emigration. I continued to imagine I felt the coolness of his hand on my liver until this hour. As for its beginning, it has come in the two Sahihs; as for its end, from his saying: Then he placed his hand, it is not mentioned. And Allah knows best."
"955","Another, 1014 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn al-Ikhwah and A'ishah bint Ma'mar informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir al-Madini narrated to us, from Muhajir ibn Mismar who said: A'ishah bint Sa'd informed me, from Sa'd, that he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the road of Makkah while he was heading to it; when he reached Ghadir Khumm he stopped the people, then sent back those who had gone ahead, and those who lagged behind caught up. When the people gathered to him he said: O people, have I conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness, saying it three times. Then he said: O people, who is your master? They said: Allah and His Messenger, three times. Then he took the hand of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and raised him, saying: Whomsoever Allah and His Messenger are his master, this is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"956","Another, 1015 - Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad, that Umar al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad informed us, al-Haytham al-Shashi informed us, Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham al-Dayra'aquli narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Bijad ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from A'ishah bint Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, that he said: It has been mentioned in the Sahih from Sa'd: I am the first man to shoot an arrow in the way of Allah; we mentioned it only for his poetry."
"957","Another, 1016 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, reading to him, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, Ubaydah bint Nabil narrated to us, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink standing."
"958","1017 - And Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Karam ibn Abi Yasir al-Mallah informed us in Baghdad, that Abu Shuja' Umar ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili al-Balkhi informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuza'i informed us, Abu Sa'id al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Ma'qil al-Shashi informed us, Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, Ubaydah bint Na'il narrated to us, from A'ishah bint Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink standing. Some said: Ubaydah bint Nabil. Thus al-Tirmidhi narrated it in the Book of al-Shama'il."
"959","Another, 1018 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, Ubaydah bint Nabil narrated to us, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: What is between my house and my prayer place is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."
"960","1019 - My uncle, the Imam, the learned Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed them, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, it was said to him: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed you, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us, Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah bint Nabil narrated to me - she was a truthful woman - freedwoman of A'ishah daughter of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my prayer place is a garden of the gardens of Paradise. Al-Farwi said: It is the prayer place of the two Eids, Fitr and Adha; and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink standing."
"961","Another, 1020 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, from Ubaydah bint Nabil, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father Sa'd that he said: Nothing prevents me from narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that I not be the most prolific of his Companions in hadith from him - but I dislike that they attribute to me."
"962","Umar ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him. 1021 - As'ad ibn Sa'd ibn Mahmud informed us in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, reading to her, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Abi Ishaq, from Umar ibn Sa'd, Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Killing a Muslim is disbelief and abusing him is wickedness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."
"963","1022 - And Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Abu al-Mahasin As'ad ibn Ziyad informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Hamawi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us. 1023 - And Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me. Both said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abi Ishaq, from Umar ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting a Muslim is disbelief and abusing him is wickedness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days. The wording is one. Ibn Rahawayh Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from him."
"964","Another, 1024 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad, that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Isa ibn Ahmad al-Asqalani narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Mujammi' who said: Umar ibn Sa'd had a need of his father, so he prefaced his need with speech of what people narrate and embellish, which he had not heard from him before; when he finished he said: O my son, have you finished your speech? He said: Yes. He said: You were never farther from your need, nor was I more indifferent to you than since I heard this speech of yours. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There will be a people who eat with their tongues as cows eat from the earth. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ya'la."
"965","1025 - Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'la and Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Yahya said: A man whose name I used to name but forgot narrated to me, from Umar ibn Sa'd who said: I had a need of Abu Sa'd. He said: And Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Mujammi' who said: Umar ibn Sa'd had a need of his father, so he prefaced his need with speech of what people narrate, embellishing, which he had not heard - meaning before - and when he finished he said: O my son, have you finished your speech? He said: Yes. He said: You were never farther from your need, nor was I more indifferent to you than since I heard this speech of yours. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a people who eat with their tongues as cows eat the earth."
"966","1026 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, reading to him, Abu Amr al-Musayyab ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab al-Awghayani informed us, Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us, the judge Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abi Hayyan al-Taymi, from Mujammi' al-Taymi who said: Umar ibn Sa'd had a need of his father. He said: He went and joined speech, then came to Sa'd and spoke to him with it, joining it to his need, speaking with speech he had not heard before that. When he finished Sa'd said to him: Have you finished, O my son, your need? He said: Yes. He said: You were never farther from your need than now, nor was I more indifferent to you than now. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a people who eat with their tongues as cows eat with their tongues. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Jarir, Isa ibn Yunus and Ya'la ibn Ubayd from Abi Hayyan, and it is from Ibn Sa'd. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abu Hayyan al-Taymi narrates it from Mujammi' al-Taymi from Umar ibn Sa'd from Sa'd. Ibn Fudayl narrated it from Abi Hayyan saying: from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd; the first is more correct."
"967","Another, 1027 - Abu Najih Fadl Allah ibn Uthman ibn Ahmad al-Juzdani informed us with my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed you, reading to him while you heard in Naysabur, Abu Nasr Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Musa informed us, reading to him, Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Harb informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Hashim ibn Hayyan al-Abdi al-Tusi narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth al-Abdi, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I marvel at the believer: if good befalls him he praises Allah and thanks Him, and if calamity befalls him he reckons it and is patient; the believer is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he raises to his mouth."
"968","1028 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father who said: I marvel at the believer: if good befalls him he praises Allah and thanks, and if calamity befalls him he praises Allah and is patient; the believer is rewarded in all his affair, even rewarded in the morsel he raises to his wife. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abd al-Razzaq from Sufyan from Abi Ishaq, and from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Shu'bah from Abi Ishaq, and from Waki' from Isra'il. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from Shu'bah. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in the Deed of Day and Night from Qutaybah from Abi al-Ahwas from Abi Ishaq. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned much disagreement, saying: Isra'il, al-Thawri, Abu al-Ahwas, Ma'mar, Khadij ibn Mu'awiyah and Shu'bah narrated it from Abi Ishaq from al-Ayzar from Umar ibn Sa'd from Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the correct of that is the saying of al-Thawri, Shu'bah and Isra'il, meaning this route."
"969","Another, 1029 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Sa'd or another, that Sa'd ibn Malik said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever degrades Quraysh, Allah, mighty and majestic, degrades him. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq."
"970","1030 - And al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and A'ishah bint Ma'mar all informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah the Exalted humiliates him."
"971","Another, 1031 - Abu Muhammad Yunus ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hashimi informed us in Misr, and Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi in Baghdad, that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Badr ibn Uthman who said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: They are martyred by killing, plague, drowning, belly disease, and a woman dying in childbirth, her death in her confinement."
"972","Al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah ibn Jawsh al-Ghatafani, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1032 - Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i said, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah who said: I said to Sa'd ibn Malik: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib recites: Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten. He said: Allah did not send the Qur'an down upon al-Musayyib; by Allah, it is only: Whatever verse We abrogate or cause you to forget, O Muhammad. He said: And remember your Lord when you forget. He said: And We shall make you recite so you shall not forget. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in al-Tafsir from him."
"973","Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1033 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us with my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, reading to him while you heard, Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to me, my father narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys full of wealth, he would wish a third to them; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever turns."
"974","1034 - And Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, reading to him while we heard in Isfahan, it was said to him: Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed you, reading to him while you heard, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would wish a third to them; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever turns. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Isma'il but Sufyan, nor from him but Hamid; al-Husayn is alone with it."
"975","Another, 1035 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us with my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed you, reading to him while you heard, Ibrahim ibn Mansur Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays who said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas led us in prayer and rose in the two rak'ahs, so we glorified Allah for him, but he stood fully upright. He said: He continued in his standing until he finished, saying: Did you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Abu Uthman - meaning Amr - said: We heard no one raise this hadith but Abu Mu'awiyah."
"976","1036 - With it, Amr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Khalid, from Qays who said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas led us in prayer, and he mentioned the like of Abi Mu'awiyah's hadith without mentioning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"977","1037 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd, that he rose from the two rak'ahs and they glorified Allah for him, but he stood fully upright. He said: Then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness when he finished, then said: Do you think I sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Abu Ya'la also narrated it from Abi Khaythamah from Abi Mu'awiyah."
"978","1038 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd that he rose in the two rak'ahs and they glorified Allah for him, but he stood fully upright, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness when he finished, then said: Did you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Bayan ibn Bishr and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrate it from Qays. As for Bayan, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid raised it from Shu'bah from Bayan from Qays from Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Ghundar and others stopped it from Shu'bah. As for Isma'il, Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir raised it and gave it chain. Za'idah, Zuhayr, Hushaym, al-Muharibi, Ibn Uyaynah, Khalid al-Wasiti, Yahya al-Qattan, Marwan, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari and others stopped it; the stopped is the preserved. Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Mani'."
"979","Another, 1039 - Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti said, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays who said: I heard Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, answer him when he supplicates You, meaning Sa'd."
"980","Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him. 1040 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us. 1041 - And al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father Muhammad narrated to me, from his father Sa'd who said: I passed by Uthman ibn Affan in the mosque and greeted him, and he stared at me, then did not return my greeting. So I came to the Commander of the Faithful Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: O Commander of the Faithful, has anything happened in Islam? Twice. He said: No, and what is that? He said: I said: Nothing, except that I passed by Uthman just now in the mosque and greeted him, and he stared at me then did not return my greeting. Umar sent to Uthman and called him, saying: What prevented you from returning your brother's greeting? Uthman said: I did not do it. Sa'd said: I said: Yes, you did. Until he swore and I swore. Then Uthman remembered and said: Yes, and I seek Allah's forgiveness and turn to Him; you passed by me just now while I was telling myself a word I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, I never remembered it but my sight and heart were covered. Sa'd said: Then I shall tell you of it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned to us the first supplication, then a Bedouin came and busied him until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood. Sa'd followed him, and when I feared he would precede me to his house I struck the ground with my foot, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to me saying: Who is this, Abu Ishaq? He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What then? He said: I said: Nothing, by Allah, except that you mentioned to us the first supplication, then this Bedouin came and busied you. He said: Yes, the supplication of Dhu al-Nun when he was in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You, glory be to You; I was of the wrongdoers. No Muslim ever supplicates his Lord with it for anything but He answers him. The wording of Imam Ahmad; in Zuhayr's narration: Has anything happened in Islam? He said: And what is that? And with him: What prevents you? And with him: Uthman said: I did not do it! And therein: Then Uthman remembered; and with him: a covering, and Sa'd said; and with him: He busied him then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and not with him: busied you; the rest is the like."
"981","1042 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a supplication, then a Bedouin came and busied him. So I followed him and he turned to me, saying: Abu Ishaq? He said: Yes. He said: What is it? I said: You mentioned a supplication then the Bedouin busied you. He said: Yes, the supplication of Dhu al-Nun when he called his Lord in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You, glory be to You; I was of the wrongdoers. No Muslim supplicates with it for anything but it is answered for him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya from Muhammad ibn Yusuf from Yunus likewise. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in the Deed of Day and Night from Humayd ibn Makhlad from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, and from al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya ibn Dinar from Ubayd ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Muhajir from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad likewise. Al-Tirmidhi said: More than one narrated this hadith from Yunus from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad from Sa'd, without mentioning from his father therein."
"982","Another, 1043 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from Abi Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Malik, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting a Muslim is disbelief, and abusing him is wickedness. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad from Waki' from Sharik. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ibn Mansur from Abi Hammam al-Dallal from Isra'il, both from Abi Ishaq. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated it from Abi Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father; Ma'mar differed, narrating it from Abi Ishaq from Umar ibn Sa'd from Sa'd; and it is said from Ma'mar from Abi Ishaq from Amir ibn Sa'd, and it is not sound; the correct is the hadith of Muhammad ibn Sa'd."
"983","Another, 1044 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan ibn al-Ala ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi, from Yusuf ibn al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah humiliates him."
"984","1045 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Abi al-Ala ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi, from Yusuf ibn al-Hakam Abi al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah, mighty and majestic, humiliates him. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abi Kamil from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, and from Abd ibn Humayd from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim from his father, saying: A strange hadith. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated it from Salih ibn Kaysan from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan from Yusuf ibn al-Hakam from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from Sa'd. Ma'mar narrated it from al-Zuhri saying: from Umar ibn Sa'd, and Ma'mar erred therein; the correct is the hadith of Salih ibn Kaysan. Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Madani - a shaykh of his - from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd from Sa'd, and it is error; the correct is the hadith of al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan."
"985","Another, 1046 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us in al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Malik, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."
"986","1047 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, raising the hadith: It is not lawful for anyone to forsake his brother for more than three days. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Yahya ibn Adam. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abi Ayyub."
"987","Another, 1048 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Tamim ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq, freedman of Thaqif, informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are of happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious house, a righteous neighbour, and a comfortable mount; and four are of misery: a bad neighbour, a bad wife, a narrow house, and a bad mount. Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar ibn Yazid al-Zuhri narrated it from Abi Asim from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd."
"988","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1049 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, that he narrated from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: That he used to pray the last Isha in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then pray witr with one, adding nothing to it. He said: It was said to him: Do you pray witr with one, adding nothing to it, O Abu Ishaq? He would say: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He who does not sleep until he prays witr is resolute. Thus Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad; and I do not think Muhammad heard from Sa'd. And Allah knows best."
"989","Mujahid ibn Jabr Abu al-Hajjaj, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1050 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuzami informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I fell severely ill. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me and placed his hand between my breasts until I felt its coolness on my heart, saying: You are a man with heart disease; go to al-Harith ibn Kaladah, brother of Thaqif, for he is a man who practices medicine; order him to take seven Ajwah dates of Madinah's Ajwah with their stones, crush them, then rub you with them."
"990","Another, 1051 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih who said: Tawus was asked about a man who omitted a pebble of the stoning of the jamarat, and said: He feeds a mouthful, and sometimes said: A date. Mujahid said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman, did he not hear what Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said? Sa'd said: We returned from the pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), some saying: I stoned with seven pebbles, some saying: I stoned with six, and none criticized another; sometimes he said: Neither criticized the other."
"991","1052 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, he said: I asked Tawus about a man who stoned the jamrah with six pebbles, and he said: Let him feed a handful of food. He said: Then I met Mujahid and asked him, mentioning Tawus's saying to him, and he said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman, has the saying of Sa'd ibn Malik not reached him? He said: We stoned the jamarat, or the jamrah, in our pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then sat discussing; some said: I stoned with six, some said: I stoned with seven, some said: I stoned with eight, some said: I stoned with nine, and they saw no harm in that. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi from Sufyan."
"992","Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' al-Asadi al-Kahili, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1053 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely tried of people are the prophets, then the next best, then the next best, then the rest of people according to their religion; whoever is thick in religion, his trial is severe, and whoever is weak in religion, his trial is weak. And it was narrated from Mus'ab from his father. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Jarir from al-Ala. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab narrated it from his father from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father. Al-Qasim ibn Malik and al-Muharibi narrated it from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father. Ibn Fudayl said: from al-Ala from his father from Sa'd; and the correct is from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud from Mus'ab from Sa'd. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abi Ya'la al-Mawsili from Ishaq ibn Isma'il al-Talqani from Jarir from al-Ala."
"993","Mus'ab ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him. 1054 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: al-Suddi claimed, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted safety to the people except four men and two women, saying: Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah: Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, Abd Allah ibn Khatal, Miqyas ibn Subabah, and Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi al-Sarh. As for Abd Allah ibn Khatal, he was caught clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah, and Sa'id ibn Hurayth and Ammar ibn Yasir raced to him; Sa'id outran Ammar - he was the younger of the two - and killed him. As for Miqyas ibn Subabah, the people caught him in the market and killed him. As for Ikrimah, he boarded the sea and a storm struck them; the ship's crew said to the passengers: Be sincere, for your gods avail you nothing here. Ikrimah said: If nothing but sincerity saves me at sea, nothing but it saves me on land. O Allah, I have a covenant upon me: if You heal me of what I am in, I shall come to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until I place my hand in his, and I shall find him pardoning and generous. He said: Then he came and embraced Islam. As for Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh, he hid with Uthman ibn Affan; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people to the pledge, Uthman brought him until he stood him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, pledge Abd Allah. He said: He raised his head and looked at him three times, each time refusing, then pledged him after three. Then he turned to his Companions and said: Was there no right-minded man among you to stand to this one when he saw me withhold my hand from his pledge and kill him? They said: How would we know, O Messenger of Allah, what was in your mind? He said: It is not fitting for a prophet to have treacherous eyes. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya ibn Dinar, both from Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal likewise."
"994","1055 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad, that Umar al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Dawradi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: al-Suddi claimed, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted safety to the people except four men and two women, saying: Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah: Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, Abd Allah ibn Khatal, Miqyas ibn Subabah, and Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh. As for Abd Allah ibn Khatal, he was caught clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah; Sa'id ibn Hurayth and Ammar ibn Yasir raced to him, and Sa'id outran Ammar - he was the younger of the two - and killed him. As for Miqyas ibn Subabah, the people caught him in the market and killed him. As for Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, he boarded the sea and a storm struck them; the ship's crew said to the passengers: Be sincere, for your gods avail you nothing here. Ikrimah said: By Allah, if nothing but sincerity saves me at sea, nothing but it saves me on land. O Allah, I have a covenant: if You heal me of what I am in, I shall come to Muhammad until I place my hand in his, and I shall find him pardoning and generous. He said: Then he came and embraced Islam. He said: As for Abd Allah ibn Abi Sarh, he hid with Uthman ibn Affan; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people to the pledge, he brought him until he stood him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, pledge Abd Allah. He raised his head and looked at him three times, each time refusing, then pledged him after that. Then he turned to his Companions and said: Was there no right-minded man among you to stand to this one when he saw me withhold my hand from his pledge and kill him? They said: How would we know, O Messenger of Allah, what was in your mind; did you not gesture to us with your eye? He said: It is not fitting for a prophet to have treacherous eyes. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal narrates it from Asbat from al-Suddi from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from Sa'd. Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated it from his father from Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal from Asbat from Simak, erring in his saying from Simak; it is only from al-Suddi."
"995","Another, 1056 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tried? He said: The prophets, then the righteous, then the next best, then the next best of people; a man is tried according to his religion: if his religion is firm, his trial is increased, and if his religion is soft, it is lightened for him. Trial keeps befalling the servant until he walks on the back of the earth with no sin upon him. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Waki'."
"996","1057 - And Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely tried of people are the prophets, then the next best, then the next best; a servant is tried only according to his religion: if he is firm in religion, his trial is severe, and if there is something in his religion, his trial is according to that. Trial keeps befalling the believer until he walks on the face of the earth with no sin upon him."
"997","1058 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tried? He said: The prophets, then the next best, then the next best; a servant is tried according to his religion. He said: Trial keeps befalling the servant until he walks on the face of the earth with no sin upon him. Hammad said: Asim hamzated it."
"998","1059 - And Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim and A'ishah bint Ma'mar informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Asim, from Ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which people are most severely tried? He said: The prophets, then the next best, then the next best; a servant is tried according to his religion: if he is firm in religion, the trial is severe upon him, and if his religion is soft, he is tried according to that. Trial keeps befalling the servant until it leaves the servant with no sin upon him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Asim, and from Affan from Hammad ibn Zayd from Asim, and from Ja'far ibn Muhammad from Shu'bah from Asim. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id from Sharik, and in a narration from Hammad ibn Zayd. Ibn Majah narrated it from Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Ma'ni and Yahya ibn Durust from Hammad ibn Zayd from Asim. Al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih hadith. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Imran ibn Musa from Hudbah ibn Khalid from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"999","Another, 1060 - Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza, and my companions said: You have uttered foul speech. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The covenant was recent, and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: There is no god but Allah alone, three times, then spit to your left three times, seek refuge with Allah from Satan three times, and do not repeat. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna and Abi Sa'id from Isra'il."
"1000","1061 - And al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza, and my companions said to me: You have uttered foul speech. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am new in covenant, and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. He said: Say: There is no god but Allah, three times, spit to your left three times, and seek refuge. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Yahya ibn Adam. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Khallal from Yahya ibn Adam. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abi Dawud al-Harrani from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad from Zuhayr from Abi Ishaq, and from Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad from Makhlad ibn Yazid from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from his father, and from Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Harrani from Makhlad. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, and from Abi Ya'la al-Mawsili from Ishaq ibn Isma'il al-Talqani from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Isra'il. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Isra'il narrated it from Abi Ishaq from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from Sa'd; Safwan ibn Sulaym differed, narrating it from Abi Ishaq from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from Abi Sa'id al-Khudri - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Muzani said it from Safwan - erring therein; the correct is Isra'il's saying."
"1001","Another, 1062 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-A'mash mentioning it, from Abi Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every trait the believer is imprinted - or he said: folded - upon except treachery and lying. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: al-A'mash narrates it from Abi Ishaq from Mus'ab from his father; Dawud ibn Rushayd said it from Ali ibn Hashim from al-A'mash. Hamzah al-Zayyat differed, narrating it from al-A'mash from Mus'ab without mentioning Abi Ishaq. Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Mus'ab; Abu Shaybah raised it from Salamah, while al-Thawri and Shu'bah differed, narrating it from Salamah as stopped, not raised. It is said from al-Thawri from Salamah as raised, and it is not established; the stopped is closest to correct."
"1002","Another, 1063 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i informed us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever supplicates with the supplication of Yunus is answered. It has preceded in the narration of Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father. Kathir: some criticized him and some praised him."
"1003","Another, 1064 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... [text breaks off in source]"
"1004","1065 - And Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that al-Mukhtar ibn Abd al-Hamid informed them, reading to him, ... Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd ibn Malik, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl and ate from it, and a remainder remained. He said: A man of Paradise will come from this pass to eat this remainder. Sa'd said: I left my brother Umayr performing ablution, saying: He is Umayr. He said: Then Abd Allah ibn Salam came and ate it. The wording is one; in Imam Ahmad's narration: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will come."
"1005","1066 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: I was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he had food remainder, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise who eats this remainder will surely appear to you from this pass. He said: I passed by Umayr ibn Malik performing ablution, saying to myself: He is its man. We kept craning to see who would appear to us, and Abd Allah ibn Salam appeared to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called him for the remainder and he ate it. Abu Ya'la narrated it from Zuhayr from Affan. It has come in the Sahih from Sa'd's hadith who said: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say of any man that he is of the people of Paradise except Abd Allah ibn Salam. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1006","Another, 1067 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, reading to him, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, that Abu Hazim narrated to him, from a son of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith began strange and shall return as it began; blessed then are the strangers when people are corrupt. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, faith shall retreat between these two mosques as a snake retreats into its hole. Thus Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad. I say: Abu Hazim did not name which of Sa'd's children he is. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Humaydi from three of Sa'd's children from Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited him in Makkah - except that Sa'd's case, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited him in Makkah, is narrated in the Sahih from Amir and Mus'ab, the two sons of Sa'd; perhaps this hadith comes in some routes. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from Ibn Umar and Abu Hurayrah."
"1007","Another, 1068 - Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad al-Khalili informed us, Ali al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham al-Shashi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from al-A'mash, from Mus'ab, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of knowledge is dearer to me than the excellence of worship, and the best of your religion is scrupulousness. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated it from al-A'mash from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from Sa'd; Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus differed, narrating it from al-A'mash from Mutarrif from Hudhayfah. Abu Muti' al-Balkhi narrated it from al-A'mash from Abi Salih from Abi Hurayrah; and it is said from al-A'mash from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Thawban. Al-Musayyab ibn Sharik said: from al-A'mash from Salim from Jabir. None of these chains is established; it is only narrated from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir as his saying."
"1008","Another, 1069 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shukr al-Tamimi informed us in Isfahan, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, reading to him, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, Khallad al-Saffar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: Alif Lam Ra, these are the verses of the clear Book; We sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an that you may understand. He said: The Qur'an came down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited it to them for a time. They said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would narrate stories to us. So Allah sent down: We relate to you the best of stories, the verse. He said: He recited it to them for a time. They said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would narrate hadith to us. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: Allah sent down the best hadith, a consistent Book with repetitions ... the verse; all of that commanding them with the Qur'an. Khallad said: Another added to me therein: They said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would remind us. So Allah sent down: Has the time not come for those who believe that their hearts humble to Allah's remembrance and what came down of truth. Imam Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad from Amr ibn Muhammad as here. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad from him. Abu Ya'la narrated it in his Musnad from al-Husayn ibn Amr ibn Muhammad - except that al-Husayn is spoken about, so we did not narrate it from him."
"1009","Another, 1070 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Mahmud ibn Khidash narrated to me, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Qanan ibn Abd Allah al-Nahmi narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to us, from his father who said: I was sitting in the mosque, I and two men with me, and we spoke ill of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came angry, anger known in his face. I sought refuge with Allah, mighty and majestic, from his anger. He said: What is with you and with me? Whoever harms Ali has harmed me. He said: Thereafter I would be approached and told: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, alludes to you, saying: Beware the trial of al-Akhnas. I would say: Did he name me? It would be said to me: No. I would say: The hidden of people are many; Allah forbid I harm the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after what I heard from him."
"1010","1071 - And Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, from Qanan ibn Abd Allah, that he heard Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrating from his father who said: I was sitting in the mosque with two men, and we mentioned Ali, disparaging him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came enraged, anger known in his face. I said: I seek refuge with Allah from the anger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What is with you and with me? Whoever harms Ali has harmed me, saying it three times. He said: Thereafter, it would be said: Ali alludes to you, saying: Beware the trial of al-Ukhaynis. I would say: Did he name me? They would say: No. I would say: The hidden of people are many; Allah forbid I harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after what I heard from him."
"1011","Mu'adh ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1072 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us. 1073 - And Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me. Both said: Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibrahim - meaning Ibn Sa'd - narrated to me, from his father, from Mu'adh al-Taymi who said: I heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Two prayers after which there is no prayer: Fajr until the sun rises, and Asr until the sun sets. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd."
"1012","Huzayl ibn Shurahbil al-Awdi, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1074 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us at Dar al-Qazz in Baghdad, that Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, reading to him, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Umar al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us. 1075 - Abu Dawud said: And Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Talhah, from Huzayl who said: A man came - Uthman said: Sa'd - and stood at the Prophet's door seeking permission, standing at the door - Uthman said: facing the door - and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Thus away from it, or thus; permission is only for the sake of sight."
"1013","1076 - With it, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Harun ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from a man, from Sa'd likewise, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1014","Abu Bakr ibn Khalid ibn Urfutah, from Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1077 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Khallal al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shaqiq ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abi Bakr ibn Khalid ibn Urfutah, that he said: I am Sa'd ibn Malik. He said: It reached me that you are offered the reviling of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in Kufah; did you revile him? He said: Allah forbid. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is Sa'd's soul, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say concerning Ali something that if a saw were placed on my parting to revile him, I would never revile him."
"1015","1078 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Abi Abd Allah - so in our hearing - though it is only Shaqiq ibn Abi Abd Allah, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Khalid ibn Urfutah narrated to us, he said: I came to Sa'd ibn Malik in Madinah, and he said: You revile Ali? He said: I said: We did. He said: Perhaps you reviled him? I said: Allah forbid. He said: Then do not revile him; if a saw were placed on the parting of my head, I would never revile him after what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); what I heard: Whomsoever I am his master, Ali is his master."
"1016","Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) 1079 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah, and A'ishah bint Mu'ammar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is it disliked for a man to die in the land from which he emigrated? He said: Yes."
"1017","Abu Kathir, said to be the freedman of Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh al-Asadi, from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him). 1080 - The Imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih al-Jili (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us at Baghdad, that Abu al-Waqt Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa ibn al-Sijzi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir, that Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas came demanding a debt owed to him by a man, and they said: He has gone out. He said: Then I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Even if a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, then killed, he would not enter Paradise until he settles his debt."
"1018","Musnad of Sa'id ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him). Musnad of Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Riyah ibn Qurt ibn Razah ibn Adi ibn Ka'b, Abu al-A'war al-Adawi (may Allah be pleased with him) 1081 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abd Allah ibn Zalim al-Mazini, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl that he said: I bear witness concerning nine that they are in Paradise, and if I were to bear witness concerning the tenth I would not sin. It was said: How is that? He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Hira, and he said: Be firm, O Hira, for there is upon you none but a Prophet, or a Siddiq, or a martyr. It was said: Who are they? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and Ibn Awf. It was said: Who is the tenth? He said: I am."
"1019","1082 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us at Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Saffar, trustworthy, from the people of good, narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Sa'id al-Qurashi narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Fulan ibn Hayyan, from Abd Allah ibn Zalim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl who said: A man came to me and said: Inform me about Ali, for I have loved him with a love I never loved anyone at all. He said: I think you have loved a man from the people of Paradise. He said: Then inform me about Uthman, for I hate him with a hatred I never hated anyone at all. He said: Evil is what you have done; you have hated a man from the people of Paradise. Then he began to narrate. He said: Hira shook, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be still, O Hira, for there is upon you none but a Prophet, or a Siddiq, or a martyr. And upon it were the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Sa'd ibn Malik. He said: And if I wished I could inform you of the tenth, meaning himself. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, from Za'idah, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Zalim; and from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah, from Husayn. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Ubayd ibn Sa'id al-Umawi, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Hilal, from Ibn Hayyan, from Abd Allah ibn Zalim. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Ala', from Abd Allah ibn Idris, from Husayn. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani' in agreement. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Idris, from Husayn; and from Ishaq, from Ubayd ibn Sa'id, from Sufyan, from Mansur. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bundar, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Shu'bah, from Husayn."
"1020","Another. 1083 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna, Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah was in the great mosque with the people of Kufah to his right and left, and a man called Sa'id ibn Zayd came, so al-Mughirah greeted him and seated him at his feet upon the couch. Then a man from the people of Kufah came, faced al-Mughirah and reviled and reviled. He said: Whom is this reviling, O Mughirah? He said: He is reviling Ali ibn Abi Talib. He said: O Mughir ibn Shu'bah - three times - shall I hear the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being reviled in your presence while you neither object nor change it! For I bear witness to what my ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and my heart retained, for I would not narrate a lie from him for which he would question me when I meet him: that he said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman is in Paradise, Sa'd ibn Malik is in Paradise, and the ninth of the believers is in Paradise; if I wished I could name him. He said: So the people of the mosque clamored, imploring him: O Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who is the ninth? He said: You have implored me by Allah, and Allah is great: I am the ninth of the believers, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the tenth. Then he followed that with an oath. He said: By Allah, a scene witnessed by a man in which his face is dusted along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is better than the deed of one of you even if he were given the lifespan of Nuh (peace be upon him)."
"1021","1084 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Musa and Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to us: that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah was in the great mosque with the people of Kufah to his right and left, and a man called Sa'id ibn Zayd came, so al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah greeted him and seated him at his feet upon the couch. Then a man from the people of Kufah came, faced al-Mughirah and reviled and reviled. He said: O Mughirah, whom is this reviling? He said: He is reviling Ali. He said: O Mughir ibn Shu'bah, shall I hear the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being reviled in your presence while you neither object nor change it! I bear witness to what my ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I never narrated a lie from him for which he would question me when I meet him: that he said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, Sa'd ibn Malik is in Paradise, and the ninth of the believers is in Paradise, and if I wished I could name him. So the people of the mosque stirred and implored him: O Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who is the ninth? He said: Do you implore me by Allah? And Allah is greatest: I am the ninth of the believers and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the tenth. Then he followed that with an oath: By Allah, a scene witnessed by a man along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which his face became dusty is better than one of you even if he were given the lifespan of Nuh."
"1022","1085 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Mubarak Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi, and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf, both at Baghdad, informed us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun informed us, Ali - he is Ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi - informed us, Ja'far - he is Ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sabbah - narrated to us, Abu Sahl Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi the blind narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna al-Nakha'i narrated to us. He said: My grandfather Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah in the mosque of Kufah with the people of Kufah present, and Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr came, so al-Mughirah welcomed him and greeted him and seated him at his foot upon the couch. Then a man from the people of Kufah called Qays ibn Alqamah came, faced him and reviled and reviled. Sa'id said: O Mughir, whom is this man reviling? He said to him: He is reviling Ali. Sa'id said to him: O Mughirah, do I see the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being reviled in your presence while you neither object nor change it! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say - and I am too rich to say what he did not say, lest he question me about it when I meet him: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Sa'd ibn Malik is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and the ninth of the Muslims, if I wished I could name him. He said: So the people stirred and implored him: O Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who is the ninth? He said: Had you not implored me I would not have informed you: I am the ninth of the Muslims, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completes the ten. Then he said: A scene of one of them along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which his face became dusty is better than the deed of one of you even if he were given the lifespan of Nuh. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Sadaqah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna in agreement; and from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd. Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham ibn Ammar, from Isa ibn Yunus, from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna."
"1023","Another, being part of the hadith before it. 1086 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Ayshi narrated to us. 1087 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, both saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: We were with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, then Sa'id ibn Zayd came and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Lying against me is not like lying against anyone; whoever lies against me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And the wording is that of the hadith of Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj."
"1024","1088 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna al-Nakha'i narrated to us. He said: My grandfather Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, he said: We were with al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah while he was in the mosque, with the people of Kufah present, and Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl came, so al-Mughirah made room for him and said: Here, sit. So he seated him with him upon the couch. Sa'id said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... whoever lies against me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and about the hadith before it, and he said: A group narrated it, among them Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir, Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Ya'la ibn Ubayd, and Umar ibn Imran al-Tufawi, and they agreed upon its chain and text. Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad and Abd Allah ibn Salamah al-Aftas narrated it from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna with this chain, and both added in it that Sa'id ibn Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Lying against me is not like lying against anyone; whoever lies against me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. This is a good, sound addition from the narration of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, for he is among the trustworthy; as for Abd Allah ibn Salamah al-Aftas, he is not strong."
"1025","Another. 1089 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah and Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me, from al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas: that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah addressed and spoke against Ali. He said: So Sa'id ibn Zayd stood and said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in Paradise, Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Sa'd is in Paradise. Then he said: If you wish I will inform you of the tenth. Then he mentioned himself. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Waki', from Shu'bah."
"1026","1090 - Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us. He said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah addressed and spoke against Ali, so Sa'id ibn Zayd stood and said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in Paradise, Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Sa'd is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman is in Paradise, and if you wish I will inform you of the tenth. Then he mentioned himself. Imam Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim, from Shu'bah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi, from Shu'bah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani' in agreement. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abdah ibn Abd Allah and al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, from Husayn, from Za'idah, from al-Husayn ibn Ubayd Allah, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah; and from Qutaybah, from Abd al-Wahid, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah; and from Hajib ibn Sulayman, from Waki', from Shu'bah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah narrates it - meaning from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas - and there is disagreement from him: al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, al-Walid ibn Qays Abu Hammam al-Sukuni, Shu'bah, Mis'ar, al-Thawri, Isma'il ibn Sawwar, and Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated it from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, from Sa'id. Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated it but did not establish its chain, saying: From Fulan ibn al-Sayyah, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas, intending al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas."
"1027","Another. 1091 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and A'ishah bint Mu'ammar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."
"1028","1092 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Abu al-Mahasin As'ad ibn Ziyad informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ibrahim informed us, my father narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his religion is a martyr, whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr, whoever is killed defending his blood is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his family is a martyr."
"1029","1093 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr, whoever is killed defending his family is a martyr, whoever is killed defending his religion is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his blood is a martyr."
"1030","1094 - Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf who said: Arwa bint Aws came to us with a group of Quraysh among them Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, and she said: I wish you would go to Sa'id ibn Zayd and speak to him and remind him, for he has taken from my land toward his land. So we went to Sa'id until we came to him in his land at al-Aqiq, and he came out to us and said: I know what brought you; Arwa bint Aws came to you and said: I took from her land toward my land what is not mine. I shall narrate to you what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes of land what is not his will be collared with it to the seventh earth; and I heard him say: Whoever fights defending his property is a martyr. He said: So we said: By Allah, we shall never speak to you after this about anything ever. He said: And we mounted and departed. We intended from him only: whoever fights defending his property. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim similarly; and from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri like the narration of al-Adani. He narrated it also from Yazid ibn Harun, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq like the narration of Yazid ibn Zuray'. He narrated it also likewise, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from Sufyan. Abu Dawud narrated it from Harun ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi and Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, from Ibrahim. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd in agreement and said: A good, sound hadith; and from Salamah ibn Shabib and Hatim ibn Siyah al-Marwazi, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri in abridged form: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim and Qutaybah, from Sufyan in abridged form; and from Amr ibn Ali, from Ibn Mahdi; and from Muhammad ibn Rafi' and Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Sulayman ibn Dawud, all from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd. Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham ibn Ammar, from Sufyan, and the hadith of Sufyan is abridged. Al-Daraqutni was asked about the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl al-Amiri, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land, in the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ishaq is the addition: And whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr; and he mentioned the disagreement about it, that some narrated it from Talhah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl, and some narrated it from Talhah, from Sa'id. He said: The most beloved to me is whoever said: From al-Zuhri, from Talhah, from Abd al-Rahman. I say: In the narration of Yazid ibn Zuray', from Muhammad ibn Ishaq which we presented, Talhah and Abd al-Rahman both heard it from Sa'id ibn Zayd, and Allah knows best. It has been narrated by other than this route."
"1031","1095 - As'ad ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah informed them: Ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri informed us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Masruq al-Kufi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abd Allah ibn Jumay', from Abi al-Tufayl, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."
"1032","Another. 1096 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, it is his."
"1033","1097 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Musa ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father (Ha). 1098 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim and A'ishah bint Mu'ammar informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' informed them by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever revives a dead land, it is his, and the unjust root has no right. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ibn Bashshar, from al-Thaqafi. Some narrated it from Hisham, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mursal. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Marwazi, from al-Thaqafi; and from Isa ibn Hammad, from al-Layth, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Hisham, from Urwah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi alone narrated it - meaning from Ayyub - from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id; and there is disagreement about it from Hisham ibn Urwah: al-Thawri narrated it from Hisham, from his father who said: One whom I do not suspect narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid followed him; and Yahya ibn Sa'id, Malik ibn Anas, Abd Allah ibn Idris, and Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi said: From Hisham, from his father, mursal."
"1034","Another. 1099 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Khalid ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Tayyib Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa ibn Shammah informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadan ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Muhammad ibn Zayyan informed us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abi al-Khayr, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, that he heard him say: A man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Advise me. He said: I advise you to feel shame before Allah, mighty and majestic, as you feel shame before a righteous man of your people. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated it, and there is disagreement from him: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it from Yazid, from Abi al-Khayr, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, or Sa'd ibn Yazid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far differed, narrating it from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abi al-Khayr, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from a cousin of his who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me ... the hadith. The statement of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far is closer to correct. I say: This narration of a Companion from a Companion is sound, so it does not affect it, and Allah knows best."
"1035","Another. 1100 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned a tribulation and magnified it. He said: So we said, or they said: O Messenger of Allah, if we reach it we shall surely perish. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nay, killing suffices you. Sa'id said: I saw my brothers killed afterwards."
"1036","1101 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us (Ha). 1102 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abd Allah ibn Zalim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: He mentioned a tribulation - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - like portions of the dark night. He said: People will rush into it most swiftly. It was said: Are all of them doomed? He said: Killing suffices them."
"1037","1103 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Mis'ar informed me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abd Allah ibn Zalim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned tribulations like portions of the dark night, I think he said: People will rush into them most swiftly. He said: It was said: Are all of them doomed or some? He said: Killing suffices them, or: killing is enough for them. Ishaq narrated it from Abu Usamah similarly. Imam Ahmad narrated it with the addition of Abd Allah ibn Zalim; and from Yahya ibn Adam, from Abi al-Ahwas, without mentioning Abd Allah ibn Zalim. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Abi al-Ahwas, without mentioning Abd Allah ibn Zalim. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah narrated it from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ibn Zalim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd; Abu Usamah alone narrated it from Mis'ar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Hilal, from Ibn Zalim; Mansur differed, narrating it from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, without mentioning Ibn Zalim therein; Abu al-Ahwas said that from Mansur; and the hadith of Mis'ar is the sound one."
"1038","Another. 1104 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us at Baghdad, that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Warraq narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, that he heard Abu Ghalib narrating, saying: I heard Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Huwaytib say: My grandmother narrated to me that she heard her father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no prayer for one without ablution, no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah, one does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and one does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar. So he mentioned it, while the well-known is Abu Thifal al-Murri in place of Abu Ghalib. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali and Bishr ibn Mu'adh, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abu Thifal al-Murri, from Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Huwaytib, from his grandmother, from her father, and he said: Her father is Sa'id ibn Zayd; and Abu Thifal al-Murri's name is Thumamah ibn Husayn. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Yazid ibn Iyad ibn Ju'dubah, from Abu Thifal. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah al-Aslami narrated it from Abu Thifal, and there is disagreement from him: Wuhayb, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, Ibn Abi Fudayk, and Sulayman ibn Bilal said: From Ibn Harmalah, from Abu Thifal, from Rabah, from his grandmother, from her father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he mentioned the disagreement therein. He said: The sound is the statement of Wuhayb, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, and those who followed them."
"1039","Another. 1105 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Asbahani informed us there, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah informed us, al-Hakam ibn Nafi' Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb informed us, Ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, Nawfal ibn Musahiq narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: This kinship is a branch from the Most Merciful; whoever severs it, Allah forbids Paradise to him."
"1040","1106 - And with it Abu al-Yaman al-Himsi narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us. He said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, Nawfal ibn Musahiq narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Among the worst of usury is attacking the honor of a Muslim without right."
"1041","1107 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Zayd al-Hawti and Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, Nawfal ibn Musahiq narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Among the worst of usury is a man attacking the honor of a Muslim without right; and this kinship is a branch from the Most Merciful, so whoever severs it, Allah forbids Paradise to him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abi al-Yaman. Abu Dawud narrated from it: Among the worst of usury is attacking the honor of a Muslim without right, from Muhammad ibn Awf, from Abi al-Yaman."
"1042","Another. 1108 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Musa - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah who said: I asked Sa'd ibn Ibrahim about Banu Najiyah. He said: They are from us - Sa'd said: It is narrated - from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: They are a clan from me. Shu'bah said: And I think he said: And I am from them."
"1043","Another. 1109 - Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us, that Umar al-Bistami informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Isma'il ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham came to Sa'id ibn Zayd - at al-Aqiq - while I was with Sa'id ibn Zayd, and asked him about Samah ibn Lu'ayy. Sa'id ibn Zayd said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, is Samah from us or are we from him? He said: He is from us; have you not heard the poet's saying of the she-camel? Abu Ishaq said: I think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) meant by his saying: The she-camel:"
"1044","Another. 1110 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Nufayl ibn Hisham ibn Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Makkah, he and Zayd ibn Harithah, when Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl passed by them, and they invited him to a meal of theirs. He said: O son of my brother, I do not eat of what is slaughtered upon the stone altars. He said: After that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen eating anything slaughtered upon the stone altars. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was as you saw and as reached you; had he met you he would have believed in you and followed you, so shall I seek forgiveness for him? He said: Yes, seek forgiveness for him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone."
"1045","1111 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja' narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Nufayl ibn Hisham ibn Sa'id ibn Zayd, from his father, from his grandfather who said: Waraqah ibn Nawfal and Zayd ibn Amr went out seeking the religion until they passed through Syria. As for Waraqah, he became Christian; as for Zayd, it was said to him: What you seek is before you. So he set out until he came to Mosul, where there was a monk. He said: From where has the traveler come? He said: From the house of Ibrahim. He said: What do you seek? He said: The religion. So he offered him Christianity, but he refused to accept, saying: I have no need of it. He said: The one you seek shall appear in your land. So he returned saying: At Your service, truly, truly, in worship and servitude; good I seek, not evil; is one who emigrates like one who says: I seek refuge in what Ibrahim sought refuge in while standing, and I deny you; O Allah, a toiling aspirant, however much You burden me, I endure. Then he would fall prostrate to the Ka'bah. He said: Zayd ibn Amr passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Zayd ibn Harithah while they were eating from a meal of theirs, and they invited him. He said: O son of my brother, I do not eat of what is slaughtered upon the stone altars. He said: From that day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen eating of what is slaughtered upon the stone altars until he was sent. He said: Sa'id ibn Zayd came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Zayd was as you saw, or as reached you, so shall I seek forgiveness for him? He said: Yes, seek forgiveness for him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from al-Mas'udi."
"1046","1112 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd who said: I and Umar ibn al-Khattab asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Zayd ibn Amr, and he said: He shall come on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone."
"1047","Another. 1113 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Sa'id who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes charge of a people without their permission, upon him is the curse of Allah. And he said: Whoever seizes his brother's wealth by his oath, Allah shall not bless it for him."
"1048","Musnad of Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him). Musnad of Abu Ubaydah Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Jarrah ibn Hilal ibn Uhayb ibn Dabbah ibn al-Harith ibn Fihr (may Allah be pleased with him) 1114 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Suraqah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he mentioned the Dajjal and described him with a description I do not retain. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our hearts be that day? Like today? He said: Or better."
"1049","1115 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abd Allah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Qurashi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Suraqah, from Abu Ubaydah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was no Prophet after Nuh but warned his people of the Dajjal, and I warn you of him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described him to us. He said: Perhaps some who saw me or heard my speech shall meet him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our hearts be that day? Like they are today? He said: Or better."
"1050","1116 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us at Baghdad, that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Suraqah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was no Prophet after Nuh but warned his people of the Dajjal, and I warn you of him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described him to us and said: Perhaps some who saw me or heard my speech shall meet him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our hearts be that day? Like they are today? He said: Or better. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Affan. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Isma'il, from Hammad. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Mu'awiyah in agreement, though Abd Allah is criticized. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Affan."
"1051","Another. 1117 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar, Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman, and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, Wasil, freedman of Abi Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Iyad ibn Ghutayf who said: We visited Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah while ill, his face toward the wall, his wife Tuhayfah sitting. I said: How did Abu Ubaydah pass the night? She said: He passed the night with reward. He heard her saying, and said: He did not pass the night with reward. He turned his face and said: Will you not ask me about what I said? They said: What you said amazed us, so how should we ask you about it? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever spends a surplus expenditure in the path of Allah, it is multiplied seven hundredfold; and whoever spends upon himself or his family, or visits a sick person, a good deed is for ten like it."
"1052","1118 - And with it Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Wasil, freedman of Abi Uyaynah, from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Iyad ibn Ghutayf, from Abu Ubaydah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is afflicted with an affliction in his body, it is an expiation for him."
"1053","1119 - And with it he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield."
"1054","1120 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' Abu Khidash narrated to us, Wasil, freedman of Abi Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf al-Jarmi, from Iyad ibn Ghutayf who said: We visited Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah for an illness that befell him, his wife Tuhayfah sitting at his head. I said: How did Abu Ubaydah pass the night? She said: By Allah, he passed the night with reward. Abu Ubaydah said: I did not pass the night with reward; he had his face toward the wall, then turned his face to the people and said: Will you not ask me about what I said? They said: What you said amazed us, so why should we ask you about it? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever spends a surplus expenditure in the path of Allah, it is seven hundredfold; and whoever spends upon himself and his family, or visits a sick person, or removes harm, a good deed is for ten like it; fasting is a shield so long as he does not tear it; and whoever Allah afflicts with an affliction in his body, it is an expiation for him. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Bashshar. Imam Ahmad narrated it also, and Ahmad ibn Mani', from Yazid ibn Harun, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Wasil; Ibn Mani' did not say in his narration (removes harm), while in Imam Ahmad's narration (removes harm from the path)."
"1055","1121 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us at Isfahan, that Mahmud al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma' narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil, freedman of Abi Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman of the people of Syria, from Iyad ibn Ghutayf, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield so long as he does not tear it. Al-Nasa'i narrated the mention of fasting from Yahya ibn Arabi, from Hammad, from Wasil; and from Muhammad ibn Hatim, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Mis'ar, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik: our companions narrated to us from Abu Ubaydah who said: Fasting ... then he mentioned it as mawquf. Abu Ya'la narrated it in full from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma', from Mahdi, from Wasil. Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Bahr ibn Nasr al-Khawlani, from Ibn Wahb, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Sayf ibn Abi Sayf with its chain: Fasting is a shield so long as he does not tear it."
"1056","Another. 1122 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun who said: Sa'd ibn Samurah ibn Jundub narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah who said: The last words spoken by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were: Expel the Jews of Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula, and know that the worst of people are those who take the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"1057","1123 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Samurah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from Abu Ubaydah who said: The last words spoken by the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were: Expel the Jews of Hijaz from the Arabian Peninsula, and know that the worst of people are those who take graves as mosques. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Yahya ibn Sa'id, and Waki' from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, freedman of the family of Samurah, except that in Waki's narration: From Ibrahim, from Ishaq ibn Sa'd ibn Samurah, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah. Yahya ibn Sa'id and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri agreed in their narration from Ibrahim, from Sa'd ibn Samurah, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from Qays, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, from Ibn Samurah, from Abu Ubaydah without naming him. Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated it like the narration of Yahya and Abi Ahmad."
"1058","1124 - The Hafiz Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us by ijazah, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by reading to him: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maymun, freedman of the family of Samurah, narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Samurah, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Expel the Jews of Najran from Hijaz. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, and he mentioned the narration of Yahya and the narration of Waki', that Waki' erred therein, and the correct is the statement of Yahya and those who followed him."
"1059","Another. 1125 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Tabarani informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us. He said: Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Aslam informed me, from Aslam, freedman of Umar: Maysarah ibn Masruq al-Qaysi narrated to us. He said: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah informed me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies against me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of more than one of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"1060","The thirteenth part of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah of Diya' al-Maqdisi. From the hadith of Abu al-Mundhir Ubayy ibn Ka'b ibn Qays ibn Ubayd ibn Zayd ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Najjari al-Ansari, master of the reciters, who witnessed Badr (may Allah be pleased with him). Musnad of Ubayy ibn Ka'b al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, servant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Ubayy (may Allah be pleased with him) 1126 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us by reading to him while we listened, at al-Harbiyyah. It was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan al-Qati'i informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid who said: Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The roof of my house was opened while I was at Makkah, and Jibril (peace be upon him) descended and opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water, then brought a basin of gold filled with wisdom and faith, poured it into my chest then closed it. Then he took my hand and ascended with me to the heaven. When he came to the lowest heaven he sought opening. He said: Who is this? He said: Jibril. He said: Is anyone with you? He said: Yes, Muhammad is with me. He said: Was he sent for? He said: Yes, so open. When we rose above the lowest heaven, there was a man with black forms to his right and black forms to his left; when he looked toward his right he smiled, and when he looked toward his left he wept. He said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son. He said: I said to Jibril (peace be upon him): Who is this? He said: This is Adam, and these black forms to his right and left are the souls of his children; the people of the right are the people of Paradise, and the black forms to his left are the people of the Fire; when he looks toward his right he laughs, and when he looks toward his left he weeps. He said: Then Jibril ascended with me until he came to the second heaven, and said to its keeper: Open. Its keeper said to him like what the keeper of the lowest heaven said, and opened for him. Anas ibn Malik said: He mentioned that he found in the heavens Adam, Idris, Musa, Isa, and Ibrahim (peace be upon them), though it was not established for me how their stations were, except that he mentioned that he found Adam in the lowest heaven, and Ibrahim in the sixth heaven. Anas said: When Jibril (peace be upon him) and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Idris, he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. He said: I said: Who is this? He said: This is Idris. He said: Then I passed by Musa, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. I said: Who is this? He said: This is Musa. Then I passed by Isa, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. I said: Who is this? He said: This is Isa son of Maryam. He said: Then I passed by Ibrahim, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son. I said: Who is this? He said: This is Ibrahim (peace be upon him). Ibn Shihab said: Ibn Hazm informed me that Ibn Abbas and Abu Habbah al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then I was ascended till I appeared at a level where I heard the scratching of the pens. Ibn Hazm and Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah blessed and exalted obligated upon my nation fifty prayers. He said: I returned with that till I passed by Musa (peace be upon him). Musa said: What did your Lord blessed and exalted obligate upon your nation? I said: He obligated upon them fifty prayers. Musa (peace be upon him) said to me: Return to your Lord blessed and exalted, for your nation cannot bear that. He said: I returned to my Lord mighty and majestic and He removed half of it. I returned to Musa and informed him. He said: Return to your Lord, for your nation cannot bear that. He said: I returned to my Lord mighty and majestic and He said: They are five and they are fifty; the word is not changed with Me. He said: I returned to Musa (peace be upon him) and he said: Return to your Lord. I said: I am shy before my Lord blessed and exalted. He said: Then I was taken till I was brought to the lote-tree of the utmost boundary. He said: Colors covered it I know not what they are. He said: Then I was admitted to Paradise, and therein were domes of pearl, and its soil was musk."
"1061","1127 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us (Ha). 1128 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us by my reading to him at Baghdad. I said to him: Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed you: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: Ubayy used to narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The roof of my house was opened while I was at Makkah, and Jibril (peace be upon him) descended and opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water, then brought a basin of gold filled with wisdom and faith and poured it into my chest, then closed it. The wording is one, except that in Abu Ya'la's narration: And Jibril descended with a basin of gold filled. Al-Daraqutni was asked about the hadith of Anas ibn Malik from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about the Mi'raj, and said: Al-Zuhri narrates it from Anas; Aqil and Yunus narrated it from him, and there is disagreement from Yunus: Abu Damrah said: From Yunus, from Ubayy; and I think Dharr dropped from him, so he made it from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, erring therein. Qatadah narrated this hadith from Anas ibn Malik, from Malik ibn Sa'sa'ah at length. Shu'bah narrated part of it from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the story of the two rivers; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Shu'bah; and it resembles that all the statements are sound, for their narrators are established. I say: Muslim narrated the hadith of the Isra' from Shayban ibn Farrukh, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought the Buraq, mentioning it at length; and with this chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited by Jibril while playing with the boys, and he seized him, threw him down, and split his heart, therein: then washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, then joined it, then returned it to its place. He narrated the hadith of Abu Dharr from Harmalah, from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, from Abu Dharr. He narrated the hadith of Malik ibn Sa'sa'ah from Ibn Muthanna, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Malik. In each hadith is something not in the other, so he brought every narration. The hadith of Abu Dharr resembles the hadith of Ubayy ibn Ka'b which we established, so for that al-Daraqutni said: I think Dharr dropped from him; except that his latter statement to me is preferable, namely his saying: it resembles that all the statements are sound, for their narrators are established. I say: Ubayy’s hadith being like Abu Dharr’s hadith does not affect it; moreover the narration therein is from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, so how would Ibn Ka'b be confused with Dharr? When the narration from Anas is sound, his narration from Abu Dharr from him, and from Malik ibn Sa'sa'ah, then his narration from Ubayy ibn Ka'b is sound, and Allah knows best. We intended from the hadith only the narration of Ubayy ibn Ka'b, for the narration of Anas at its end Muslim mentioned in the narration of Abu Dharr."
"1062","Another. 1129 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: A man recited a verse, and I recited it differently from his recitation. I said: Who taught you this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me. So I set out with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes. The man said: Did you teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes. Then he said: Jibril and Mika'il (peace be upon them) came to me; Jibril sat to my right and Mika'il to my left. Jibril said: O Muhammad, recite the Qur'an upon one letter. Mika'il said: Ask for more. Jibril said: Recite it upon two letters. Mika'il said: Ask for more. So I said to Jibril: Give me more. He said: Recite it upon three letters. Mika'il said: Ask for more, likewise, until it reached seven letters, each time Jibril saying: Recite; and Mika'il saying: Ask for more; until it reached seven letters. He said: Recite it upon seven letters, each healing and sufficient. It was mentioned in the Sahih with a similar hadith, except that in this is mentioned ... and his saying: Each healing and sufficient was not mentioned therein."
"1063","1130 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: A man recited a verse, and I recited it differently from his recitation. I said: Who taught you this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me. I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you teach me such-and-such verse, such-and-such? He said: Yes. The man said: Did you teach me such-and-such verse, such-and-such? He said: Yes. Then he said: Jibril and Mika'il came to me; Jibril sat to my right and Mika'il to my left. Jibril said: O Muhammad, recite the Qur'an upon one letter. Mika'il said: Ask for more. I said: Give me more. He said: Recite it upon two letters. Mika'il said: Ask for more. I said: Give me more. He said: Recite it upon three. Mika'il said: Ask for more, until it reached seven letters, each time Jibril saying: Recite; and Mika'il saying: Ask for more; until it reached seven letters. He said: Recite it upon seven letters, each healing and sufficient."
"1064","Another. 1131 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd Allah - meaning Ibn al-Mubarak - informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I, Ubayy, and Abu Talhah were sitting, and we ate meat and bread. Then I called for ablution water. They said: Why should we perform ablution? I said: For this food we ate. They said: Should we perform ablution for wholesome things? One better than you did not perform ablution for it."
"1065","Jabir ibn Abd Allah ibn Haram al-Ansari, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them) 1132 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf narrated to me, Shabbabah narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, from Abi Sufyan, from Jabir, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized him. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from Bishr ibn Khalid, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah with its chain, from Jabir who said: A man shot Ubayy, making it the musnad of Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"1066","Another. 1133 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar ibn Yahya al-Mu'addib informed us at Dar al-Qazz, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them by reading to him. He said: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us by reading to him. He said: Abu Umar Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Humayd informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khirash narrated to us, Shabbabah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abi Sufyan, from Jabir, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he was asked about the mosque founded upon piety, and he said: It is this mosque of mine. This hadith in the original of Abi Umar is with the correction of Abi al-Abbas al-Fazari, who said: Abu Umar informed me: I saw Ibn Sa'id when doubting something ... with this text; while the preserved with this chain is: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a physician to Ubayy who cauterized him."
"1067","Al-Jarud ibn Sabrah, also said Ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) 1134 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Al-Khuza'i said in his hadith: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said to me."
"1068","1135 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people and omitted a verse. He said: Which of you retained anything of my recitation for me? Ubayy said: I did, O Messenger of Allah; you omitted such-and-such verse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knew, if anyone retained it for me, it is you."
"1069","1136 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Mansur ibn Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from al-Jarud ibn Sabrah al-Hudhali who said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people and omitted a verse. When he finished he said: Did anyone retain anything of the Qur'an for me? Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: Then you omitted such-and-such verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knew, if anyone retained it for me, it is you."
"1070","1137 - Abu Zur'ah Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Muqri' informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people and omitted a verse. He said: Who retained my recitation for me? Ubayy said: I did. He said: I knew, if anyone retained it for me, it is you. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Sulayman ibn Harb."
"1071","Abu Dharr Jundub ibn Junadah al-Ghifari, a Companion, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1138 - Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Asadi al-Dimashqi informed us there, that his grandfather Abu al-Qasim al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ala' al-Missisi informed us. He said: I read to Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Sulayman al-Nasibi, saying to him: Ahmad ibn Yusuf ibn Khallad al-Nasibi informed you, Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us, Sa'id ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Dharr that he said: I entered the mosque on Friday while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching, and I sat near Ubayy ibn Ka'b. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Bara'ah. I said to Ubayy: When was this surah revealed? He frowned at me and did not speak to me. Then I waited a while, then asked him, and he frowned at me and did not speak to me. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished praying, I said to Ubayy: I asked you and you frowned at me and did not speak to me. Ubayy said: You have of your prayer nothing but what idle talk you engaged in. I went to the Prophet and said: O Prophet of Allah, I was beside Ubayy ibn Ka'b while you recited Bara'ah, and I asked: When was this surah revealed? He frowned at me and did not speak to me. He said: You have of your prayer nothing but what idle talk you engaged in. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ubayy spoke the truth. This also enters the musnad of Abu Dharr."
"1072","1139 - Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us: Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayri narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Bara'ah on Friday while standing, reminding of the days of Allah Almighty, with Ubayy ibn Ka'b facing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu al-Darda' and Abu Dharr present. One of them nudged Ubayy ibn Ka'b and said: When was this surah revealed, O Ubayy, for I heard it only now? He signaled to him: Be silent. When they departed he said: I asked you when this surah was revealed and you did not inform me. Ubayy said: You have of your prayer today nothing but what idle talk you engaged in. I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioned that to him, and informed him of what Ubayy said. He said: Ubayy spoke the truth. Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Aban, from Abi Maryam."
"1073","Jundub - I think: Ibn Abd Allah ibn Sufyan al-Bajali al-Alaqi, a Companion - from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1140 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq ibn Asma' al-Jarmi narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us, from Abi Imran al-Jawni: Jundub narrated to us. He said: I came to Madinah seeking knowledge, and people were in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in circles conversing. I moved through the circles until I came to a circle with a pale man wearing two garments, as though newly arrived from travel. I heard him say: By the Lord of the Ka'bah, the people of the knot are ruined, and I feel no sorrow for them. He said it three times. I sat with him, and he spoke what was decreed for him, then stood. When he stood I asked about him, saying: Who is this? They said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b, master of the Muslims. I followed him until he reached his house, which was shabby in dwelling and shabby in clothing, each resembling the other. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting. Then he asked me: From where are you? I said: From the people of Iraq. He said: Most given to asking. When he said that I grew angry, knelt upon my knees, faced the qiblah, raised my hands, and said: O Allah, we complain of them to You; we spend our provisions, weary our bodies, and journey our mounts seeking knowledge, and when we meet them they treat us harshly and speak to us. He said: He kept soothing me, so Ubayy wept and kept soothing me, saying: Woe to you, I did not mean that. Then he said: I promise you, if you keep me till Friday, I shall speak what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without fearing anyone's blame. When he said that I left him, awaiting Friday to hear his speech. When Thursday came I went out for a need, and the streets were crowded with people; I took no street but people met me. I said: What is with the people? They said: We deem you a stranger. I said: Yes. They said: The master of the Muslims, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, has died. I met Abu Musa in Iraq and narrated the hadith to him. He said: Alas, had he remained till the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I think his saying: He returned the greeting, was not in our hearing, and Allah knows best."
"1074","Abu al-Aliyah Rufay' al-Riyahi, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) 1141 - The Imam Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz al-Zahid al-Harbi informed us by reading to him while we listened, at al-Harbiyyah. It was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn al-Shaybani informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Malik al-Qati'i informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min al-Muqri' narrated to me, Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them, reciting a long surah, then bowing five bowings and two prostrations. Then he stood for the second, reciting a long surah, bowing five bowings and prostrating two prostrations. Then he sat as he was, facing the qiblah, supplicating until its eclipse cleared."
"1075","1142 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Adib al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq ibn Asma' al-Jarmi narrated to us. He said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Abu Ja'far al-Razi Isa ibn Abi Isa narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them, reciting a surah from the long ones, then bowing five bowings and prostrating two prostrations. Then he stood for the second, reciting a surah from the long ones, bowing five bowings and prostrating two prostrations. Then he sat as he was, facing the qiblah, supplicating until its eclipse cleared. Abu Ya'la narrated it from Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min, Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us with its chain similarly, but it was not in our hearing. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated it from Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat ibn Khalid al-Razi, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far al-Razi, from Abi Ja'far al-Razi. Abu Dawud said: And I was narrated from Umar ibn Shaqiq, Abu Ja'far narrated to us. Abu Ja'far's name is Isa ibn Mahan."
"1076","Another. 1143 - Abu Isma'il Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Mashadah, and Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them by reading to him while they listened: Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Khalaf al-Maghribi informed us by reading to him: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isa ibn Ubayd, from Rabi' - he is Ibn Anas - from Abi al-Aliyah: Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, he said: On the day of Uhud sixty-four men of the Ansar were struck, and six of the Muhajirun, among them Hamzah, and they were mutilated. The Ansar said: If we gain a day like this over them, we shall surely exceed against them. When the day of the conquest of Makkah came, Allah mighty and majestic revealed: And if you punish, punish with the like of what you were afflicted with; but if you are patient, it is better for the patient. A man said: No Quraysh after today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spare the people except four."
"1077","1144 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Salih Hadiyyah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Marwazi narrated to me, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Isa ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: On the day of Uhud sixty-four men of the Ansar were killed, and six of the Muhajirun. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If we have a day like this over the polytheists, we shall surely exceed against them. When the day of the conquest came, an unknown man said: No Quraysh after today. The crier of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: The black and the white are safe except so-and-so and so-and-so, naming people. Allah Almighty revealed: And if you punish, punish with the like ... but if you are patient, it is better for the patient. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall be patient and not punish. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth in agreement, saying: A good, strange hadith from the hadith of Ubayy. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated it also from Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi, from Abi Tumaylah, from Isa ibn Ubayd similarly. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it like the hadith of al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Fadl ibn Musa."
"1078","Another. 1145 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed us by reading to him while I listened, at Isfahan. It was said to him: Abu Sa'd Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Naysaburi, who came to you at Isfahan, informed you: Abu Hafs Umar ibn Shah ibn al-Husayn al-Muqri' al-Sawwaf informed us, al-Sayyid Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hasani informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Sharqi informed us, and Abu Ali al-Hafiz conveyed it to me from him, Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came to Madinah and the Ansar sheltered them, the Arabs shot at them from a single bow. They would not pass the night except in arms, nor rise in the morning except likewise. They said: Do you think we shall live till we pass a night safe and secure, fearing none but Allah mighty and majestic? Allah mighty and majestic revealed: Allah has promised those who believe among you and do righteous deeds that He shall grant them succession in the land as He granted succession to those before them, and shall establish for them their religion which He approved for them, and shall change them after their fear to security; they worship Me, associating nothing with Me; and whoever disbelieves after that, meaning after the blessing, then they are the defiantly disobedient."
"1079","1146 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed me at Isfahan, that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim informed them by reading to him: Ahmad al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa al-Hafiz informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Khadir al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, the Arabs shot at them from a single bow. They would not pass the night except in arms. They said: Do you think a night shall come upon us in which we pass the night calm and secure, fearing none but Allah? Allah revealed: Allah has promised those who believe among you and do righteous deeds that He shall grant them succession in the land ... the verse."
"1080","Another. 1147 - Abu al-Ala' Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja' ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahani informed us by ijazah, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by reading to him: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us. He said: Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Thaqafi informed me, Sulayman ibn Amir narrated to us. He said: I heard al-Rabi' ibn Anas say: I read to Abi al-Aliyah, and Abu al-Aliyah read to Ubayy ibn Ka'b. He said: Ubayy said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I was commanded to recite the Qur'an to you. I said: Was I mentioned there? He said: Yes. Ubayy wept. He said: I know not whether from longing or fear."
"1081","1148 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Sa'adat ibn Tirad informed us at Baghdad, that the Imam Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Nasir al-Salami informed them by reading to him: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abi al-Saqr al-Anbari informed us, Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Maymun ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghaffar al-Sadafi informed us by my reading; I said to him: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh informed you, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali ibn Bahr al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Sulayman ibn Amir narrated to us. He said: I heard al-Rabi' ibn Anas say: I read the Qur'an to Abi al-Aliyah, and Abu al-Aliyah read to Ubayy. He said: Ubayy said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I was commanded to recite the Qur'an to you. He said: I said: Was I mentioned there? He said: Yes, so Ubayy wept; I know not whether from longing or fear. So al-Nasa'i narrated it in Fada'il al-Qur'an."
"1082","Another. 1149 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us by my reading to him at Baghdad. I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Abu Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Rabi', from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b concerning His saying, blessed and exalted: He is Able to send punishment upon you from above you, the verse. He said: They are four, all punishment, all inevitably occurring. Two passed after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by twenty-five years: they were made into factions and tasted one another's might. Two remain, inevitably occurring: sinking and stoning."
"1083","1150 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib informed us at Isfahan, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi', from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b: He is Able to send punishment upon you from above you, or from beneath your feet, or make you into factions and make some taste the might of others. He said: They are four traits. He said: Two of them came after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by twenty-five: they were made into factions, and some tasted the might of others. Two remain, inevitably occurring: stoning and sinking."
"1084","Another. 1151 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Zahid al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us. 1152 - ... And Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas. Abd al-Wahid said in his hadith: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Give this nation glad tidings of splendor, victory, and establishment; whoever of them does a deed of the Hereafter for the world shall have no share in the Hereafter."
"1085","1153 - And with it Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzar narrated to me, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give this nation glad tidings of splendor and establishment in the lands, victory and elevation in religion; whoever of them does a deed of the Hereafter for the world shall have no share in the Hereafter. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Abd al-Razzaq, from Sufyan, from Abi Salamah Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim. Abd Allah narrated it from Abi al-Sha'tha' Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti, from Yahya ibn Yaman, from Sufyan, from Mughirah al-Sarraj, from al-Rabi'."
"1086","1154 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki al-Razi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Mu'tamir informed us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to me, from al-Mughirah Abi Salamah, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give this nation glad tidings of splendor, elevation in religion, victory and establishment in the land; whoever of them seeks the world by a deed of the Hereafter shall have no share in the Hereafter."
"1087","Another. 1155 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min narrated to me, Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b: that they gathered the Qur'an into codices in the caliphate of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him); men would write while Ubayy ibn Ka'b dictated to them. When they reached this verse of surah Bara'ah: Then they turned away; Allah turned their hearts because they are a people who do not understand, they thought this was the last revealed of the Qur'an. Ubayy ibn Ka'b said to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to me after it two verses: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves, grievous to him is what you suffer, eager for you, to the believers kind and merciful, to: And He is Lord of the Mighty Throne. He said: This is the last revealed of the Qur'an. He said: So he sealed what he began with: Allah, besides Whom there is no god; and it is the saying of Allah blessed and exalted: And We sent no Messenger before you but We revealed to him that there is no god but I, so worship Me."
"1088","1156 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shukr al-Tamimi informed us at Isfahan, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi and Abu Yahya al-Za'farani narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'd al-Dashtaki narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us. He said: My father narrated to me, from al-Rabi', from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b: that they gathered the Qur'an into codices in the caliphate of Abu Bakr; men would write while Ubayy ibn Ka'b dictated to them. When they reached this verse of surah Bara'ah: Then they turned away; Allah turned their hearts because they are a people who do not understand, they thought this was the last revealed of the Qur'an. Ubayy ibn Ka'b said to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to me after it two verses: There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves ... So if they turn away, say: Allah suffices me; there is no god but He; upon Him I rely, and He is Lord of the Mighty Throne. He said: This is the last revealed of the Qur'an. He said: So he sealed the matter with what he began with: There is no god but Allah; Allah says: And We sent no Messenger before you but We revealed to him that there is no god but I, so worship Me."
"1089","Another. 1157 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us by my reading to him on the western side of Baghdad. I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed you by reading to him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hadiyyah ibn Abd al-Wahhab and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to me, both saying: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b: They call upon none besides Him but females. He said: With every idol is a female jinn."
"1090","Another. 1158 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Zahid informed us by reading to him while we listened, at al-Harbiyyah. It was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you by reading to him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Rabbali narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us. He said: I heard my father narrate from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Rufay' Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b concerning the saying of Allah mighty and majestic: And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their loins, their offspring. He said: He gathered them and made them souls, then fashioned them and made them speak, and they spoke. Then He took upon them the covenant and pact, and made them bear witness against themselves: Am I not your Lord? He said: I make the seven heavens and the seven earths bear witness against you, and I make your father Adam (peace be upon him) bear witness against you, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: We knew nothing of this. Know that there is no god besides Me and no lord besides Me, so associate nothing with Me. I shall send to you My messengers reminding you of My covenant and pact, and reveal to you My books. They said: We bear witness that You are our Lord and our God; we have no lord besides You, no god besides us besides You. So they affirmed that, and Adam was raised above them looking on. He saw the rich and the poor, the handsome and otherwise. He said: O Lord, why did You not make Your servants equal? He said: I wished to be thanked. He saw the prophets among them like lamps upon them light, singled out with another covenant in message and prophethood, and it is His saying, blessed and exalted: And when We took from the prophets their covenant, to His saying: And Isa son of Maryam. He was among those souls, and He sent him to Maryam; he narrated from Ubayy that he entered through her mouth."
"1091","1159 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shukr al-Mu'addib al-Asbahani informed us there, that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar informed them by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us. He said: I read to Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b concerning His saying: And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their loins, their offspring, and made them bear witness against themselves: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, to His saying: Shall You destroy us for what the falsifiers did. He said: He gathered them for him that day, all that shall be till the Day of Resurrection, made them pairs, then fashioned them, then made them speak and they spoke, took upon them the covenant and pact, and made them bear witness against themselves: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we bear witness, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: We were heedless of this. He said: I make the seven heavens and the seven earths bear witness against you, and I make your father Adam bear witness against you, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: We knew nothing of this. Know that there is no god besides Me and no lord besides Me, so associate nothing with Me. I shall send to you My messengers reminding you of My covenant and pact, and reveal to you My books. They said: We bear witness that You are our Lord and our God; we have no lord besides You, no god besides us besides You. So they affirmed obedience to Him that day. He raised above them their father Adam, who looked at them and saw among them the rich and the poor, the handsome and otherwise. He said: O Lord, had You wished You could have made Your servants equal. He said: I wished to be thanked. He saw among them the prophets like lamps upon them light, singled out with another covenant in message and prophethood, and it is what He says: And when We took from the prophets their covenant, and from you, and from Nuh, Ibrahim, Musa, and Isa son of Maryam, and We took from them a solemn covenant. And it is His saying: The nature of Allah upon which He fashioned people; and concerning that He said: This is a warner from the warners of old; and concerning that He said: And We found most of them with no covenant, and We found most of them defiantly disobedient; and concerning that He said: Then We sent after him messengers to their people, and they brought them clear proofs, but they would not believe in what they had denied before. It was in His knowledge the day they affirmed what they affirmed, who denies it and who affirms it."
"1092","1160 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us at Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b concerning His saying: And when We took from the prophets their covenant, and from you, and from Nuh. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of them is Nuh, then the first, then the first."
"1093","Another. 1161 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, al-Hasan ibn Musa informed us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b: that Umar ordered Ubayy to lead the people in prayer in Ramadan. He said: People fast the day but cannot recite well; if you would recite the Qur'an to them at night. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, this is something that was not. He said: I know, but it is better. So he prayed with them twenty rak'ahs."
"1094","Zirr ibn Hubaysh al-Asadi Abu Maryam al-Kufi, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) 1162 - The Hafiz Imam Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us in his book, that Abu al-Qasim Ghanim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Ayyub ibn Ziyad al-Burji informed them by reading to him: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us. He said: Asim ibn Bahdalah informed me, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah blessed and exalted commanded me to recite the Qur'an to you. He said: So he recited to him: Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book; and recited to him: The religion with Allah is the easy Hanifiyyah, neither polytheist nor Jewish nor Christian; and whoever does good shall never be denied it. And he recited to him: Had the son of Adam a valley, he would seek a second to it; and had he been given a second, he would seek a third to it; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"1095","1163 - Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah blessed and exalted commanded me to recite the Qur'an to you. He said: So he recited: Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book. He said: And he recited therein: Had the son of Adam asked for a valley of wealth and been given it, he would ask for a second; and had he asked for a second and been given it, he would ask for a third; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents; and the religion with Allah is the Hanifiyyah, neither polytheist nor Jewish nor Christian; and whoever does good shall never be denied it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it similarly from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, saying: A good, sound hadith. Al-Bukhari narrated in his Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Shihab, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had the son of Adam two valleys of gold, he would love to have two valleys; and nothing shall fill his mouth but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents. Anas said: From Ubayy who said: We deemed this part of the Qur'an until: Rivalry diverted you, was revealed."
"1096","Another. 1164 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr who said: I asked Ubayy ibn Ka'b about the verse of stoning. He said: How many do you count surah al-Ahzab? I said: Seventy-three or seventy-four verses. He said: It used to nearly equal surah al-Baqarah or longer, and therein was the verse of stoning: The old man and the old woman, stone them as a deterrent from Allah; and Allah is Mighty, Wise."
"1097","1165 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us at Isfahan, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Yahya ibn Abi Busrah narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: Surah al-Ahzab used to equal surah al-Baqarah, and therein was the verse of stoning: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them outright. Hammad ibn Zayd, Hammad ibn Salamah, Abu Awanah, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb, and Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated it from Asim."
"1098","1166 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr who said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said to me: How many do you recite surah al-Ahzab? Or: How many do you count it? He said: I said to him: Seventy-three verses. He said: Ever? I saw it, and it equaled surah al-Baqarah; and we recited therein: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them outright as a deterrent from Allah; and Allah is Knowing, Wise. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim, from Hafs, from Mansur, from Asim similarly. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim similarly, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Asim."
"1099","Another. 1167 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir informed us, Abu Mu'ammar al-Qati'i narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a bier has a qirat, whoever witnesses it till burial has two qirats, and whoever eats of this herb shall not approach our mosque. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani but Jarir."
"1100","Another. 1168 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah informed us, my grandfather Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Jibril (peace be upon him) and said: O Jibril, I was sent to a nation among whom are the old woman, the aged elder, the boy, the girl, and the man who never read a book at all. He said: O Muhammad, the Qur'an was revealed upon seven letters."
"1101","1169 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Jibril at the stones of al-Mira'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent to an unlettered nation, among them the elder, the old woman, the girl, and the Persian man who never read anything at all. He said: Jibril (peace be upon him) said to him: The Qur'an descended upon seven letters. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani', saying: A good, sound hadith. The mention of seven letters was mentioned in the Sahih, but what precedes it was not mentioned."
"1102","Another. 1170 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir informed us, Abu Mu'ammar al-Qati'i narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a bier has a qirat, whoever witnesses it till burial has two qirats, and whoever eats of this herb shall not approach our mosque. Sulayman said: None narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani but Jarir."
"1103","Ziyad al-Ansari, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) 1171 - Ubayd Allah al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind who said: Muhammad ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, from Ziyad - a man of the Ansar - who said: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: What if the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had died, would he have been permitted to marry? He said: What would forbid that to him? Sometimes Dawud said: What prevents him from that? He said: I said: His saying: Women are not lawful to you after this. He said: He permitted him only a kind of women, saying: O Prophet, We have permitted to you your wives, reciting till he reached: Women are not lawful to you after this."
"1104","1172 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Umar informed them: Yazid ibn Zuray' and Abd al-A'la narrated to us, both saying: Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Musa, from Ziyad al-Ansari who said: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: Had all the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, would it be lawful for him to marry? He said: What would forbid that to him? He said: I said: For His saying: Women are not lawful to you after this. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was permitted only a kind of women."
"1105","Sulayman ibn Surad al-Khuza'i, a Companion, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1173 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: I recited a verse, and Ibn Mas'ud recited differently. We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Did you not teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes. Ibn Mas'ud said: Did you not teach it to me so-and-so? He said: Yes, both of you are good and right. He said: I said to him, and he struck my chest, saying: O Ubayy ibn Ka'b, I was taught the Qur'an, and it was said to me: Upon one letter or upon two letters? The angel with me said: Upon two letters. I said: Upon two letters. He said: Upon two or three? The angel with me said: Upon three. I said: Upon three, till it reached seven letters, none but healing and sufficient; if you say Forgiving, Merciful, or say Hearing, Knowing, or Knowing, Hearing, Allah is so, so long as you do not seal a verse of punishment with mercy, or a verse of mercy with punishment."
"1106","1174 - And with it Abd Allah narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid al-Qaysi narrated to me, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: I recited a verse, Ibn Mas'ud recited differently, and another man recited differently. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"1107","1175 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili narrated to us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Sulayman ibn Surad who said: Ubayy recited a verse, Ibn Mas'ud recited a verse differently, and another man recited differently from both. Ubayy said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Did you not teach me such-and-such verse? Ibn Mas'ud said: Did you not teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes, all of you are good and right. Ubayy said: He struck my chest and said: O Ubayy, I recited the Qur'an upon one letter, and said: Or two letters? The angel with me said: Upon two letters. I said: Upon two or three? The angel with me said to me: Rather upon three. I said: Upon three, and it remained so till it reached seven letters, none but healing and sufficient; if you say Forgiving, Merciful, or say: Mighty, Wise, or say: Hearing, Knowing, whichever you say, Allah is so. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated it from Abi al-Walid, from Hammam similarly. We brought it out only for his saying: Healing and sufficient, to its end, for it was not mentioned in the Sahih."
"1108","1176 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid informed us, Ubayd Allah informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us. He said: Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani informed me, from Sulayman ibn Surad, that Ubayy ibn Ka'b brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two men differing in recitation, each saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had them recite, and they recited. He said to them: You did well. Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: Doubt entered me such as I had in Jahiliyyah. I said: You did well?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck my chest and said: O Allah, remove Satan from him. He said: I broke into sweat, as though looking at Allah mighty and majestic in fear. Then he said: Jibril came to me and said: Recite the Qur'an upon seven letters, each healing and sufficient. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani, from Yazid similarly. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from Isra'il, from Abi Ishaq, from Suqayr al-Abdi, from Sulayman ibn Surad, adding in its chain Suqayr. Therein are wordings not in the Sahih, among them the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him, his saying healing and sufficient, and other than that, and Allah knows best."
"1109","Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, a Companion, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1177 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Mutarrif Abi Ghassan, from Abi Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd: Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that the fatwa they used to give: Water is from water, was a concession the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed at the beginning of time, then he commanded bathing afterwards."
"1110","1178 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us. He said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The fatwa concerning water from water was but a concession in the beginning of Islam, then it was forbidden. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Uthman ibn Umar; and from Ali ibn Ishaq, from Ibn al-Mubarak, both from Yunus; and from Abi al-Yaman, from Shu'ayb, from al-Zuhri. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal; and from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Abd Allah ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Shihab who said: One whom I approve narrated to me that Sahl informed him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani', saying: A good, sound hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Uthman ibn Umar, from Yunus ibn Yazid. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Mihran."
"1111","Al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1179 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Hashim ibn al-Harith and Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-Qurashi narrated to us, both saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, I shall be the imam of the prophets, their spokesman, and the holder of their intercession, without boast. And he said: Were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar; and had the Ansar taken a valley or a path, I would be with the Ansar."
"1112","1180 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Abu al-Qasim Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them by reading to him: Abu Amir al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Nasawi al-Qumasi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn al-Muqri' informed us by reading to him at Isfahan: Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Abi Ma'shar al-Harrani informed us, Bundar narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us. 1181 - Abu Arubah said: And Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Abi al-Zard narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Had people taken a valley or a path, I would be with the Ansar; I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar."
"1113","1182 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar."
"1114","1183 - And with it: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, I shall be the imam of the prophets, their spokesman, and the holder of their intercession, without boast. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar; and had people taken a valley or a path, I would be with the Ansar. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abi Amir. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abi Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr al-Aqadi, except that he made it two hadiths: in the first to his saying without boast he said: A good, sound hadith; and in his saying: Were it not for the Hijrah, a good hadith. Ibn Majah narrated the first from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-Raqqi, from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi similarly."
"1115","Another. 1184 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father who said: When a quarter of the night had gone, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand and say: O people, remember Allah; the quaking has come, followed by the following; death has come with what is in it, death has come with what is in it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Qabisah, saying: A good hadith."
"1116","1185 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani al-Razi informed us, Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: When a quarter of the night had gone, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand and say: O people, remember Allah, remember Allah; the quaking has come, followed by the following; death has come with what is in it, death has come with what is in it, death has come with what is in it. Ubayy said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send many blessings upon you; how much of my prayer shall I devote to you? He said: What you wish. He said: A quarter? He said: What you wish, and if you add it is better. He said: Half? He said: What you wish, and if you add it is better. He said: Two-thirds? He said: What you wish, and if you add it is better. He said: Shall I devote all my prayer to you? He said: Then your concern shall be sufficed and your sin forgiven."
"1117","1186 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The quaking has come, followed by the following; death has come with what is in it."
"1118","1187 - And with it, from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I devote all my prayer to you? He said: Then Allah blessed and exalted shall suffice you what concerns you of your world and Hereafter."
"1119","1188 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah informed us, my grandfather Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send many blessings upon you; how much of my prayer shall I devote to you? He said: What you wish. I said: A quarter? He said: What you wish, and if you add it is better. I said: Half? He said: What you wish, and if you add it is better. I said: Two-thirds? He said: What you wish, and if you add it is better. I said: Shall I devote all my prayer to you? He said: Then your concern shall be sufficed and your sin forgiven for you. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Qabisah ibn Uqbah."
"1120","Another. 1189 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness among the prophets is the likeness of a man who built a house and perfected it, leaving a brick; I am that brick."
"1121","1190 - Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Amir narrated to us, both saying: Zuhayr - meaning Ibn Muhammad - narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: My likeness among the prophets is like a man who built a house, perfected and completed it, leaving the place of a brick unplaced; people go round the building, admiring it and saying: Had the place of this brick been completed; I among the prophets am the place of that brick."
"1122","1191 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Fannaki informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness among the prophets is like a man who built a house, beautified, adorned and completed it, leaving the place of a brick; people go round the building, marveling at it and saying: Had the place of that brick been completed; I am their spokesman and the holder of their intercession, without boast. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated it from Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath ibn Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman, from Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad similarly. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abi Amir similarly, saying: A good, sound hadith. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"1123","Another. 1192 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid and Isa ibn Salim both narrated to us, both saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward a trunk when the mosque was a thatch, and he would preach leaning to that trunk. One of his Companions said: Shall we make for you something upon which you stand on Friday so people see you and hear your sermon? He said: Yes. So three steps were made for him, which are the uppermost of the pulpit. When the pulpit was made and placed where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to stand upon the pulpit, he passed by the trunk to which he used to preach. When he passed the trunk it moaned till it cracked and split. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), hearing the trunk's voice, descended and wiped it with his hand till it calmed. Then he returned to the pulpit; when he prayed he prayed toward it. When the mosque was demolished and altered, Ubayy ibn Ka'b took the trunk, keeping it in his house till it decayed, eaten by termites, returning to dust. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Zakariyya ibn Adi, from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr similarly. His son Abd Allah narrated it from Isa ibn Salim; and from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman, from Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, with: It had three steps which are the uppermost of the pulpit. Ibn Majah narrated it from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Umar and Jabir, with routes from more than one of the Companions."
"1124","Another. 1193 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali ibn al-Ma'tush informed us at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: While we were in rows behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr or Asr, we saw him reaching for something before him while in prayer to take it, then reaching to take it, then it was kept from him. Then he stepped back and we stepped back; then he stepped back a second time and we stepped back. When he gave salam, Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you today do in your prayer something you never did! He said: Paradise with its blossom and verdure was shown to me, and I reached for a cluster of its grapes to bring to you; had I taken it, all between heaven and earth would eat of it without diminishing it. I was kept from it. The Fire was shown to me; when I felt the heat of its flame I stepped back. Most whom I saw therein were women who, if entrusted, disclose; if they ask, they press importunately. My father said: Zakariyya ibn Adi said: Pester; if given, they are ungrateful. I saw therein Luhayy ibn Amr dragging his entrails; the one I saw most resembling him is Ma'bad ibn Aktham. Ma'bad said: O Messenger of Allah, is harm feared for me from resembling him, for he is a forefather? He said: No, you are a believer and he is a disbeliever; he is the first who gathered the Arabs upon idols."
"1125","1194 - And with it, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah - meaning Ibn Amr - narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"1126","Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir al-Abdi al-Kufi and his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1195 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf, both at Baghdad, informed us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Ma'mun informed us, Ali - he is Ibn Umar al-Harbi - informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad - he is Ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Basri, minister of al-Rashid - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir, from his father (Ha). 1196 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them at Isfahan: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir who said: I was with Ubayy ibn Ka'b during his illness, and he heard the caller with the adhan. He said: Is this the adhan or the iqamah? We said: The iqamah. He said: What are you waiting for? Will you not rise to your prayer? We said: Nothing keeps us but your place. He said: Do not do so; rise. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us Fajr; when he gave salam he faced the people and said: Is so-and-so present, till he called three, all in their homes, not attending. He said: The heaviest prayer upon the hypocrites is Fajr and Isha'; had they known what is in them they would come to them even crawling. Know that your prayer with a man is better than your prayer alone, and your prayer with two men is better than your prayer with a man; and the more, the more beloved to Allah. Know that the foremost row is like the row of the angels; had you known its merit you would hasten to it. Know that the congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-four or twenty-five degrees. The wording of Muhammad ibn Muhammad's hadith. In al-Ruyani's narration: Is this the iqamah or the adhan? With him: Will you not rise to the prayer? We said: Nothing keeps us but your place. He said: Then do not do so. With him: Till he called three. With him: And the more, the more beloved; I think (was) dropped; the rest is the same."
"1127","1197 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, I heard Aba Ishaq that he heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir narrate from Ubayy ibn Ka'b that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Subh and said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: These two prayers are among the heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites; had they known what is in them they would come to them even crawling; the foremost row is like the row of the angels; had you known its merit you would hasten to it; a man's prayer with a man is purer than his prayer alone; his prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with a man; and the more, the more beloved to Allah blessed and exalted. So Imam Ahmad narrated it. He narrated it from Waki', from Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from Shu'bah, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Allah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b."
"1128","1198 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us Fajr; when he gave salam he said: Is so-and-so present? They said: Yes, though he had not attended; he said it thrice. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heaviest prayer upon the hypocrites is Isha' and Fajr; had they known what is in them they would come to them even crawling; the first row is like the row of the angels; had you known its merit you would hasten to it; your prayer with a man is purer than your prayer alone; your prayer with two men is purer than your prayer with a man; and the more, the more beloved to Allah mighty and majestic."
"1129","1199 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us at Baghdad, that his father Abu Mansur Ali ibn Ali informed them by reading to him: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us, Abd Allah, he is al-Baghawi, narrated to us, Ali - he is Ibn al-Ja'd - narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir, from his father who said: I came to Madinah and met Ubayy ibn Ka'b. I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, narrate to me the most wondrous hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us, or said: prayed for us, the morning prayer, then said: Is so-and-so present? We said: Yes, though he had not attended the prayer. He said: The heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites are Isha' and Fajr; had you known what is in them you would come to them even crawling; the first row is like the row of the angels; had you known its merit you would hasten to it; your prayer with a man is purer than your prayer alone; your prayer with two men is purer than your prayer with a man; and the more, the more beloved to Allah mighty and majestic. Abu Dawud narrated it from Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi, from Shu'bah, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir, from Ubayy. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar al-Bahrani, from Abu Bakr Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir, from his father in part. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shu'bah, from Abi Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Basir, from his father, from Ubayy. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abi Khalifah, from Muhammad ibn Kathir similarly."
"1130","1200 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them - by ijazah if not by hearing: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Shayban narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abi Basir al-Abdi, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b that he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the morning prayer, then said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No, till he asked about three men, none attending the prayer. He said: No prayer is heavier upon the hypocrites than these two prayers; had they known what is in them they would come to them even crawling; the first row is like the row of the angels; had you known its merit you would hasten to it; a man's prayer with a man is purer than his prayer alone; his prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with a man; and the more, the more beloved to Allah mighty and majestic."
"1131","1201 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed me, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Abi Basir who said: Ubayy said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us Fajr; when he finished the prayer he saw few people of the mosque. He said: Is so-and-so present? We said: Yes, till he counted three men. He said: No prayer is heavier upon the hypocrites than the last Isha' prayer and the Fajr prayer. He mentioned the hadith at length."
"1132","Abd Allah ibn Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, ally of Banu Zuhrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) 1202 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Zubayr informed me. He said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrate from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, that Abd Allah ibn Khabbab narrated to him from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: His eye is red as though a green glass. Al-Bukhari said in his Tarikh: And Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar said, Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, mentioning with its chain from Ubayy: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal; his eye is green."
"1133","1203 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri' al-Razi informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki al-Razi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The Dajjal's eye is green like glass; and we seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."
"1134","1204 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafiyan informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Zubayr informed me. He said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrate from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Shu'bah as Bundar narrated it."
"1135","1205 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Harrani informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Rawh narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr. He said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl. Rawh said: al-Anazi narrate from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Rawh said in his hadith: Abd Allah ibn Khabbab narrated to him from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Dajjal was mentioned before him, and he said: His eye is green like glass; so seek refuge from the punishment of the grave. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi', from Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from Shu'bah."
"1136","Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1206 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah informed us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from Abi Habib ibn Ya'la ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas (Ha). 1207 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us. He said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to me. He said: Mis'ar narrated to me, from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from Abi Habib ibn Ya'la ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to Umar and said: The hyena has eaten us - Mis'ar said: The hyena is the year of drought. He asked: Of whom is he? He informed him, and he kept tracing his lineage till he knew him, and he was wealthy. Umar said: Had a man two valleys, he would seek a third to them. Ibn Abbas said: Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns thereafter to whoever repents. Umar said to Ibn Abbas: From whom did you hear this? He said: From Ubayy ibn Ka'b. He said: In the morning come to me. Ibn Abbas returned to his mother Umm al-Fadl and mentioned that to her. She said: What have you to do with speaking before Umar? Ibn Abbas feared Ubayy might have forgotten. His mother said to him: Ubayy may not have forgotten. In the morning he went to Umar with the staff. They came to Ubayy, who came out to them having performed ablution. He said: I experienced madhiy, so I washed my private part and performed ablution. Umar said: Does that suffice? He said: Yes. He said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: And he asked him about what Ibn Abbas said, and he affirmed it. The wording is Abu Hammam's; in Ahmad's narration: Umar asked him: Of whom are you? He kept tracing his lineage; with him: a valley or two valleys; with him: and nothing fills; then Allah turns to whoever repents; with him: he said: from Ubayy; with him: he returned to his mother; with him: in the morning he went to Umar with the staff, and they set out to Ubayy; with him: my private part - Mis'ar doubted - Umar said: Does it suffice? The rest is like it."
"1137","1208 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Fannaki informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to me, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from Abi Habib ibn Ya'la ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b that he experienced madhiy, washed his private part and performed ablution. Umar said to him: Does that suffice? He said: Yes. He said: And did you hear it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Muhammad ibn Bishr similarly."
"1138","1209 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abi Mu'awiyah, from Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to Umar asking him; Umar kept looking at his head then at his feet, whether he saw any sign of misery upon him. Then Umar said to him: How much is your wealth? He said: Forty camels. Ibn Abbas said: I said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth: Had the son of Adam two valleys of gold, he would seek a third; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents. Umar said: What is this? I said: So Ubayy taught it to me. He said: Take us to him. They came to Ubayy. He said: What says this? Ubayy said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me; shall I affirm it? He said: Yes, so affirm it. Al-Bukhari said in Kitab al-Riqaq: Abu al-Walid said to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had the son of Adam, the hadith. Anas said: From Ubayy who said: We deemed this part of the Qur'an till: Rivalry diverted you, was revealed. Though not a ta'liq, in this narration is his saying: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me, which is not in al-Bukhari's narration."
"1139","Another. 1210 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that Abu al-Muzahhar Abd al-Mun'im ibn Ahmad ibn Ya'qub ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi and Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to both: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Sulayman ibn Isa al-Jawhari and Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father informed us. He said: I heard Ayyub narrate from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when Jibril (peace be upon him) struck Zamzam with his heel, Umm Isma'il began gathering the gravel. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Hajar - or Umm Isma'il - had she left it, it would have been a flowing spring."
"1140","1211 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Sha'ir narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to me, I asked him, my father narrated to us. He said: I heard Ayyub narrate from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that when Jibril struck Zamzam with his heel, Umm Isma'il began gathering the gravel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Hajar, Umm Isma'il; had she left it, it would have been a flowing spring. Al-Bukhari narrated this hadith from Ahmad ibn Sa'id, from Wahb ibn Jarir, from his father, from Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, without mentioning Ubayy. He said: Ali ibn al-Madini and Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir both narrated it from Wahb, from his father, from Ayyub, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this, omitting Abd Allah ibn Sa'id and adding Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Wahb said: I said to my father: Hammad does not mention Ubayy ibn Ka'b nor raise it. He said: I retain it thus; so Ayyub dictated it. Therein is more speech than this. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ahmad ibn Sa'id with its chain as al-Bukhari narrated, and I think he mentioned Ubayy; and from Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Sayf, from Ali ibn al-Madini, from Wahb with its chain from Ubayy. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Salih al-Bukhari, from Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir with its chain from Ubayy ibn Ka'b."
"1141","Another. 1212 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd and Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Harbiyan informed us - by reading to both while we listened, at al-Harbiyyah. It was said to both: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays. Affan said in his hadith: al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, from Nubayh, from Ibn Abbas, that Ubayy said to Umar: O Commander of the Faithful, I received the Qur'an from one who received it. Affan said: From one who receives it from Jibril (peace be upon him), while it is fresh."
"1142","Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Ubayy (may Allah be pleased with them). 1213 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And for pregnant women their term is to lay down their burden ... Is it for the thrice-divorced or for the widow? He said: It is for the thrice-divorced and for the widow."
"1143","1214 - Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi informed us, from al-Muthanna, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And for pregnant women their term is to lay down their burden - for the thrice-divorced or for the widow? He said: It is for the thrice-divorced and for the widow."
"1144","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza al-Khuza'i, freedman of Nafi' ibn Abd al-Harith, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) 1215 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us by my reading to him on the western side of Baghdad. I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from al-A'mash (Ha). 1216 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us by my reading to him at Isfahan. I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Talhah and Zubayd, from Zirr, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One."
"1145","1217 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us by my reading to him at Isfahan. I said: Abu al-Faraj Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed you - by ijazah if not by hearing: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali al-Muqri' informed us, Abdan narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One, and would supplicate qunut before bowing. Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah both narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi. Ibn Majah narrated: He would perform witr and supplicate qunut before bowing, from Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi."
"1146","1218 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan al-Attar informed us (Ha). 1219 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us at Baghdad, that Abd al-Khaliq ibn Abd al-Rahman ... ibn al-Ma'mun both said: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Harbi informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi informed us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zubayd and Talhah, from Dharr, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One. Abu Hatim al-Busti, from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar."
"1147","Another. 1220 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Talhah al-Iyami, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One; and when he gave salam he would say: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times."
"1148","1221 - Abu al-Fath Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Hurfi informed us in his book from Isfahan, that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them by reading to him: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform witr with three rak'ahs: reciting in the first: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High; in the second: Say: O disbelievers; in the third: Say: He is Allah, One; and would supplicate qunut before bowing. When finished he would say at his finishing: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times, prolonging the last of them. So al-Nasa'i brought it out. Abu Dawud brought out that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he gave salam in witr, would say: Glory be to the King, the Holy, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah."
"1149","Another. 1222 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to me, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza. 1223 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Zahid al-Harbi informed us by reading to him while we listened, at al-Harbiyyah. It was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me, Asbat ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not revile the wind; when you see of it what you dislike, say: O Allah, we ask You of the good of this wind, the good within it, and the good it was sent with; and we seek refuge with You from the evil of this wind, the evil within it, and the evil it was sent with."
"1150","1224 - And with it Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Kufi narrated to me, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Dharr ibn Abd Allah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the wind, for it is from the breeze of Allah blessed and exalted; ask Allah its good, the good within it, and the good it was sent with; and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, the evil within it, and the evil it was sent with."
"1151","1225 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us at Damascus, that Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tha'labi informed them by reading to him: Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us, Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i informed us, Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: A wind raged and a man reviled it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile it; ask Allah its good, the good within it, and the good it was sent with; and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, the evil within it, and the evil it was sent with. So al-Nasa'i brought it out in Kitab Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah. He and al-Tirmidhi both narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from al-A'mash, from Habib, from Dharr, from Sa'id, from his father, al-Tirmidhi saying: A good, sound hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it therein from Ibn al-Muthanna in agreement, without Dharr therein. He narrated it also therein from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from Jarir; and from Ibn al-Muthanna, from Yahya ibn Hammad, both from al-A'mash, from Habib, from Dharr, from Sa'id, from his father, from Ubayy as his saying. And from Bundar, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Shu'bah, from Habib, from Dharr, from Sa'id, from his father; and from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Shu'bah, from Habib, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ubayy as his saying, without raising it."
"1152","Another. 1226 - Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to recite the Qur'an to you. He said: I said: And did your Lord name me to you? He said: Yes. He said: So he recited to me: Say: In Allah's bounty and His mercy, in that let them rejoice; it is better than what they gather."
"1153","1227 - Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ajlah, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah blessed and exalted commanded me to present the Qur'an to you. He said: And did my Lord name me to you, blessed and exalted? He said: In Allah's bounty and His mercy, in that let them rejoice. So Ubayy recited it."
"1154","1228 - And with it my father narrated to me, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Aslam al-Minqari narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ubayy, I was commanded to recite to you such-and-such surah. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was I mentioned there? He said: Yes. He said: I said to him: O Abu al-Mundhir, did you rejoice at that? He said: What prevents me, while Allah blessed and exalted says: Say: In Allah's bounty and His mercy, in that let them rejoice; it is better than what they gather. Mu'ammal said: I said to Sufyan: Is this recitation in the hadith? He said: Yes. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, from al-Mughirah ibn Salamah, from Ibn al-Mubarak; and from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Sufyan."
"1155","Another. 1229 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer and omitted a verse, with Ubayy ibn Ka'b among the people. He said: O Messenger of Allah, did you forget such-and-such verse, or was it abrogated? He said: I was made to forget it."
"1156","1230 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn al-Tarrah and Abu al-Fadl Shuja' ibn Salim ibn Ali ibn Salamah al-Baytar informed us at Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Ma'mun informed us, al-Daraqutni informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Nayruz al-Anmati narrated to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Dharr, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forgot a verse of Allah's Book, with Ubayy among the people. He said: O Messenger of Allah, did you forget such-and-such verse or forget it? He said: Rather I was made to forget it. Al-Daraqutni said: Strange from the hadith of al-Thawri from Salamah ibn Kuhayl; none attributed it from Ubayy ibn Ka'b but Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan. It was narrated from Ishaq al-Azraq, from al-Thawri, mursal and musnad."
"1157","1231 - Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz informed us by reading to him, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Dharr, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us Fajr and omitted a verse. Ubayy came having missed part of the prayer. When he finished he said: O Messenger of Allah, was this verse abrogated or did you forget it? He said: No, rather I was made to forget it. Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Bundar, from Yahya ibn Sa'id."
"1158","Abu Hurayrah Abd al-Rahman ibn Sakhr al-Dawsi, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with them both) 1232 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing in the Torah nor the Gospel like Umm al-Qur'an; it is the seven oft-repeated, divided between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks."
"1159","1233 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Isma'il Abu Mu'ammar narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you a surah, nothing in the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel, nor the Qur'an like it? I said: Yes, (Ha)."
"1160","1234 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi al-Muqri' informed us, Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub al-Huraqi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you a surah, nothing in the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel, nor the Furqan like it? I said: Yes. He said: I hope not to leave that door till you know it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and I stood with him. He took my hand and spoke to me till near the door. He said: I reminded him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, the surah you mentioned to me. He said: How do you recite when you stand to pray? He recited Fatihat al-Kitab. He said: It is it; it is the seven oft-repeated and the mighty Qur'an I was given afterwards. The wording of Abd Allah ibn Ahmad's hadith. In al-Ruyani's narration: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Perhaps you shall not leave that door till I inform you of it. He said: I stood with him, conversing while his hand was in mine; I slowed, disliking that he leave before informing me. When near the door I said: O Messenger of Allah, the surah you promised me. He said: How do you recite when you stand for prayer? I recited Fatihat al-Kitab. He said: It is it; it is the seven oft-repeated which Allah said: And We gave you seven of the oft-repeated and the mighty Qur'an; it is what I was given - or granted. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated it also from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr like the narration of Abu Ya'la. Al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i both narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, from al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far similarly. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Mu'ammar ibn Rib'i al-Qaysi, from Abu Usamah similarly. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abdan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated from al-Ala', from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to Ubayy ibn Ka'b and said: O Ubayy. Ubayy turned but did not answer him ... mentioning the hadith, whose completion is this hadith. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah, saying: A good, sound hadith, making it from the musnad of Abu Hurayrah. I say: This does not affect the soundness of the hadith, for much sound hadith a Companion narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and narrates from another Companion from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Bukhari narrated from Adam ibn Abi Iyas, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umm al-Qur'an is the seven oft-repeated and the mighty Qur'an."
"1161","1235 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to me, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Ubayy (may Allah be pleased with him): that a man vaunted his lineage in the manner of Jahiliyyah, so Ubayy told him to bite his father's private part. They said: You were never foul-mouthed! He said: We were commanded with that."
"1162","1236 - Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban al-Kufi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ziyad, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: Two men exchanged harsh words before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the nose of one of them swelled with anger, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know a word which, if he said it, what he feels would go away: I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan."
"1163","1237 - Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us at Damascus, that Maali ibn Hibat Allah al-Thalabi informed them: Sahl ibn Bishr al-Isfarayini informed us, Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Hayyawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik - he is Ibn Umayr - from Ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: Two men reviled each other before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and one of them became angry, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know a word which, if he said it, his anger would go away: I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan."
"1164","1238 - With the same chain, Ahmad ibn Shuayb informed us: Yusuf ibn Isa informed us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, Yazid - meaning Ibn Ziyad ibn al-Jad - narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab, similar to it. This hadith has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Sulayman ibn Surad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Nasai narrated it thus in the Book of the Deeds of Day and Night."
"1165","1239 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us at Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab - or a man from the Ansar - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites (Say: He is Allah, the One) it is as if he recited a third of the Quran. Then Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, from Ubayy ibn Kab, as his own statement, mawquf."
"1166","1240 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us at Isfahan, that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar and Uthman ibn Nasr ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hallali informed them by reading to them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh the Hafiz informed us, Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hushaym informed us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab - or from a man from the Ansar - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (Say: He, Allah, is One) is a third of the Quran. Al-Nasai narrated it in the Book of the Deeds of Day and Night, from Hilal ibn al-Ala, from his father, from Hushaym, from Husayn, from Ibn Abi Layla, without mentioning Hilal ibn Yasaf, as Ahmad ibn Mani and Yahya ibn Yahya mentioned from Hushaym, and they are more precise than al-Ala, and Allah knows best."
"1167","1241 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali the preacher informed us at al-Harbiyyah, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: Two men boasted of their lineage in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so son of so-and-so, so who are you, may you have no mother? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men boasted of lineage in the time of Musa (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so - until he counted nine - so who are you, may you have no mother? He said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so son of Islam. He said: So Allah revealed to Musa (peace be upon him): As for these two boasters; as for you, O you who affiliate to nine in the Fire, you are the tenth of them, and as for you, O you who affiliate to two in Paradise, you are the third of them in Paradise. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah with his chain, except that he said: Two men reviled one another in both places, and these two revilers, and in it: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so son of Islam."
"1168","1242 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar the preacher - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us by reading while we listened at al-Harbiyyah - it was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Kab. He said: I saw a man boast in the manner of Jahiliyyah before Ubayy - he boasted of his father - so he told him to bite his father and did not use a euphemism, then he said: Indeed I see what is in their hearts; I could do nothing but that. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever boasts in the manner of Jahiliyyah, tell him to bite and do not use a euphemism. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Awf. And Yunus narrated it from al-Hasan."
"1169","1243 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani - may Allah have mercy on him, at Isfahan - informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri al-Razi informed us, Abu al-Qasim Jafar ibn Abd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Fannaki informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Utayy ibn Damrah, who said: We were with Ubayy when a man vaunted something of the vaunts of Jahiliyyah, so Ubayy said: Bite your father's private part, and he did not use a euphemism. It was as if the people were offended by his words. Ubayy said: I see what is in your faces; I could only say that. We used to be commanded, when a man vaunted with something of the vaunts of Jahiliyyah, to tell him to bite his father's private part and not use a euphemism."
"1170","1244 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh informed us by reading to him while we listened at Isfahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed you by reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Kab (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you see a man vaunting with the vaunts of Jahiliyyah, tell him to bite and do not use a euphemism. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Ismail, from Yunus, similar to it. And his son Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Maysarah, from Yazid ibn Zuray. And Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi, from Yahya al-Qattan. And in al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah, from Muawiyah ibn Hafs, from al-Sari ibn Yahya; and from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Awf - both - from al-Hasan, from Utayy, similar to it. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Khallad, from Yahya ibn Said."
"1171","1245 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush informed us by my reading to him at Baghdad - I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you by reading to him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of the son of Adam has been made an example of this world; even if he seasons it and salts it, look at what it becomes."
"1172","1246 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to her while they listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Kab (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of the son of Adam has been struck as an example of this world, so look at what comes out of the son of Adam even if he seasons it and salts it; it is known what it becomes. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Musa ibn al-Hasan ibn Hisham, from Abu Hudhayfah."
"1173","1247 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us. 1248 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us by my reading to him at Herat - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah al-Naysaburi informed us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Musab narrated to us, from Yunus, from Utayy ibn Damrah al-Sadi, from Ubayy ibn Kab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For ablution there is a devil called Walhan, so beware of the whispering about water. The wording is one."
"1174","1249 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa al-Anazi narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Musab narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For ablution there is a devil called al-Walhan, so fear him - or he said - so beware of him. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah both narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar. Al-Tirmidhi said: A strange hadith and its chain is not strong; we know no one who narrated it marfu except Kharijah, and it has been narrated in other ways from al-Hasan as his statement. And Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we have brought it out. I say: Kharijah ibn Musab has been much spoken about, and we only mentioned it because Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Khaythamah, from Musa ibn Ismail al-Minqari, from Muhammad ibn Dinar, from Yunus. And Muhammad ibn Dinar was declared weak by Yahya ibn Main. Ibn Adi said: His hadith is good."
"1175","1250 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi and Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafiyan - all at Isfahan - informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: Utayy al-Sadi narrated to me, he said: I heard Ubayy ibn Kab."
"1176","1251 - Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar the preacher at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, who said: I saw an old man at Madinah speaking, so I asked about him and they said: This is Ubayy ibn Kab. He said: When Adam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was dying, he said to his sons: O my sons, I desire some of the fruits of Paradise. So they went seeking for him, and the angels met them with his shrouds and embalming perfume, and with them were axes, spades and baskets. They said to them: O sons of Adam, what do you want and what do you seek, or where are you going? They said: Our father is ill and desires some of the fruits of Paradise. They said to them: Return, for the decree of your father has been decreed. So they came, and when Hawwa saw them she recognized them and clung to Adam. He said: Away from me, away from me; I was only afflicted through you. Leave me with the angels of my Lord, blessed and exalted. So they took his soul, washed him, shrouded him, embalmed him, dug for him, made a lahd for him, prayed over him, then entered his grave and placed him in his grave and placed bricks over him, then came out of the grave, then threw earth over him, then said: O sons of Adam, this is your practice. This is the wording of the hadith of Humayd from al-Hasan. The narration of Yunus from him is similar in meaning, and at its end: Your practice regarding your dead, so do likewise."
"1177","1252 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Abu al-Qasim Jafar ibn Abd Allah ibn Fannaki informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Adam died, a lahd was made for him and the angels washed him with water an odd number of times, and said: This is the practice of the children of Adam after him. Rawh ibn Aslam was criticized by more than one of the Imams, and the well-known is not marfu, and Allah knows best."
"1178","1253 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani and Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Muslim, from Atiyyah ibn Qays al-Kalai, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that he taught a man the Quran and he gifted him a bow, so something occurred in his heart, so he mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If you take it, then take it as a bow of Fire. Our Shaykh Abu al-Faraj ibn al-Jawzi mentioned in the Book of the Weak: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Muslim, from Atiyyah, as weak, without attributing that to anyone. Ibn Majah narrated it from Sahl ibn Abi Sahl, from Yahya ibn Said, and with him it is Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm."
"1179","1254 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi - may Allah have mercy on him - at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Umarah ibn Hazm, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to collect the charity of Bali and Udhrah. I passed a man of Bali who had thirty camels, so I said: Upon these camels of yours is due a she-camel in its second year. He said: That is what has neither back to ride nor milk, and it does not befit me to lend Allah the worst of my wealth, so choose. Ubayy ibn Kab said: I would not take more than what is due upon you, and here is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so go to him. He went to him and said similar to what he said to Ubayy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is what is due upon you, but if you bring more we shall accept it from you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a great fat she-camel, so order it to be taken. So he ordered it to be taken and supplicated for blessing in his wealth. Umarah said: Time struck its blows, and Marwan appointed me over the charity of Bali and Udhrah in the time of Muawiyah. I passed this man and assessed his wealth at thirty hiqqahs with their stallion, upon one thousand five hundred camels. Ibn Ishaq said: I said to Ibn Abi Bakr: What is its stallion? He said: Except that it is in the Sunnah that when a man's charity reaches thirty hiqqahs, its stallion is taken with it. Abu Yala narrated it thus in his Musnad from the narration of Yunus ibn Bukayr. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it in his Musnad from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq. And Wahb ibn Jarir narrated it from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, and they added a man in its chain."
"1180","1255 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar the preacher informed us by reading to him while we listened at al-Harbiyyah - it was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you by reading to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah, from Umarah ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me as a collector upon Bali and Udhrah and all of Banu Sad ibn Hudhaym ibn Qudaah. Ubayy said: And Yaqub said in another place: of Qudaah. He said: So I collected from them until I passed the last man among them, whose home was the nearest of their homes to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Madinah. When he gathered his wealth to me, I found nothing due upon him but a she-camel in its second year, so I told him it was his charity. He said: That is what has no milk in it and no back to ride, and by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never stood in my wealth, nor any messenger of his before you, and I would not lend Allah, blessed and exalted, from my wealth what has no milk and no back; but this is a young fat she-camel, so take it. He said: I said to him: I will not take what I was not commanded. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is near you, so if you wish to come to him and offer to him what you offered to me, do so; if he accepts it from you he accepts, and if he returns it to you he returns it. He said: I will do so. So he came out with me with the she-camel he offered me, until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to him: O Prophet of Allah, your messenger came to me to take the charity of my wealth, and by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never stood in my wealth, nor any messenger of his before him. I gathered my wealth for him and he claimed that what is due upon me is a she-camel in its second year, and that is what has no milk and no back, and I offered him a young fat she-camel to take, but he refused. Here it is, I have brought it to you, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), take it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: That is what is due upon you, but if you give extra good we shall accept it from you and Allah will reward you for it. He said: Here it is, O Messenger of Allah, I have brought it to you, so take it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it to be taken, and supplicated for blessing in his wealth."
"1181","1256 - With the same chain, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Yahya ibn Abd Allah, from Umarah ibn Hazm: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him as a collector, and he mentioned similar to the hadith of Ubayy, and added in it: Umarah said: I was put in charge of their charities in the time of Muawiyah, and I took from that man thirty hiqqahs for one thousand five hundred camels of his. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, similar to it. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili."
"1182","1257 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Sufi and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yaish informed us by reading to them while we listened at Baghdad; it was said to each of them: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn informed you by reading to him: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us, he said: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muzakki informed us by reading to him: Ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Sadusi narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Qays ibn Abbad: While I was at Madinah in the mosque in the first row standing in prayer, a man pulled me from behind and moved me aside and stood in my place. By Allah, I did not comprehend my prayer. When he finished, behold it was Ubayy ibn Kab. He said: O young man, may Allah not grieve you; this is a covenant from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to us that we stay close to him. Then he faced the qiblah and said: The people of the knot are ruined, by the Lord of the Kabah, by the Lord of the Kabah - three times - then he said: By Allah, I do not grieve over them, but I grieve over those whom they lead astray. He said: I said: Whom do you mean by this? He said: The rulers."
"1183","1258 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us by reading to him, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by ijazah: Abu Nuaym informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Jamrah informed me: I heard Iyas ibn Qatadah narrating from Qays ibn Abbad, who said: I came to Madinah to meet the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and none of them was dearer to me to meet than Ubayy ibn Kab. I stood in the first row, then he came out and prayed. When he prayed he looked intently, and I never saw men craning their necks toward anything directed to him. I heard him say: The people of the knot are ruined, by the Lord of the Kabah - he said it three times - they are ruined and they ruin; indeed I do not grieve over them, but I grieve over those of the Muslims whom they cause to perish."
"1184","1259 - And this Abu Ahmad informed us by reading to him, that his father Abu Mansur Ali informed them by reading to him: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Jamrah informed me, he said: I heard Iyas ibn Qatadah narrating from Qays ibn Abbad, who said: I came to Madinah to meet the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no man among them to meet was dearer to me than Ubayy ibn Kab. The prayer was established, and Umar came out with the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I stood in the first row, then a man came and looked at the faces of the people and recognized them except me, so he moved me aside and stood in my place. I did not comprehend my prayer. When he prayed, he said: O young man, may Allah not grieve you; I did not do what I did out of ignorance, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Be in the row next to me. I looked at the faces of the people and recognized them except you. Then he narrated, and I never saw men craning their necks toward anything directed to him. I heard him say: The people of the knots are ruined, by the Lord of the Kabah; indeed I do not grieve over them, but I grieve over those of the Muslims whom they cause to perish - and behold it was Ubayy. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Dawud. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Ibn Khuzaymah."
"1185","1260 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us by reading to him there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq, from Muhammad ibn Ubayy ibn Kab, from his father: that he had a store of dates which kept decreasing, so he guarded it one night and behold a creature like an adolescent boy. He greeted him and he returned the greeting. He said: What are you, jinn or human? He said: No, rather jinn. He said: Give me your hand. So he gave him his hand, and behold his hand was a dog's hand and his hair a dog's hair. He said: Such is the creation of the jinn. He said: The jinn know that there is no man among them stronger than me. He said: What brought you? He said: It reached us that you love charity, so we came to take some of your food. He said: What protects us from you? He said: This verse in Surat al-Baqarah: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer. Whoever says it in the evening is protected from us until morning, and whoever says it in the morning is protected from us until evening. In the morning he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: The wicked one told the truth."
"1186","1261 - And Abu Zura al-Laftuwani and Abu al-Majd al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Khallal the litterateur informed them by reading to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Fannaki informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ubayy ibn Kab who said: My grandfather had a threshing floor of dates whose count kept decreasing for him, so he guarded it one night and behold something like a creature. He greeted him and he returned it. He said: Jinn or human? He said: Jinn. He said: Show me your hand; behold a dog's hand and a dog's hair. He said: Such is the creation of the jinn. He said: The jinn know there is none among them stronger than me. He said: What brought you? He said: I was told you love charity, so I came to take some of your food. He said: What protects us from you? He said: This verse from Surat al-Baqarah: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer. If you recite it in the morning you are protected from us until night, and if you recite it at night you are protected from us until morning. So Ubayy ibn Kab went in the morning to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: The wicked one told the truth. Al-Nasai narrated it in the Book of the Deeds of Day and Night from Abu Dawud al-Harrani, from Muadh ibn Hani, from Harb ibn Shaddad with his chain, he said: My grandfather had... and he mentioned it. And from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Musa, from Shayban, from Yahya, from al-Hadrami, from Muhammad who said: Ubayy ibn Kab, the grandfather of Muhammad, said: My father had a store... and he mentioned similar. And from Abd al-Hamid ibn Said, from Mubashshir, from al-Awzai: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Ibn Ubayy narrated to me that his father told him that they had a store - the hadith. Thus he said: Ibn Ubayy narrated to me without naming him. Al-Walid ibn Mazyad narrated it likewise from al-Awzai. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Sallam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim, from al-Walid, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn Ubayy ibn Kab, from his father. He said: His name is al-Tufayl. In my view this statement is a mistake by Abu Hatim ibn Hibban - and Allah knows best - for we did not find this hadith from the narration of al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy from his father; we only found it from the narration of Muhammad ibn Ubayy. We found it in a narration from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Kab, from his father, with the addition of Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah in its chain. Abu Abd Allah al-Hakim narrated it in al-Mustadrak from Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani, from Ibrahim ibn Ishaq, from Harun ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, from Harb ibn Shaddad, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Hadrami, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ubayy ibn Kab, from his grandfather, and he said: This is sahih in chain though they did not narrate it. I did not see this hadith in the Musnad of Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi."
"1187","1262 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal the litterateur informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Kab: that his father told him that he had a store containing dates. Ubayy used to look after it and found it decreasing, so he guarded it one night and behold a creature like an adolescent boy. He said: I greeted and he returned the greeting. I said: What are you, jinn or human? He said: Jinn. He said: Give me your hand. He gave it, and behold a dog's hand and a dog's hair. I said: Such is the creation of the jinn. He said: The jinn know there is none among them stronger than me. He said: What made you do what you did? He said: It reached me you are a man who loves charity, so we wished to take some of your food. Ubayy said to him: What protects us from you? He said: This verse, Ayat al-Kursi. Then he went in the morning to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wicked one told the truth."
"1188","1263 - My maternal uncle the jurist, the Imam, the scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Ahmad ibn Abd al-Ghani and Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan informed them by reading to them: Nasr ibn Ahmad ibn al-Batir informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Bayyi narrated to us, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us: my father narrated to me from my grandfather, from my father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is the first thing you noticed of the matter of prophethood? He said: You have asked; I was in a desert with speech above me descending to me which I heard, and a man saying to the other: Is it he? He said: Yes. They faced me with faces whiter than which I never saw, and garments more beautiful than which I never saw, and fragrances the like of which I never smelled from anyone. One of them took my upper arm and the other took my other upper arm, and I felt no touch of them. One of them said to the other: Lay him down. So they laid me down without violence or force. He said to his companion: Split his chest. So he split my chest as I saw, without pain or ache or blood. He said: Remove rancor and envy from him, and put compassion and mercy into him. So he removed a clot and threw it away, then took something from a tray and put it in him, and said: This is compassion and mercy. Then he pressed with his right thumb upon my chest and said: Go and be safe. Then I stood, and I came back other than as I had gone in the morning, with mercy for the young and compassion for the old. In this narration one would think the narrator from Ubayy ibn Kab is Muadh, but it is not so; Yunus ibn Muhammad clarified in his narration that he is Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayy ibn Kab."
"1189","1264 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya al-Bazzaz narrated to me, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us: my father Muhammad ibn Muadh narrated to me from Muadh, from Muhammad, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that Abu Hurayrah used to be bold in asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about things none but he asked him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the first thing you saw of the matter of prophethood? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat up straight and said: You have asked, Abu Hurayrah. I was in a desert, a boy of ten years and months, when there was speech above my head, and a man saying to a man: Is it he? He said: Yes. They faced me with faces I never saw in any creature, and fragrances I never smelled from any creature, and garments I never saw on anyone. They came to me walking until each of them took my upper arm, and I felt no touch of their taking. One of them said to his companion: Lay him down. So they laid me down without force or violence. One of them said to his companion: Split his chest. He reached - and in a narration: one of them stooped to my chest and split it as I saw - without blood or pain. He said to him: Remove rancor and envy. So he removed something like a clot, then cast it away and threw it. He said to him: Put in compassion and mercy; behold something like what he removed, resembling silver. Then he shook my right big toe and said: Go and be safe. So I returned with it, going with tenderness for the young and mercy for the old. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated its beginning from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, from Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari, from Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba, from Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: Abu Hurayrah used to be bold toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), asking him about things none but he asked him."
"1190","1265 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari informed us, Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kneel upon his knees and would not recline. This hadith is abridged from a hadith narrated by Ibn Hibban from Abu Yala."
"1191","1266 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us. 1267 - And Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Muadh - meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab - narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubayy ibn Kab (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu al-Mundhir, I have been commanded to present the Quran to you. He said: In Allah I believe, at your hand I submitted, and from you I learned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated the words, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, was I mentioned there? He said: Yes, by your name and lineage in the highest assembly. He said: Then recite, O Messenger of Allah. And the one before it is the completion of this."
"1192","1268 - My maternal uncle the Imam, the scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Ghani informed them by reading to them: Nasr ibn Ahmad ibn al-Batir informed us, Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Bayyi informed us, Abu Abd Allah al-Hasan ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us: my father narrated to me from my grandfather, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Fever and its harm trouble me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Seek chastity and be patient. The man repeated to him three times, adding nothing to his words, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have been commanded to present the Quran to you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, in Allah, mighty and exalted, I believe, at your hands I submitted, and from you I learned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated the words, so Ubayy - may Allah have mercy on him - said: Was I mentioned there, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, in the highest assembly, by your name and lineage. He said: Then recite, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sat, would kneel upon his knees and would not recline. This too contains abridgment."
"1193","1269 - Asad informed us, that Fatimah informed them: Ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubayy ibn Kab (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of fever? He said: Good deeds flow for its bearer as long as a foot throbs upon him or a vein beats upon him. Ubayy said: O Allah, I ask You for a fever that does not prevent me going out in Your path, nor going out to Your House, nor to the mosque of Your Prophet. So Ubayy was never untouched except that fever was in him."
"1194","1270 - And Abu Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr at Isfahan informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of fever? He said: Good deeds flow for its bearer as long as a foot throbs upon him or a vein beats upon him. He - meaning Ubayy - said: O Allah, I ask You for a fever that does not prevent me going out in Your path, nor going out to Your House, nor to the mosque of Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Ubayy was never untouched except that fever was in him."
"1195","1271 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah informed us, Jami ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seclude himself in the last ten nights; then he traveled one year and did not seclude himself, so in the next year he secluded himself for twenty days."
"1196","1272 - And Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala informed us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Ubayy ibn Kab."
"1197","1273 - And al-Mubarak ibn al-Mattush at Baghdad informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Ubayy ibn Kab."
"1198","1274 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani at Isfahan informed us, that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them while present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Ubayy ibn Kab."
"1199","1275 - And Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Akhdar the Hafiz at Baghdad informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi the Hafiz and Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarraḥ and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn Abd al-Salam informed them by reading to them. 1276 - And Abu al-Fadl Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Mawsili at Baghdad informed us, that Yahya ibn al-Tarraḥ informed them by reading to him. 1277 - And Abu Hamid Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit ibn Zayd ibn Hawaliq at Baghdad informed us, that the judge Abu al-Fath Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Baydawi informed them by reading to him - they said: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Naqqur informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seclude himself in the last ten of the month of Ramadan, then he traveled one year and did not seclude himself; in the next year he secluded himself for twenty nights. The wording of al-Baghawi. In the narration of Abd Allah ibn Ahmad: He used to seclude himself in the last ten of Ramadan, then he traveled one year and did not seclude himself; in the next year he secluded himself for twenty days. The narration of Abu Yala is likewise except that he did not say one year. The narration of Ibn Abi Asim says in it: After a year he was busy and did not seclude himself, so in the next year he secluded himself for twenty days. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Hasan ibn Musa and Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Ismail, from Hammad. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya. Al-Nasai narrated it from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, both from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi. Al-Nasai also narrated it from Harun ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Dawud, both from Hammad ibn Salamah. Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili. The last of the hadith of Ubayy ibn Kab."
"1200","1278 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us. 1279 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us. 1280 - He said: And Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ubayy ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever reaches his parents or one of them and then enters the Fire, may Allah cast him far away."
